

relation Type_alpha: `typeIR''''` and `typeIR'''''`


. If let `baseTypeIR` be `typeIR''''`:
 .. Check that `typeIR'''''` has type `baseTypeIR`.
 .. Let `baseTypeIR'` be `typeIR'''''`.
 .. Check that `baseTypeIR` is equal to `baseTypeIR'`.
 .. Group baseTypeIR:
  ... The relation holds.
. Else if let `tid` be `typeIR''''`:
 .. Check that `typeIR'''''` has type `nameTypeIR`.
 .. Let `tid'` be `typeIR'''''`.
 .. Check that `tid` is equal to `tid'`.
 .. Group nameTypeIR:
  ... The relation holds.
. Else if let `typeDefIR~a~ < typeIR~a~^{asterisk}^ >` be `typeIR''''`:
 .. Check that `typeIR'''''` has type `specializedTypeIR`.
 .. Let `typeDefIR~b~ < typeIR~b~^{asterisk}^ >` be `typeIR'''''`.
 .. Group specializedTypeIR:
  ... Let `typeIR~a_spec~` be `<<specialize_typeDefIR, $specialize_typeDefIR(typeDefIR~a~, typeIR~a~^{asterisk}^)>>`.
  ... Let `typeIR~b_spec~` be `<<specialize_typeDefIR, $specialize_typeDefIR(typeDefIR~b~, typeIR~b~^{asterisk}^)>>`.
  ... Check that <<Type_alpha, `typeIR~a_spec~` and `typeIR~b_spec~` are the same type>>.
  ... If `<<is_nominal_typeIR, $is_nominal_typeIR(typeIR~a_spec~)>>` *and* `<<is_nominal_typeIR, $is_nominal_typeIR(typeIR~b_spec~)>>`:
   .... Check that <<Type_alpha, `typeIR~a~` and `typeIR~b~` are the same type>>, for all `typeIR~a~` in `typeIR~a~^{asterisk}^` and `typeIR~b~` in `typeIR~b~^{asterisk}^`.
   .... The relation holds.
  ... Else if `~<<is_nominal_typeIR, $is_nominal_typeIR(typeIR~a_spec~)>>` *and* `~<<is_nominal_typeIR, $is_nominal_typeIR(typeIR~b_spec~)>>`:
   .... The relation holds.
. Group typedefTypeIR:
 .. If let `TYPEDEF ++_++ typeIR~a~` be `typeIR''''`:
  ... Check that <<Type_alpha, `typeIR~a~` and `typeIR'''''` are the same type>>.
  ... The relation holds.
 .. Else if let `TYPEDEF ++_++ typeIR~b~` be `typeIR'''''`:
  ... Check that <<Type_alpha, `typeIR''''` and `typeIR~b~` are the same type>>.
  ... The relation holds.
. If let `TYPE tid typeIR~a~` be `typeIR''''`:
 .. Check that `typeIR'''''` has type `newTypeIR`.
 .. Let `TYPE tid' typeIR~b~` be `typeIR'''''`.
 .. Check that `tid` is equal to `tid'`.
 .. Group newTypeIR:
  ... Check that <<Type_alpha, `typeIR~a~` and `typeIR~b~` are the same type>>.
  ... The relation holds.
. Else if let `LIST < typeIR~a~ >` be `typeIR''''`:
 .. Check that `typeIR'''''` has type `listTypeIR`.
 .. Let `LIST < typeIR~b~ >` be `typeIR'''''`.
 .. Group listTypeIR:
  ... Check that <<Type_alpha, `typeIR~a~` and `typeIR~b~` are the same type>>.
  ... The relation holds.
. Else if let `TUPLE < typeIR~a~^{asterisk}^ >` be `typeIR''''`:
 .. Check that `typeIR'''''` has type `tupleTypeIR`.
 .. Let `TUPLE < typeIR~b~^{asterisk}^ >` be `typeIR'''''`.
 .. Group tupleTypeIR:
  ... Check that <<Type_alpha, `typeIR~a~` and `typeIR~b~` are the same type>>, for all `typeIR~a~` in `typeIR~a~^{asterisk}^` and `typeIR~b~` in `typeIR~b~^{asterisk}^`.
  ... The relation holds.
. Else if let `typeIR~a~ [ n~size~ ]` be `typeIR''''`:
 .. Check that `typeIR'''''` has type `headerStackTypeIR`.
 .. Let `typeIR~b~ [ n~size'~ ]` be `typeIR'''''`.
 .. Check that `n~size~` is equal to `n~size'~`.
 .. Group headerStackTypeIR:
  ... Check that <<Type_alpha, `typeIR~a~` and `typeIR~b~` are the same type>>.
  ... The relation holds.
. Else if let `STRUCT tid { (typeIR~field_a~ id~field~ ;)^{asterisk}^ }` be `typeIR''''`:
 .. Check that `typeIR'''''` has type `structTypeIR`.
 .. Let `STRUCT tid' { (typeIR~field_b~ id~field'~ ;)^{asterisk}^ }` be `typeIR'''''`.
 .. Check that `id~field~` is equal to `id~field'~`, for all `id~field~` in `id~field~^{asterisk}^` and `id~field'~` in `id~field'~^{asterisk}^`.
 .. Check that `tid` is equal to `tid'`.
 .. Group structTypeIR:
  ... Check that <<Type_alpha, `typeIR~field_a~` and `typeIR~field_b~` are the same type>>, for all `typeIR~field_a~` in `typeIR~field_a~^{asterisk}^` and `typeIR~field_b~` in `typeIR~field_b~^{asterisk}^`.
  ... The relation holds.
. Else if let `HEADER tid { (typeIR~field_a~ id~field~ ;)^{asterisk}^ }` be `typeIR''''`:
 .. Check that `typeIR'''''` has type `headerTypeIR`.
 .. Let `HEADER tid' { (typeIR~field_b~ id~field'~ ;)^{asterisk}^ }` be `typeIR'''''`.
 .. Check that `id~field~` is equal to `id~field'~`, for all `id~field~` in `id~field~^{asterisk}^` and `id~field'~` in `id~field'~^{asterisk}^`.
 .. Check that `tid` is equal to `tid'`.
 .. Group headerTypeIR:
  ... Check that <<Type_alpha, `typeIR~field_a~` and `typeIR~field_b~` are the same type>>, for all `typeIR~field_a~` in `typeIR~field_a~^{asterisk}^` and `typeIR~field_b~` in `typeIR~field_b~^{asterisk}^`.
  ... The relation holds.
. Else if let `HEADER_UNION tid { (typeIR~field_a~ id~field~ ;)^{asterisk}^ }` be `typeIR''''`:
 .. Check that `typeIR'''''` has type `headerUnionTypeIR`.
 .. Let `HEADER_UNION tid' { (typeIR~field_b~ id~field'~ ;)^{asterisk}^ }` be `typeIR'''''`.
 .. Check that `id~field~` is equal to `id~field'~`, for all `id~field~` in `id~field~^{asterisk}^` and `id~field'~` in `id~field'~^{asterisk}^`.
 .. Check that `tid` is equal to `tid'`.
 .. Group headerUnionTypeIR:
  ... Check that <<Type_alpha, `typeIR~field_a~` and `typeIR~field_b~` are the same type>>, for all `typeIR~field_a~` in `typeIR~field_a~^{asterisk}^` and `typeIR~field_b~` in `typeIR~field_b~^{asterisk}^`.
  ... The relation holds.
. Else if let `enumTypeIR` be `typeIR''''`:
 .. Check that `typeIR'''''` has type `enumTypeIR`.
 .. Let `enumTypeIR'` be `typeIR'''''`.
 .. Group enumTypeIR:
  ... If let `ENUM tid { id~field~^{asterisk}^ }` be `enumTypeIR`:
   .... Check that `enumTypeIR'` is equal to `ENUM tid { id~field~^{asterisk}^ }`.
   .... The relation holds.
  ... Else let `ENUM tid < typeIR~a~ > { (id~field~ = value~field~ ;)^{asterisk}^ }` be `enumTypeIR`:
   .... Check that `enumTypeIR'` matches pattern `ENUM % < % > { % }`.
   .... Let `ENUM tid' < typeIR~b~ > { valueFieldIR^{asterisk}^ }` be `enumTypeIR'`.
   .... Check that `tid'` is equal to `tid`.
   .... Check that `valueFieldIR^{asterisk}^` is equal to `(id~field~ = value~field~ ;)^{asterisk}^`.
   .... Check that <<Type_alpha, `typeIR~a~` and `typeIR~b~` are the same type>>.
   .... The relation holds.
. Else if let `EXTERN tid { (cid~a~ : externMethodTypeDefIR~a~)^{asterisk}^ }` be `typeIR''''`:
 .. Check that `typeIR'''''` has type `externObjectTypeIR`.
 .. Let `EXTERN tid' { (cid~b~ : externMethodTypeDefIR~b~)^{asterisk}^ }` be `typeIR'''''`.
 .. Check that `tid` is equal to `tid'`.
 .. Group externObjectTypeIR:
  ... Check that <<eq_set, `{ cid~a~^{asterisk}^ }` is equal to `{ cid~b~^{asterisk}^ }`>>.
  ... Let `externMethodTypeDefIR^?^^{asterisk}^` be the list of `externMethodTypeDefIR^?^`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
      * Let `externMethodTypeDefIR^?^` be `<<find_map, $find_map<cid, externMethodTypeDefIR>({ (cid~a~ : externMethodTypeDefIR~a~)^{asterisk}^ }, cid~a~)>>`.
--
+
for each `cid~a~` in `cid~a~^{asterisk}^`
  ... Check that `externMethodTypeDefIR^?^` is Some value, for all `externMethodTypeDefIR^?^` in `externMethodTypeDefIR^?^^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Let `externMethodTypeDefIR~a'~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `externMethodTypeDefIR~a'~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
      * Let `externMethodTypeDefIR~a'~` be `externMethodTypeDefIR^?^`.
--
+
for each `externMethodTypeDefIR^?^` in `externMethodTypeDefIR^?^^{asterisk}^`
  ... Let `externMethodTypeDefIR'^?^^{asterisk}^` be the list of `externMethodTypeDefIR'^?^`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
      * Let `externMethodTypeDefIR'^?^` be `<<find_map, $find_map<cid, externMethodTypeDefIR>({ (cid~b~ : externMethodTypeDefIR~b~)^{asterisk}^ }, cid~a~)>>`.
--
+
for each `cid~a~` in `cid~a~^{asterisk}^`
  ... Check that `externMethodTypeDefIR'^?^` is Some value, for all `externMethodTypeDefIR'^?^` in `externMethodTypeDefIR'^?^^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Let `externMethodTypeDefIR~b'~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `externMethodTypeDefIR~b'~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
      * Let `externMethodTypeDefIR~b'~` be `externMethodTypeDefIR'^?^`.
--
+
for each `externMethodTypeDefIR'^?^` in `externMethodTypeDefIR'^?^^{asterisk}^`
  ... Check that <<CallableTypeDef_alpha, `externMethodTypeDefIR~a'~` and `externMethodTypeDefIR~b'~` are the same type>>, for all `externMethodTypeDefIR~a'~` in `externMethodTypeDefIR~a'~^{asterisk}^` and `externMethodTypeDefIR~b'~` in `externMethodTypeDefIR~b'~^{asterisk}^`.
  ... The relation holds.
. Else if let `PARSER ( parameterTypeIR~a~^{asterisk}^ )` be `typeIR''''`:
 .. Check that `typeIR'''''` has type `parserObjectTypeIR`.
 .. Let `PARSER ( parameterTypeIR~b~^{asterisk}^ )` be `typeIR'''''`.
 .. Group parserObjectTypeIR:
  ... Check that <<ParameterType_alpha, `parameterTypeIR~a~` and `parameterTypeIR~b~` are the same type>>, for all `parameterTypeIR~a~` in `parameterTypeIR~a~^{asterisk}^` and `parameterTypeIR~b~` in `parameterTypeIR~b~^{asterisk}^`.
  ... The relation holds.
. Else if let `CONTROL ( parameterTypeIR~a~^{asterisk}^ )` be `typeIR''''`:
 .. Check that `typeIR'''''` has type `controlObjectTypeIR`.
 .. Let `CONTROL ( parameterTypeIR~b~^{asterisk}^ )` be `typeIR'''''`.
 .. Group controlObjectTypeIR:
  ... Check that <<ParameterType_alpha, `parameterTypeIR~a~` and `parameterTypeIR~b~` are the same type>>, for all `parameterTypeIR~a~` in `parameterTypeIR~a~^{asterisk}^` and `parameterTypeIR~b~` in `parameterTypeIR~b~^{asterisk}^`.
  ... The relation holds.
. Else if let `PACKAGE { typeIR~a~^{asterisk}^ }` be `typeIR''''`:
 .. Check that `typeIR'''''` has type `packageObjectTypeIR`.
 .. Let `PACKAGE { typeIR~b~^{asterisk}^ }` be `typeIR'''''`.
 .. Group packetObjectTypeIR:
  ... Check that <<Type_alpha, `typeIR~a~` and `typeIR~b~` are the same type>>, for all `typeIR~a~` in `typeIR~a~^{asterisk}^` and `typeIR~b~` in `typeIR~b~^{asterisk}^`.
  ... The relation holds.
. Else if let `tableObjectTypeIR` be `typeIR''''`:
 .. Check that `typeIR'''''` has type `tableObjectTypeIR`.
 .. Let `tableObjectTypeIR'` be `typeIR'''''`.
 .. Check that `tableObjectTypeIR` is equal to `tableObjectTypeIR'`.
 .. Group tableObjectTypeIR:
  ... The relation holds.
. Else if let `defaultTypeIR` be `typeIR''''`:
 .. Check that `typeIR'''''` has type `defaultTypeIR`.
 .. Let `defaultTypeIR'` be `typeIR'''''`.
 .. Group defaultTypeIR:
  ... The relation holds.
. Else if let `invalidHeaderTypeIR` be `typeIR''''`:
 .. Check that `typeIR'''''` has type `invalidHeaderTypeIR`.
 .. Let `invalidHeaderTypeIR'` be `typeIR'''''`.
 .. Group invalidHeaderTypeIR:
  ... The relation holds.
. Else if let `sequenceTypeIR` be `typeIR''''`:
 .. Check that `typeIR'''''` has type `sequenceTypeIR`.
 .. Let `sequenceTypeIR'` be `typeIR'''''`.
 .. Group sequenceTypeIR:
  ... If let `SEQ < typeIR~a~^{asterisk}^ >` be `sequenceTypeIR`:
   .... Check that `sequenceTypeIR'` matches pattern `SEQ < % >`.
   .... Let `SEQ < typeIR~b~^{asterisk}^ >` be `sequenceTypeIR'`.
   .... Check that <<Type_alpha, `typeIR~a~` and `typeIR~b~` are the same type>>, for all `typeIR~a~` in `typeIR~a~^{asterisk}^` and `typeIR~b~` in `typeIR~b~^{asterisk}^`.
   .... The relation holds.
  ... Else let `SEQ < typeIR~a~^{asterisk}^ , ... >` be `sequenceTypeIR`:
   .... Check that `sequenceTypeIR'` matches pattern `SEQ < % , ... >`.
   .... Let `SEQ < typeIR~b~^{asterisk}^ , ... >` be `sequenceTypeIR'`.
   .... Check that <<Type_alpha, `typeIR~a~` and `typeIR~b~` are the same type>>, for all `typeIR~a~` in `typeIR~a~^{asterisk}^` and `typeIR~b~` in `typeIR~b~^{asterisk}^`.
   .... The relation holds.
. Else if let `recordTypeIR` be `typeIR''''`:
 .. Check that `typeIR'''''` has type `recordTypeIR`.
 .. Let `recordTypeIR'` be `typeIR'''''`.
 .. Group recordTypeIR:
  ... If let `RECORD { (typeIR~field_a~ id~field~ ;)^{asterisk}^ }` be `recordTypeIR`:
   .... Check that `recordTypeIR'` matches pattern `RECORD { % }`.
   .... Let `RECORD { (typeIR~field_b~ id ;)^{asterisk}^ }` be `recordTypeIR'`.
   .... Check that `id` is equal to `id~field~`, for all `id` in `id^{asterisk}^` and `id~field~` in `id~field~^{asterisk}^`.
   .... Check that <<Type_alpha, `typeIR~field_a~` and `typeIR~field_b~` are the same type>>, for all `typeIR~field_a~` in `typeIR~field_a~^{asterisk}^` and `typeIR~field_b~` in `typeIR~field_b~^{asterisk}^`.
   .... The relation holds.
  ... Else let `RECORD { (typeIR~field_a~ id~field~ ;)^{asterisk}^ , ... }` be `recordTypeIR`:
   .... Check that `recordTypeIR'` matches pattern `RECORD { % , ... }`.
   .... Let `RECORD { (typeIR~field_b~ id ;)^{asterisk}^ , ... }` be `recordTypeIR'`.
   .... Check that `id` is equal to `id~field~`, for all `id` in `id^{asterisk}^` and `id~field~` in `id~field~^{asterisk}^`.
   .... Check that <<Type_alpha, `typeIR~field_a~` and `typeIR~field_b~` are the same type>>, for all `typeIR~field_a~` in `typeIR~field_a~^{asterisk}^` and `typeIR~field_b~` in `typeIR~field_b~^{asterisk}^`.
   .... The relation holds.
. Else if let `SET < typeIR^{asterisk}^ >` be `typeIR''''`:
 .. Check that `typeIR^{asterisk}^` is a list of length 1.
 .. Let `[typeIR~a~]` be `typeIR^{asterisk}^`.
 .. Check that `typeIR'''''` has type `setTypeIR`.
 .. Let `SET < typeIR''^{asterisk}^ >` be `typeIR'''''`.
 .. Check that `typeIR''^{asterisk}^` is a list of length 1.
 .. Let `[typeIR~b~]` be `typeIR''^{asterisk}^`.
 .. Group setTypeIR:
  ... Check that <<Type_alpha, `typeIR~a~` and `typeIR~b~` are the same type>>.
  ... The relation holds.
. Else if let `tableMetadataTypeIR` be `typeIR''''`:
 .. Check that `typeIR'''''` has type `tableMetadataTypeIR`.
 .. Let `tableMetadataTypeIR'` be `typeIR'''''`.
 .. Check that `tableMetadataTypeIR` is equal to `tableMetadataTypeIR'`.
 .. Group tableMetadataTypeIR:
  ... The relation holds.


relation ParameterType_alpha: `direction typeIR~a~ ++_++ ++_++^?^` and `direction' typeIR~b~ ++_++ ++_++^?^`


. Check that `direction` is equal to `direction'`.
. Group :
 .. Check that <<Type_alpha, `typeIR~a~` and `typeIR~b~` are the same type>>.
 .. The relation holds.


relation CallableType_alpha: `callableTypeIR` and `callableTypeIR'`


. If let `ACTION ( parameterTypeIR~a~^{asterisk}^ )` be `callableTypeIR`:
 .. Check that `callableTypeIR'` has type `actionTypeIR`.
 .. Let `ACTION ( parameterTypeIR~b~^{asterisk}^ )` be `callableTypeIR'`.
 .. Group actionTypeIR:
  ... Check that <<ParameterType_alpha, `parameterTypeIR~a~` and `parameterTypeIR~b~` are the same type>>, for all `parameterTypeIR~a~` in `parameterTypeIR~a~^{asterisk}^` and `parameterTypeIR~b~` in `parameterTypeIR~b~^{asterisk}^`.
  ... The relation holds.
. Else if let `FUNCTION ( parameterTypeIR~a~^{asterisk}^ ) : typeIR~a~` be `callableTypeIR`:
 .. Check that `callableTypeIR'` has type `definedFunctionTypeIR`.
 .. Let `FUNCTION ( parameterTypeIR~b~^{asterisk}^ ) : typeIR~b~` be `callableTypeIR'`.
 .. Group definedFunctionTypeIR:
  ... Check that <<ParameterType_alpha, `parameterTypeIR~a~` and `parameterTypeIR~b~` are the same type>>, for all `parameterTypeIR~a~` in `parameterTypeIR~a~^{asterisk}^` and `parameterTypeIR~b~` in `parameterTypeIR~b~^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Check that <<Type_alpha, `typeIR~a~` and `typeIR~b~` are the same type>>.
  ... The relation holds.
. Else if let `EXTERN_FUNCTION ( parameterTypeIR~a~^{asterisk}^ ) : typeIR~a~` be `callableTypeIR`:
 .. Check that `callableTypeIR'` has type `externFunctionTypeIR`.
 .. Let `EXTERN_FUNCTION ( parameterTypeIR~b~^{asterisk}^ ) : typeIR~b~` be `callableTypeIR'`.
 .. Group externFunctionTypeIR:
  ... Check that <<ParameterType_alpha, `parameterTypeIR~a~` and `parameterTypeIR~b~` are the same type>>, for all `parameterTypeIR~a~` in `parameterTypeIR~a~^{asterisk}^` and `parameterTypeIR~b~` in `parameterTypeIR~b~^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Check that <<Type_alpha, `typeIR~a~` and `typeIR~b~` are the same type>>.
  ... The relation holds.
. Else if let `BUILTIN_METHOD ( parameterTypeIR~a~^{asterisk}^ ) : typeIR~a~` be `callableTypeIR`:
 .. Check that `callableTypeIR'` has type `builtinMethodTypeIR`.
 .. Let `BUILTIN_METHOD ( parameterTypeIR~b~^{asterisk}^ ) : typeIR~b~` be `callableTypeIR'`.
 .. Group builtinMethodTypeIR:
  ... Check that <<ParameterType_alpha, `parameterTypeIR~a~` and `parameterTypeIR~b~` are the same type>>, for all `parameterTypeIR~a~` in `parameterTypeIR~a~^{asterisk}^` and `parameterTypeIR~b~` in `parameterTypeIR~b~^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Check that <<Type_alpha, `typeIR~a~` and `typeIR~b~` are the same type>>.
  ... The relation holds.
. Else if let `externMethodTypeIR` be `callableTypeIR`:
 .. Check that `callableTypeIR'` has type `externMethodTypeIR`.
 .. Let `externMethodTypeIR'` be `callableTypeIR'`.
 .. Group externMethodTypeIR:
  ... If let `EXTERN_METHOD ( parameterTypeIR~a~^{asterisk}^ ) : typeIR~a~` be `externMethodTypeIR`:
   .... Check that `externMethodTypeIR'` matches pattern `EXTERN_METHOD ( % ) : %`.
   .... Let `EXTERN_METHOD ( parameterTypeIR~b~^{asterisk}^ ) : typeIR~b~` be `externMethodTypeIR'`.
   .... Check that <<ParameterType_alpha, `parameterTypeIR~a~` and `parameterTypeIR~b~` are the same type>>, for all `parameterTypeIR~a~` in `parameterTypeIR~a~^{asterisk}^` and `parameterTypeIR~b~` in `parameterTypeIR~b~^{asterisk}^`.
   .... Check that <<Type_alpha, `typeIR~a~` and `typeIR~b~` are the same type>>.
   .... The relation holds.
  ... Else let `EXTERN_METHOD ABSTRACT ( parameterTypeIR~a~^{asterisk}^ ) : typeIR~a~` be `externMethodTypeIR`:
   .... Check that `externMethodTypeIR'` matches pattern `EXTERN_METHOD ABSTRACT ( % ) : %`.
   .... Let `EXTERN_METHOD ABSTRACT ( parameterTypeIR~b~^{asterisk}^ ) : typeIR~b~` be `externMethodTypeIR'`.
   .... Check that <<ParameterType_alpha, `parameterTypeIR~a~` and `parameterTypeIR~b~` are the same type>>, for all `parameterTypeIR~a~` in `parameterTypeIR~a~^{asterisk}^` and `parameterTypeIR~b~` in `parameterTypeIR~b~^{asterisk}^`.
   .... Check that <<Type_alpha, `typeIR~a~` and `typeIR~b~` are the same type>>.
   .... The relation holds.
. Else if let `PARSER_APPLY ( parameterTypeIR~a~^{asterisk}^ )` be `callableTypeIR`:
 .. Check that `callableTypeIR'` has type `parserApplyMethodTypeIR`.
 .. Let `PARSER_APPLY ( parameterTypeIR~b~^{asterisk}^ )` be `callableTypeIR'`.
 .. Group parserApplyMethodTypeIR:
  ... Check that <<ParameterType_alpha, `parameterTypeIR~a~` and `parameterTypeIR~b~` are the same type>>, for all `parameterTypeIR~a~` in `parameterTypeIR~a~^{asterisk}^` and `parameterTypeIR~b~` in `parameterTypeIR~b~^{asterisk}^`.
  ... The relation holds.
. Else if let `CONTROL_APPLY ( parameterTypeIR~a~^{asterisk}^ )` be `callableTypeIR`:
 .. Check that `callableTypeIR'` has type `controlApplyMethodTypeIR`.
 .. Let `CONTROL_APPLY ( parameterTypeIR~b~^{asterisk}^ )` be `callableTypeIR'`.
 .. Group controlApplyMethodTypeIR:
  ... Check that <<ParameterType_alpha, `parameterTypeIR~a~` and `parameterTypeIR~b~` are the same type>>, for all `parameterTypeIR~a~` in `parameterTypeIR~a~^{asterisk}^` and `parameterTypeIR~b~` in `parameterTypeIR~b~^{asterisk}^`.
  ... The relation holds.
. Else let `tableApplyMethodTypeIR` be `callableTypeIR`:
 .. Check that `callableTypeIR'` has type `tableApplyMethodTypeIR`.
 .. Let `tableApplyMethodTypeIR'` be `callableTypeIR'`.
 .. Check that `tableApplyMethodTypeIR` is equal to `tableApplyMethodTypeIR'`.
 .. Group tableApplyMethodTypeIR:
  ... The relation holds.


relation CallableTypeDef_alpha: `callableTypeDefIR~a~` and `callableTypeDefIR~b~`


. Group :
 .. Let `(tid~tparam_expl_a~^{asterisk}^, tid~tparam_impl_a~^{asterisk}^)` be `<<type_parameters_of_callableTypeDefIR, $type_parameters_of_callableTypeDefIR(callableTypeDefIR~a~)>>`.
 .. Let `(tid~tparam_expl_b~^{asterisk}^, tid~tparam_impl_b~^{asterisk}^)` be `<<type_parameters_of_callableTypeDefIR, $type_parameters_of_callableTypeDefIR(callableTypeDefIR~b~)>>`.
 .. Check that the length of `tid~tparam_expl_a~^{asterisk}^` is equal to the length of `tid~tparam_expl_b~^{asterisk}^`.
 .. Check that the length of `tid~tparam_impl_a~^{asterisk}^` is equal to the length of `tid~tparam_impl_b~^{asterisk}^`.
 .. Let `tid~tparam_fresh~^{asterisk}^` be <<fresh_tids, the length of `tid~tparam_expl_a~^{asterisk}^ {pp} tid~tparam_impl_a~^{asterisk}^` fresh type variables>>.
 .. Let `tid~tparam_a~^{asterisk}^` be `tid~tparam_expl_a~^{asterisk}^ {pp} tid~tparam_impl_a~^{asterisk}^`.
 .. Let `theta~a~` be `{ (tid~tparam_a~ : tid~tparam_fresh~)^{asterisk}^ }`.
 .. Let `callableTypeIR~a~` be `<<type_of_callableTypeDefIR, $type_of_callableTypeDefIR(callableTypeDefIR~a~)>>`.
 .. Let `callableTypeIR~a_subst~` be `<<subst_callableTypeIR, $subst_callableTypeIR(theta~a~, callableTypeIR~a~)>>`.
 .. Let `tid~tparam_b~^{asterisk}^` be `tid~tparam_expl_b~^{asterisk}^ {pp} tid~tparam_impl_b~^{asterisk}^`.
 .. Let `theta~b~` be `{ (tid~tparam_b~ : tid~tparam_fresh~)^{asterisk}^ }`.
 .. Let `callableTypeIR~b~` be `<<type_of_callableTypeDefIR, $type_of_callableTypeDefIR(callableTypeDefIR~b~)>>`.
 .. Let `callableTypeIR~b_subst~` be `<<subst_callableTypeIR, $subst_callableTypeIR(theta~b~, callableTypeIR~b~)>>`.
 .. Check that <<CallableType_alpha, `callableTypeIR~a_subst~` and `callableTypeIR~b_subst~` are the same type>>.
 .. The relation holds.


relation Type_wf: `bound` and `typeIR'''`


. If let `baseTypeIR` be `typeIR'''`:
 .. Group baseTypeIR:
  ... The relation holds.
. Else if let `tid` be `typeIR'''`:
 .. Group nameTypeIR:
  ... Check that <<in_set, `tid` is an element of the set `bound`>>.
  ... The relation holds.
. Else if let `typeDefIR~base~ < typeIR~arg~^{asterisk}^ >` be `typeIR'''`:
 .. Group specializedTypeIR:
  ... Let `typeIR~spec~` be `<<specialize_typeDefIR, $specialize_typeDefIR(typeDefIR~base~, typeIR~arg~^{asterisk}^)>>`.
  ... Check that <<Type_wf, `typeIR~spec~` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `bound`>>.
  ... The relation holds.
. Else if let `TYPEDEF ++_++ typeIR` be `typeIR'''`:
 .. Group typedefTypeIR:
  ... Check that <<nestable_typedef, `typeIR` can be used in a typedef>>.
  ... Check that <<Type_wf, `typeIR` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `bound`>>.
  ... The relation holds.
. Else if let `TYPE ++_++ typeIR` be `typeIR'''`:
 .. Group newTypeIR:
  ... Check that <<nestable_new, `typeIR` can be used in a new type>>.
  ... Check that <<Type_wf, `typeIR` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `bound`>>.
  ... The relation holds.
. Else if let `LIST < typeIR >` be `typeIR'''`:
 .. Group listTypeIR:
  ... Check that <<nestable_list, `typeIR` can be nested in a list type>>.
  ... Check that <<Type_wf, `typeIR` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `bound`>>.
  ... The relation holds.
. Else if let `TUPLE < typeIR^{asterisk}^ >` be `typeIR'''`:
 .. Group tupleTypeIR:
  ... Check that <<nestable_tuple, `typeIR` can be nested in a tuple type>>, for all `typeIR` in `typeIR^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Check that <<Type_wf, `typeIR` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `bound`>>, for all `typeIR` in `typeIR^{asterisk}^`.
  ... The relation holds.
. Else if let `typeIR [ ++_++ ]` be `typeIR'''`:
 .. Group headerStackTypeIR:
  ... Check that <<nestable_headerStack, `typeIR` can be nested in a header stack type>>.
  ... Check that <<Type_wf, `typeIR` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `bound`>>.
  ... The relation holds.
. Else if let `STRUCT ++_++ { (typeIR~field~ id~field~ ;)^{asterisk}^ }` be `typeIR'''`:
 .. Group structTypeIR:
  ... Check that <<distinct_, the elements of `id~field~^{asterisk}^` are distinct>>.
  ... Check that <<nestable_struct, `typeIR~field~` can be nested in a struct type>>, for all `typeIR~field~` in `typeIR~field~^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Check that <<Type_wf, `typeIR~field~` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `bound`>>, for all `typeIR~field~` in `typeIR~field~^{asterisk}^`.
  ... The relation holds.
. Else if let `HEADER ++_++ { (typeIR~field~ id~field~ ;)^{asterisk}^ }` be `typeIR'''`:
 .. Group headerTypeIR:
  ... Check that <<distinct_, the elements of `id~field~^{asterisk}^` are distinct>>.
  ... Check that <<nestable_header, `typeIR~field~` can be used in a header type>>, for all `typeIR~field~` in `typeIR~field~^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Check that <<Type_wf, `typeIR~field~` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `bound`>>, for all `typeIR~field~` in `typeIR~field~^{asterisk}^`.
  ... The relation holds.
. Else if let `HEADER_UNION ++_++ { (typeIR~field~ id~field~ ;)^{asterisk}^ }` be `typeIR'''`:
 .. Group headerUnionTypeIR:
  ... Check that <<distinct_, the elements of `id~field~^{asterisk}^` are distinct>>.
  ... Check that <<nestable_headerUnion, `typeIR~field~` can be used in a header union type>>, for all `typeIR~field~` in `typeIR~field~^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Check that <<Type_wf, `typeIR~field~` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `bound`>>, for all `typeIR~field~` in `typeIR~field~^{asterisk}^`.
  ... The relation holds.
. Else if let `enumTypeIR` be `typeIR'''`:
 .. Group enumTypeIR:
  ... If let `ENUM ++_++ { id~field~^{asterisk}^ }` be `enumTypeIR`:
   .... Check that <<distinct_, the elements of `id~field~^{asterisk}^` are distinct>>.
   .... The relation holds.
  ... Else let `ENUM ++_++ < typeIR > { (id~field~ = ++_++ ;)^{asterisk}^ }` be `enumTypeIR`:
   .... Check that <<distinct_, the elements of `id~field~^{asterisk}^` are distinct>>.
   .... Check that <<nestable_enum_serializable, `typeIR` can be used in a serializable enum type>>.
   .... Check that <<Type_wf, `typeIR` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `bound`>>.
   .... The relation holds.
. Else if let `EXTERN ++_++ { (++_++ : externMethodTypeDefIR)^{asterisk}^ }` be `typeIR'''`:
 .. Group externObjectTypeIR:
  ... Check that <<CallableTypeDef_wf, `externMethodTypeDefIR` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `bound`>>, for all `externMethodTypeDefIR` in `externMethodTypeDefIR^{asterisk}^`.
  ... The relation holds.
. Else if let `PARSER ( parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^ )` be `typeIR'''`:
 .. Group parserObjectTypeIR:
  ... Check that <<ParameterTypes_wf, `parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `bound`>>.
  ... The relation holds.
. Else if let `CONTROL ( parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^ )` be `typeIR'''`:
 .. Group controlObjectTypeIR:
  ... Check that <<ParameterTypes_wf, `parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `bound`>>.
  ... The relation holds.
. Else if let `PACKAGE { typeIR^{asterisk}^ }` be `typeIR'''`:
 .. Group packageObjectTypeIR:
  ... Check that <<Type_wf, `typeIR` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `bound`>>, for all `typeIR` in `typeIR^{asterisk}^`.
  ... The relation holds.
. Else if let `TABLE ++_++ { tableMetadataStructTypeIR }` be `typeIR'''`:
 .. Group tableObjectTypeIR:
  ... Check that <<Type_wf, `tableMetadataStructTypeIR` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `bound`>>.
  ... The relation holds.
. Else if let `defaultTypeIR` be `typeIR'''`:
 .. Group defaultTypeIR:
  ... The relation holds.
. Else if let `invalidHeaderTypeIR` be `typeIR'''`:
 .. Group invalidHeaderTypeIR:
  ... The relation holds.
. Else if let `sequenceTypeIR` be `typeIR'''`:
 .. Group sequenceTypeIR:
  ... If let `SEQ < typeIR^{asterisk}^ >` be `sequenceTypeIR`:
   .... Check that <<Type_wf, `typeIR` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `bound`>>, for all `typeIR` in `typeIR^{asterisk}^`.
   .... The relation holds.
  ... Else let `SEQ < typeIR^{asterisk}^ , ... >` be `sequenceTypeIR`:
   .... Check that <<Type_wf, `typeIR` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `bound`>>, for all `typeIR` in `typeIR^{asterisk}^`.
   .... The relation holds.
. Else if let `recordTypeIR` be `typeIR'''`:
 .. Group recordTypeIR:
  ... If let `RECORD { (typeIR~field~ id~field~ ;)^{asterisk}^ }` be `recordTypeIR`:
   .... Check that <<distinct_, the elements of `id~field~^{asterisk}^` are distinct>>.
   .... Check that <<Type_wf, `typeIR~field~` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `bound`>>, for all `typeIR~field~` in `typeIR~field~^{asterisk}^`.
   .... The relation holds.
  ... Else let `RECORD { (typeIR~field~ id~field~ ;)^{asterisk}^ , ... }` be `recordTypeIR`:
   .... Check that <<distinct_, the elements of `id~field~^{asterisk}^` are distinct>>.
   .... Check that <<Type_wf, `typeIR~field~` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `bound`>>, for all `typeIR~field~` in `typeIR~field~^{asterisk}^`.
   .... The relation holds.
. Else if let `SET < typeIR'^{asterisk}^ >` be `typeIR'''`:
 .. Check that `typeIR'^{asterisk}^` is a list of length 1.
 .. Let `[typeIR]` be `typeIR'^{asterisk}^`.
 .. Group setTypeIR:
  ... Check that <<nestable_set, `typeIR` can be used in a set type>>.
  ... Check that <<Type_wf, `typeIR` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `bound`>>.
  ... The relation holds.
. Group tableMetadataTypeIR:
 .. If let `TABLE_ENUM ++_++ { id^{asterisk}^ }` be `typeIR'''`:
  ... Check that <<distinct_, the elements of `id^{asterisk}^` are distinct>>.
  ... The relation holds.
 .. Else if let `TABLE_STRUCT ++_++ { HIT ++_++ ; MISS ++_++ ; ACTION_RUN tableMetadataEnumTypeIR ; }` be `typeIR'''`:
  ... Check that <<Type_wf, `tableMetadataEnumTypeIR` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `bound`>>.
