relation ConstructorType_wf: `bound` and `CONSTRUCTOR ( parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^ ) : typeIR~object~`


. Group externObjectTypeIR:
 .. Check that <<ConstructorParameterTypes_wf, `parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `bound`>>.
 .. Check that <<Type_wf, `typeIR~object~` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `bound`>>.
 .. Let `typeIR'` be <<canon_typeIR, the canonicalized form of `typeIR~object~`>>.
 .. Check that `typeIR'` has type `externObjectTypeIR`.
 .. Let `externObjectTypeIR` be `typeIR'`.
 .. Let `typeIR^{asterisk}^` be the list of `typeIR`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
    * Let `typeIR` be the type of `parameterTypeIR`.
--
+
for each `parameterTypeIR` in `parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^`
 .. Check that `<<nestable_constructor_extern, $nestable_constructor_extern(typeIR)>>`, for all `typeIR` in `typeIR^{asterisk}^`.
 .. The relation holds.
. Group parserObjectTypeIR:
 .. Check that <<ConstructorParameterTypes_wf, `parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `bound`>>.
 .. Check that <<Type_wf, `typeIR~object~` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `bound`>>.
 .. Let `typeIR'` be <<canon_typeIR, the canonicalized form of `typeIR~object~`>>.
 .. Check that `typeIR'` has type `parserObjectTypeIR`.
 .. Let `parserObjectTypeIR` be `typeIR'`.
 .. Let `typeIR^{asterisk}^` be the list of `typeIR`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
    * Let `typeIR` be the type of `parameterTypeIR`.
--
+
for each `parameterTypeIR` in `parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^`
 .. Check that `<<nestable_constructor_parser, $nestable_constructor_parser(typeIR)>>`, for all `typeIR` in `typeIR^{asterisk}^`.
 .. The relation holds.
. Group controlObjectTypeIR:
 .. Check that <<ConstructorParameterTypes_wf, `parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `bound`>>.
 .. Check that <<Type_wf, `typeIR~object~` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `bound`>>.
 .. Let `typeIR'` be <<canon_typeIR, the canonicalized form of `typeIR~object~`>>.
 .. Check that `typeIR'` has type `controlObjectTypeIR`.
 .. Let `controlObjectTypeIR` be `typeIR'`.
 .. Let `typeIR^{asterisk}^` be the list of `typeIR`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
    * Let `typeIR` be the type of `parameterTypeIR`.
--
+
for each `parameterTypeIR` in `parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^`
 .. Check that `<<nestable_constructor_control, $nestable_constructor_control(typeIR)>>`, for all `typeIR` in `typeIR^{asterisk}^`.
 .. The relation holds.
. Group packageObjectTypeIR:
 .. Check that <<ConstructorParameterTypes_wf, `parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `bound`>>.
 .. Check that <<Type_wf, `typeIR~object~` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `bound`>>.
 .. Let `typeIR'` be <<canon_typeIR, the canonicalized form of `typeIR~object~`>>.
 .. Check that `typeIR'` has type `packageObjectTypeIR`.
 .. Let `packageObjectTypeIR` be `typeIR'`.
 .. Let `typeIR^{asterisk}^` be the list of `typeIR`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
    * Let `typeIR` be the type of `parameterTypeIR`.
--
+
for each `parameterTypeIR` in `parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^`
 .. Check that `<<nestable_constructor_package, $nestable_constructor_package(typeIR)>>`, for all `typeIR` in `typeIR^{asterisk}^`.
 .. The relation holds.


relation ConstructorTypeDef_wf: `bound` and `CONSTRUCTOR < tid~tparam_expl~^{asterisk}^ , tid~tparam_impl~^{asterisk}^ > ( parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^ ) : typeIR~object~`


. Group :
 .. Check that `<<definable_constructor, $definable_constructor(typeIR~object~)>>`.
 .. Check that <<distinct_, the elements of `tid~tparam_expl~^{asterisk}^ {pp} tid~tparam_impl~^{asterisk}^` are distinct>>.
 .. Let `bound~inner~` be <<union_set, the union of the sets `bound` and `{ tid~tparam_expl~^{asterisk}^ {pp} tid~tparam_impl~^{asterisk}^ }`>>.
 .. Check that <<ConstructorType_wf, `CONSTRUCTOR ( parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^ ) : typeIR~object~` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `bound~inner~`>>.
 .. The relation holds.


relation Expr_eval_lctk: `p`, `TC`, and <<typedExpressionIR, `expressionIR` annotated with `++_++`>>


. If let `booleanLiteral` be `expressionIR`:
 .. Group literalExpressionIR-boolean:
  ... If `booleanLiteral` matches pattern `TRUE`:
   .... Result in `B true`.
  ... Else `booleanLiteral` matches pattern `FALSE`:
   .... Result in `B false`.
. Else if let `integerLiteral` be `expressionIR`:
 .. Group literalExpressionIR-number:
  ... If let `D i` be `integerLiteral`:
   .... Result in `D i`.
  ... Else if let `n W i` be `integerLiteral`:
   .... Result in `n W i`.
  ... Else let `n S i` be `integerLiteral`:
   .... Result in `n S i`.
. Else if let `" text "` be `expressionIR`:
 .. Group literalExpressionIR-stringLiteral:
  ... Result in `" text "`.
. Else if let `prefixedNameIR` be `expressionIR`:
 .. Group referenceExpressionIR:
  ... Let `value` be `<<find_var_value_t, $find_var_value_t(p, TC, prefixedNameIR)>>`.
  ... Result in `value`.
. Else if let `defaultExpression` be `expressionIR`:
 .. Group defaultExpressionIR:
  ... Result in `DEFAULT`.
. Else if let `unop typedExpressionIR` be `expressionIR`:
 .. Group unaryExpressionIR:
  ... Let `value` be the result of <<Expr_eval_lctk, the local compile-time evaluation of `typedExpressionIR`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Result in <<un_op, `unop` `value`>>.
. Else if let `typedExpressionIR~l~ binop' typedExpressionIR~r~` be `expressionIR`:
 .. Group binaryExpressionIR:
  ... Check that `binop'` is not in `[&&, ||]`.
  ... Let `value~l~` be the result of <<Expr_eval_lctk, the local compile-time evaluation of `typedExpressionIR~l~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `value~r~` be the result of <<Expr_eval_lctk, the local compile-time evaluation of `typedExpressionIR~r~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Result in <<bin_op, `value~l~` `binop'` `value~r~`>>.
  ... If `binop'` matches pattern `&&`:
   .... Let `value` be the result of <<Expr_eval_lctk, the local compile-time evaluation of `typedExpressionIR~l~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Else if `value` is equal to `B false`:
    ..... Result in `B false`.
   .... Else if `value` is equal to `B true`:
    ..... Let `value~r~` be the result of <<Expr_eval_lctk, the local compile-time evaluation of `typedExpressionIR~r~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
    ..... Result in `value~r~`.
  ... Else if `binop'` matches pattern `||`:
   .... Let `value` be the result of <<Expr_eval_lctk, the local compile-time evaluation of `typedExpressionIR~l~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Else if `value` is equal to `B true`:
    ..... Result in `B true`.
   .... Else if `value` is equal to `B false`:
    ..... Let `value~r~` be the result of <<Expr_eval_lctk, the local compile-time evaluation of `typedExpressionIR~r~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
    ..... Result in `value~r~`.
. Else if let `typedExpressionIR~cond~ ? typedExpressionIR~true~ : typedExpressionIR~false~` be `expressionIR`:
 .. Group ternaryExpressionIR:
  ... Let `value` be the result of <<Expr_eval_lctk, the local compile-time evaluation of `typedExpressionIR~cond~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Else if `value` is equal to `B true`:
