relation Type_ok: `p`, `TC`, and `typeOrVoid`


. Check that `typeOrVoid` matches pattern `VOID`.
. Group void:
 .. Result in the type `VOID` and a set of fresh type variables `[ ]`.
. If let `baseType` be `typeOrVoid`:
 .. If `baseType` matches pattern `BOOL`:
  ... Group boolean:
   .... Result in the type `BOOL` and a set of fresh type variables `[ ]`.
 .. Else if `baseType` matches pattern `ERROR`:
  ... Group error:
   .... Result in the type `ERROR` and a set of fresh type variables `[ ]`.
 .. Else if `baseType` matches pattern `MATCH_KIND`:
  ... Group matchKind:
   .... Result in the type `MATCH_KIND` and a set of fresh type variables `[ ]`.
 .. Else if `baseType` matches pattern `STRING`:
  ... Group string:
   .... Result in the type `STRING` and a set of fresh type variables `[ ]`.
 .. Else if `baseType` matches pattern `INT`:
  ... Group arbitraryInt:
   .... Result in the type `INT` and a set of fresh type variables `[ ]`.
 .. Group fixedInt:
  ... If let `INT < int >` be `baseType`:
   .... Check that `int` has type `nat`.
   .... Let `n` be `int`.
   .... Result in the type `INT < n >` and a set of fresh type variables `[ ]`.
  ... Else if let `INT < ( expression ) >` be `baseType`:
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Check that `<<ctk_of_typedExpressionIR, $ctk_of_typedExpressionIR(typedExpressionIR)>>` matches pattern `LCTK`.
   .... Let `value` be the result of <<Expr_eval_lctk, the local compile-time evaluation of `typedExpressionIR`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Let `int` be <<int_of_value, the integer representation of  `value`>>.
   .... Check that `int` has type `nat`.
   .... Let `n` be `int`.
   .... Result in the type `INT < n >` and a set of fresh type variables `[ ]`.
 .. Group fixedBit:
  ... If `baseType` matches pattern `BIT`:
   .... Result in the type `BIT < 1 >` and a set of fresh type variables `[ ]`.
  ... Else if let `BIT < int >` be `baseType`:
   .... Check that `int` has type `nat`.
   .... Let `n` be `int`.
   .... Result in the type `BIT < n >` and a set of fresh type variables `[ ]`.
  ... Else if let `BIT < ( expression ) >` be `baseType`:
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Check that `<<ctk_of_typedExpressionIR, $ctk_of_typedExpressionIR(typedExpressionIR)>>` matches pattern `LCTK`.
   .... Let `value` be the result of <<Expr_eval_lctk, the local compile-time evaluation of `typedExpressionIR`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Let `int` be <<int_of_value, the integer representation of  `value`>>.
   .... Check that `int` has type `nat`.
   .... Let `n` be `int`.
   .... Result in the type `BIT < n >` and a set of fresh type variables `[ ]`.
 .. Group variableBit:
  ... If let `VARBIT < int >` be `baseType`:
   .... Check that `int` has type `nat`.
   .... Let `n` be `int`.
   .... Result in the type `VARBIT < n >` and a set of fresh type variables `[ ]`.
  ... Else if let `VARBIT < ( expression ) >` be `baseType`:
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Check that `<<ctk_of_typedExpressionIR, $ctk_of_typedExpressionIR(typedExpressionIR)>>` matches pattern `LCTK`.
   .... Let `value` be the result of <<Expr_eval_lctk, the local compile-time evaluation of `typedExpressionIR`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Let `int` be <<int_of_value, the integer representation of  `value`>>.
   .... Check that `int` has type `nat`.
   .... Let `n` be `int`.
   .... Result in the type `VARBIT < n >` and a set of fresh type variables `[ ]`.
. Else if let `prefixedTypeName` be `typeOrVoid`:
 .. Group prefixedTypeName:
  ... Let `prefixedNameIR` be <<prefixedTypeName, the prefixed name of  `prefixedTypeName`>>.
  ... Let `typeDefIR'^?^` be `<<find_typeDef_t, $find_typeDef_t(p, TC, prefixedNameIR)>>`.
  ... Check that `typeDefIR'^?^` is Some value.
  ... Let `typeDefIR` be `typeDefIR'^?^`.
  ... If `<<is_monomorphic_typeDefIR, $is_monomorphic_typeDefIR(typeDefIR)>>`:
   .... Let `typeIR` be `<<type_of_typeDefIR, $type_of_typeDefIR(typeDefIR)>>`.
   .... Result in the type `typeIR` and a set of fresh type variables `[ ]`.
  ... Else `~<<is_monomorphic_typeDefIR, $is_monomorphic_typeDefIR(typeDefIR)>>`:
   .... Check that (`[ ]`, `[ ]`) is equal to `<<type_parameters_of_typeDefIR, $type_parameters_of_typeDefIR(typeDefIR)>>`.
   .... Result in the type `typeDefIR < [ ] >` and a set of fresh type variables `[ ]`.
. Else if let `prefixedTypeName < typeArgumentList >` be `typeOrVoid`:
 .. Group specializedType:
  ... Let `prefixedNameIR` be <<prefixedTypeName, the prefixed name of  `prefixedTypeName`>>.
  ... Let `typeDefIR'^?^` be `<<find_typeDef_t, $find_typeDef_t(p, TC, prefixedNameIR)>>`.
  ... Check that `typeDefIR'^?^` is Some value.
  ... Let `typeDefIR` be `typeDefIR'^?^`.
  ... Check that `<<is_polymorphic_typeDefIR, $is_polymorphic_typeDefIR(typeDefIR)>>`.
  ... Let `typeArgument^{asterisk}^` be <<flatten_typeArgumentList, the list of type arguments in `typeArgumentList`>>.
  ... Let `typeIR~arg~^{asterisk}^` and `tid~fresh~^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<TypeArguments_ok, typing `typeArgument^{asterisk}^`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Result in the type `typeDefIR < typeIR~arg~^{asterisk}^ >` and a set of fresh type variables `tid~fresh~^{asterisk}^`.
. Else if let `namedType [ expression~size~ ]` be `typeOrVoid`:
 .. Group headerStackType:
  ... If let `prefixedTypeName` be `namedType`:
   .... Let `typeIR~base~` and `tid^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Type_ok, typing `prefixedTypeName`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Check that `tid^{asterisk}^` is an empty list.
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR~size~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~size~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Check that `<<ctk_of_typedExpressionIR, $ctk_of_typedExpressionIR(typedExpressionIR~size~)>>` matches pattern `LCTK`.
   .... Let `value~size~` be the result of <<Expr_eval_lctk, the local compile-time evaluation of `typedExpressionIR~size~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Let `int` be <<int_of_value, the integer representation of  `value~size~`>>.
   .... Check that `int` has type `nat`.
   .... Let `n~size~` be `int`.
   .... Result in the type `typeIR~base~ [ n~size~ ]` and a set of fresh type variables `[ ]`.
  ... Else let `specializedType` be `namedType`:
   .... Let `typeIR~base~` and `tid~fresh~^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Type_ok, typing `specializedType`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR~size~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~size~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Check that `<<ctk_of_typedExpressionIR, $ctk_of_typedExpressionIR(typedExpressionIR~size~)>>` matches pattern `LCTK`.
   .... Let `value~size~` be the result of <<Expr_eval_lctk, the local compile-time evaluation of `typedExpressionIR~size~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Let `int` be <<int_of_value, the integer representation of  `value~size~`>>.
   .... Check that `int` has type `nat`.
   .... Let `n~size~` be `int`.
   .... Result in the type `typeIR~base~ [ n~size~ ]` and a set of fresh type variables `tid~fresh~^{asterisk}^`.
. Else if let `LIST < typeArgument >` be `typeOrVoid`:
 .. Group listType:
  ... Let `typeIR~arg~` and `tid~fresh~^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<TypeArgument_ok, typing `typeArgument`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Result in the type `LIST < typeIR~arg~ >` and a set of fresh type variables `tid~fresh~^{asterisk}^`.
. Else if let `TUPLE < typeArgumentList >` be `typeOrVoid`:
 .. Group tupleType:
  ... Let `typeArgument^{asterisk}^` be <<flatten_typeArgumentList, the list of type arguments in `typeArgumentList`>>.
  ... Let `typeIR~arg~^{asterisk}^` and `tid~fresh~^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<TypeArguments_ok, typing `typeArgument^{asterisk}^`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Result in the type `TUPLE < typeIR~arg~^{asterisk}^ >` and a set of fresh type variables `tid~fresh~^{asterisk}^`.


relation TypeArgument_ok: `p`, `TC`, and `typeArgument`


. If let `type` be `typeArgument`:
 .. Group type:
  ... Let `typeIR` and `tid~impl~^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Type_ok, typing `type`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Result in the type argument `typeIR` and set of fresh type variables `tid~impl~^{asterisk}^`.
. Else if let `nonTypeName` be `typeArgument`:
 .. Group nonTypeName:
  ... Let `tid` be <<name, the name of `nonTypeName`>>.
  ... Result in the type argument `tid` and set of fresh type variables `[ ]`.
. Check that `typeArgument` has type `realTypeArgument`.
. Let `realTypeArgument` be `typeArgument`.
. If `realTypeArgument` matches pattern `VOID`:
 .. Group void:
  ... Result in the type argument `VOID` and set of fresh type variables `[ ]`.
. Else if `realTypeArgument` matches pattern `_`:
 .. Group dontcare:
  ... Let `tid~impl~` be <<fresh_tid, a fresh type variable>>.
  ... Result in the type argument `tid~impl~` and set of fresh type variables `[tid~impl~]`.


relation TypeArguments_ok: `p`, `TC`, and `typeArgument^{asterisk}^`


. If `typeArgument^{asterisk}^` is an empty list:
 .. Group nil:
  ... Result in the type argument list `[ ]` and set of fresh type variables `[ ]`.
. Else let `typeArgument~h~ {two-colons} typeArgument~t~^{asterisk}^` be `typeArgument^{asterisk}^`:
 .. Group cons:
  ... Let `typeArgumentIR~h~` and `tid~impl_h~^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<TypeArgument_ok, typing `typeArgument~h~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `typeArgumentIR~t~^{asterisk}^` and `tid~impl_t~^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<TypeArguments_ok, typing `typeArgument~t~^{asterisk}^`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `tid~impl~^{asterisk}^` be `tid~impl_h~^{asterisk}^ {pp} tid~impl_t~^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Result in the type argument list `typeArgumentIR~h~ {two-colons} typeArgumentIR~t~^{asterisk}^` and set of fresh type variables `tid~impl~^{asterisk}^`.


relation Sub_expl: `typeIR~a~` and `typeIR~b~`


. Group :
 .. Let `typeIR~a_canon~` be <<canon_typeIR, the canonicalized form of `typeIR~a~`>>.
 .. Let `typeIR~b_canon~` be <<canon_typeIR, the canonicalized form of `typeIR~b~`>>.
 .. Check that <<Sub_expl_canon, `typeIR~a_canon~` can be explicitly cast to `typeIR~b_canon~` after canonicalization>>.
 .. The relation holds.


relation Sub_expl_canon: `typeIR~a~` and `typeIR~b~`


. Group equals:
 .. Check that <<Type_alpha, `typeIR~a~` and `typeIR~b~` are the same type>>.
 .. The relation holds.
. Group not-equals:
 .. Check that <<Type_alpha, `typeIR~a~` and `typeIR~b~` are not the same type>>.
 .. Check that <<Sub_expl_canon_neq, `typeIR~a~` can be explicitly cast to `typeIR~b~` when they are not the same type after canonicalization>>.
 .. The relation holds.


relation Sub_expl_canon_neq: `typeIR''''''` and `typeIR'''''''`


. If let `boolTypeIR` be `typeIR''''''`:
 .. Check that `typeIR'''''''` is equal to `BIT < 1 >`.
 .. Group boolean-fixBit:
  ... The relation holds.
. Else if let `integerTypeIR` be `typeIR''''''`:
 .. If `integerTypeIR` matches pattern `INT`:
  ... Group arbitraryInt:
   .... If `typeIR'''''''` is equal to `BOOL`:
    ..... The relation holds.
   .... Else if let `integerTypeIR'` be `typeIR'''''''`:
    ..... If let `INT < ++_++ >` be `integerTypeIR'`:
     ...... The relation holds.
    ..... Else if let `BIT < ++_++ >` be `integerTypeIR'`:
     ...... The relation holds.
 .. Else if let `INT < nat >` be `integerTypeIR`:
  ... Check that `typeIR'''''''` has type `integerTypeIR`.
  ... Let `integerTypeIR` be `typeIR'''''''`.
  ... Group fixInt:
   .... If `integerTypeIR` matches pattern `INT`:
    ..... The relation holds.
   .... Else if `integerTypeIR` matches pattern `INT < % >`:
    ..... The relation holds.
   .... Check that `integerTypeIR` is equal to `BIT < nat >`.
   .... The relation holds.
 .. Else if let `BIT < nat >` be `integerTypeIR`:
  ... Group fixBit:
   .... If `nat` is equal to `1`:
    ..... Check that `typeIR'''''''` is equal to `BOOL`.
    ..... The relation holds.
   .... Else if `typeIR'''''''` is equal to `INT`:
    ..... The relation holds.
   .... Else if `typeIR'''''''` is equal to `INT < nat >`:
    ..... The relation holds.
   .... Else if let `integerTypeIR` be `typeIR'''''''`:
    ..... Check that `integerTypeIR` matches pattern `BIT < % >`.
    ..... The relation holds.
. Group newTypeIR:
 .. If let `TYPE ++_++ typeIR~a~` be `typeIR''''''`:
  ... Check that <<Sub_impl, `typeIR~a~` can be implicitly cast to `typeIR'''''''`>>.
  ... The relation holds.
 .. Else if let `TYPE ++_++ typeIR~b~` be `typeIR'''''''`:
  ... Check that <<Sub_impl, `typeIR''''''` can be implicitly cast to `typeIR~b~`>>.
  ... The relation holds.
. Group enumTypeIR-serializable:
 .. If let `enumTypeIR` be `typeIR''''''`:
  ... Check that `enumTypeIR` matches pattern `ENUM % < % > { % }`.
  ... Let `ENUM ++_++ < typeIR~a~ > { ++_++^{asterisk}^ }` be `enumTypeIR`.
  ... Check that <<Sub_impl, `typeIR~a~` can be implicitly cast to `typeIR'''''''`>>.
  ... The relation holds.
 .. Else if let `enumTypeIR` be `typeIR'''''''`:
  ... Check that `enumTypeIR` matches pattern `ENUM % < % > { % }`.
  ... Let `ENUM ++_++ < typeIR~b~ > { ++_++^{asterisk}^ }` be `enumTypeIR`.
  ... Check that <<Sub_impl, `typeIR''''''` can be implicitly cast to `typeIR~b~`>>.
  ... The relation holds.
. If let `defaultTypeIR` be `typeIR''''''`:
 .. Group defaultTypeIR:
  ... Check that `<<is_defaultable_typeIR, $is_defaultable_typeIR(typeIR''''''')>>`.
  ... The relation holds.
. Else if let `invalidHeaderTypeIR` be `typeIR''''''`:
 .. Group invalidHeaderTypeIR:
  ... If let `HEADER ++_++ { ++_++^{asterisk}^ }` be `typeIR'''''''`:
   .... The relation holds.
  ... Else if let `HEADER_UNION ++_++ { ++_++^{asterisk}^ }` be `typeIR'''''''`:
   .... The relation holds.
. Else if let `sequenceTypeIR` be `typeIR''''''`:
 .. If let `SEQ < typeIR~a~^{asterisk}^ >` be `sequenceTypeIR`:
  ... Group sequenceTypeIR-non-default:
   .... If let `LIST < typeIR~b~ >` be `typeIR'''''''`:
    ..... Check that <<Sub_expl, `typeIR~a~` can be explicitly cast to `typeIR~b~`>>, for all `typeIR~a~` in `typeIR~a~^{asterisk}^`.
    ..... The relation holds.
   .... Else if let `TUPLE < typeIR~b~^{asterisk}^ >` be `typeIR'''''''`:
    ..... Check that <<Sub_expl, `typeIR~a~` can be explicitly cast to `typeIR~b~`>>, for all `typeIR~a~` in `typeIR~a~^{asterisk}^` and `typeIR~b~` in `typeIR~b~^{asterisk}^`.
    ..... The relation holds.
   .... Else if let `typeIR~b~ [ n~size~ ]` be `typeIR'''''''`:
    ..... Check that the length of `typeIR~a~^{asterisk}^` is less than or equal to `n~size~`.
