relation Expr_ok: `p`, `TC`, and `expression'''`


. If let `booleanLiteral` be `expression'''`:
 .. Group literalExpression-boolean:
  ... If `booleanLiteral` matches pattern `TRUE`:
   .... Let `expressionNoteIR` be <<expressionNoteIR, type `BOOL` and compile-time known-ness `LCTK`>>.
   .... Result in the typed expression <<typedExpressionIR, `TRUE` annotated with `expressionNoteIR`>>.
  ... Else `booleanLiteral` matches pattern `FALSE`:
   .... Let `expressionNoteIR` be <<expressionNoteIR, type `BOOL` and compile-time known-ness `LCTK`>>.
   .... Result in the typed expression <<typedExpressionIR, `FALSE` annotated with `expressionNoteIR`>>.
. Else if let `integerLiteral` be `expression'''`:
 .. Group literalExpression-number:
  ... If let `D i` be `integerLiteral`:
   .... Let `expressionNoteIR` be <<expressionNoteIR, type `INT` and compile-time known-ness `LCTK`>>.
   .... Result in the typed expression <<typedExpressionIR, `D i` annotated with `expressionNoteIR`>>.
  ... Else if let `n S i` be `integerLiteral`:
   .... Let `expressionNoteIR` be <<expressionNoteIR, type `INT < n >` and compile-time known-ness `LCTK`>>.
   .... Result in the typed expression <<typedExpressionIR, `n S i` annotated with `expressionNoteIR`>>.
  ... Else let `n W i` be `integerLiteral`:
   .... Let `expressionNoteIR` be <<expressionNoteIR, type `BIT < n >` and compile-time known-ness `LCTK`>>.
   .... Result in the typed expression <<typedExpressionIR, `n W i` annotated with `expressionNoteIR`>>.
. Else if let `" text "` be `expression'''`:
 .. Group literalExpression-stringLiteral:
  ... Let `expressionNoteIR` be <<expressionNoteIR, type `STRING` and compile-time known-ness `LCTK`>>.
  ... Result in the typed expression <<typedExpressionIR, `" text "` annotated with `expressionNoteIR`>>.
. Group referenceExpression:
 .. If let `prefixedNonTypeName` be `expression'''`:
  ... Let `prefixedNameIR` be <<prefixedNonTypeName, the prefixed name of  `prefixedNonTypeName`>>.
  ... Let `varTypeIR^?^` be `<<find_var_t, $find_var_t(p, TC, prefixedNameIR)>>`.
  ... Check that `varTypeIR^?^` is Some value.
  ... Let `++_++ typeIR ctk ++_++^?^` be `varTypeIR^?^`.
  ... Let `expressionNoteIR` be <<expressionNoteIR, type `typeIR` and compile-time known-ness `ctk`>>.
  ... Result in the typed expression <<typedExpressionIR, `prefixedNameIR` annotated with `expressionNoteIR`>>.
 .. Else if `expression'''` is equal to `THIS`:
  ... Let `prefixedNameIR` be `"this"`.
  ... Let `varTypeIR^?^` be `<<find_var_t, $find_var_t(p, TC, prefixedNameIR)>>`.
  ... Check that `varTypeIR^?^` is Some value.
  ... Let `++_++ typeIR ctk ++_++^?^` be `varTypeIR^?^`.
  ... Let `expressionNoteIR` be <<expressionNoteIR, type `typeIR` and compile-time known-ness `ctk`>>.
  ... Result in the typed expression <<typedExpressionIR, `prefixedNameIR` annotated with `expressionNoteIR`>>.
. If let `defaultExpression` be `expression'''`:
 .. Group defaultExpression:
  ... Let `expressionNoteIR` be <<expressionNoteIR, type `DEFAULT` and compile-time known-ness `LCTK`>>.
  ... Result in the typed expression <<typedExpressionIR, `...` annotated with `expressionNoteIR`>>.
. Else if let `unop expression` be `expression'''`:
 .. If `unop` matches pattern `!`:
  ... Group unaryExpression-lnot:
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR'^?^` be `<<reduce_serenum_unary, $reduce_serenum_unary(typedExpressionIR, $compat_lnot)>>`.
   .... Check that `typedExpressionIR'^?^` is Some value.
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR~reduced~` be `typedExpressionIR'^?^`.
   .... Let `typeIR~reduced~` be <<type_of_typedExpressionIR, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~reduced~`>>.
   .... Let `ctk~reduced~` be <<ctk_of_typedExpressionIR, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~reduced~`>>.
   .... Let `expressionNoteIR` be <<expressionNoteIR, type `typeIR~reduced~` and compile-time known-ness `ctk~reduced~`>>.
   .... Result in the typed expression <<typedExpressionIR, `! typedExpressionIR~reduced~` annotated with `expressionNoteIR`>>.
 .. Else if `unop` matches pattern `~`:
  ... Group unaryExpression-bnot:
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR'^?^` be `<<reduce_serenum_unary, $reduce_serenum_unary(typedExpressionIR, $compat_bnot)>>`.
   .... Check that `typedExpressionIR'^?^` is Some value.
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR~reduced~` be `typedExpressionIR'^?^`.
   .... Let `typeIR~reduced~` be <<type_of_typedExpressionIR, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~reduced~`>>.
   .... Let `ctk~reduced~` be <<ctk_of_typedExpressionIR, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~reduced~`>>.
   .... Let `expressionNoteIR` be <<expressionNoteIR, type `typeIR~reduced~` and compile-time known-ness `ctk~reduced~`>>.
   .... Result in the typed expression <<typedExpressionIR, `~ typedExpressionIR~reduced~` annotated with `expressionNoteIR`>>.
 .. Group unaryExpression-uplusminus:
  ... If `unop` matches pattern `+`:
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR'^?^` be `<<reduce_serenum_unary, $reduce_serenum_unary(typedExpressionIR, $compat_uplusminus)>>`.
   .... Check that `typedExpressionIR'^?^` is Some value.
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR~reduced~` be `typedExpressionIR'^?^`.
   .... Let `typeIR~reduced~` be <<type_of_typedExpressionIR, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~reduced~`>>.
   .... Let `ctk~reduced~` be <<ctk_of_typedExpressionIR, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~reduced~`>>.
   .... Let `expressionNoteIR` be <<expressionNoteIR, type `typeIR~reduced~` and compile-time known-ness `ctk~reduced~`>>.
   .... Result in the typed expression <<typedExpressionIR, `unop typedExpressionIR~reduced~` annotated with `expressionNoteIR`>>.
  ... Else if `unop` matches pattern `-`:
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR'^?^` be `<<reduce_serenum_unary, $reduce_serenum_unary(typedExpressionIR, $compat_uplusminus)>>`.
   .... Check that `typedExpressionIR'^?^` is Some value.
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR~reduced~` be `typedExpressionIR'^?^`.
   .... Let `typeIR~reduced~` be <<type_of_typedExpressionIR, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~reduced~`>>.
   .... Let `ctk~reduced~` be <<ctk_of_typedExpressionIR, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~reduced~`>>.
   .... Let `expressionNoteIR` be <<expressionNoteIR, type `typeIR~reduced~` and compile-time known-ness `ctk~reduced~`>>.
   .... Result in the typed expression <<typedExpressionIR, `unop typedExpressionIR~reduced~` annotated with `expressionNoteIR`>>.
. Else if let `expression~l~ binop expression~r~` be `expression'''`:
 .. Group binaryExpression-plusminusmult:
  ... Check that `binop` is in `[+, -, *]`.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~l~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~l~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~r~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~r~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)^?^` be <<coerce_binary, implicitly cast  `typedExpressionIR~l~`  and  `typedExpressionIR~r~`  to equal types>>.
  ... Check that `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)^?^` is Some value.
  ... Let `(typedExpressionIR~l_cast~, typedExpressionIR~r_cast~)` be `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)^?^`.
  ... Let `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)'^?^` be `<<reduce_serenum_binary, $reduce_serenum_binary(typedExpressionIR~l_cast~, typedExpressionIR~r_cast~, $compat_plusminusmult)>>`.
  ... Check that `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)'^?^` is Some value.
  ... Let `(typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~, typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~)` be `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)'^?^`.
  ... Let `typeIR~reduced~` be <<type_of_typedExpressionIR, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~`>>.
  ... Let `ctk~l_reduced~` be <<ctk_of_typedExpressionIR, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~`>>.
  ... Let `ctk~r_reduced~` be <<ctk_of_typedExpressionIR, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~`>>.
  ... Let `ctk~reduced~` be `<<join_ctk, $join_ctk(ctk~l_reduced~, ctk~r_reduced~)>>`.
  ... Let `expressionNoteIR` be <<expressionNoteIR, type `typeIR~reduced~` and compile-time known-ness `ctk~reduced~`>>.
  ... Result in the typed expression <<typedExpressionIR, `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~ binop typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~` annotated with `expressionNoteIR`>>.
 .. Group binaryExpression-satplusminus:
  ... Check that `binop` is in `[|+|, |-|]`.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~l~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~l~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~r~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~r~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)^?^` be <<coerce_binary, implicitly cast  `typedExpressionIR~l~`  and  `typedExpressionIR~r~`  to equal types>>.
  ... Check that `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)^?^` is Some value.
  ... Let `(typedExpressionIR~l_cast~, typedExpressionIR~r_cast~)` be `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)^?^`.
  ... Let `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)'^?^` be `<<reduce_serenum_binary, $reduce_serenum_binary(typedExpressionIR~l_cast~, typedExpressionIR~r_cast~, $compat_satplusminus)>>`.
  ... Check that `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)'^?^` is Some value.
  ... Let `(typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~, typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~)` be `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)'^?^`.
  ... Let `typeIR~reduced~` be <<type_of_typedExpressionIR, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~`>>.
  ... Let `ctk~l_reduced~` be <<ctk_of_typedExpressionIR, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~`>>.
  ... Let `ctk~r_reduced~` be <<ctk_of_typedExpressionIR, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~`>>.
  ... Let `ctk~reduced~` be `<<join_ctk, $join_ctk(ctk~l_reduced~, ctk~r_reduced~)>>`.
  ... Let `expressionNoteIR` be <<expressionNoteIR, type `typeIR~reduced~` and compile-time known-ness `ctk~reduced~`>>.
  ... Result in the typed expression <<typedExpressionIR, `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~ binop typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~` annotated with `expressionNoteIR`>>.
 .. Group binaryExpression-divmod:
  ... Check that `binop` is in `[/, %]`.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~l~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~l~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~r~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~r~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)^?^` be <<coerce_binary, implicitly cast  `typedExpressionIR~l~`  and  `typedExpressionIR~r~`  to equal types>>.
  ... Check that `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)^?^` is Some value.
  ... Let `(typedExpressionIR~l_cast~, typedExpressionIR~r_cast~)` be `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)^?^`.
  ... Let `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)'^?^` be `<<reduce_serenum_binary, $reduce_serenum_binary(typedExpressionIR~l_cast~, typedExpressionIR~r_cast~, $compat_divmod)>>`.
  ... Check that `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)'^?^` is Some value.
  ... Let `(typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~, typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~)` be `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)'^?^`.
  ... Let `typeIR~reduced~` be <<type_of_typedExpressionIR, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~`>>.
  ... Let `ctk~l_reduced~` be <<ctk_of_typedExpressionIR, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~`>>.
  ... Let `ctk~r_reduced~` be <<ctk_of_typedExpressionIR, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~`>>.
  ... If `ctk~r_reduced~` matches pattern `LCTK`:
   .... Let `value~r~` be the result of <<Expr_eval_lctk, the local compile-time evaluation of `typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Let `int` be <<int_of_value, the integer representation of  `value~r~`>>.
   .... Check that `int` has type `nat`.
   .... Let `n~r~` be `int`.
   .... Check that `n~r~` is greater than `0`.
   .... Let `ctk~reduced~` be `<<join_ctk, $join_ctk(ctk~l_reduced~, ctk~r_reduced~)>>`.
   .... Let `expressionNoteIR` be <<expressionNoteIR, type `typeIR~reduced~` and compile-time known-ness `ctk~reduced~`>>.
   .... Result in the typed expression <<typedExpressionIR, `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~ binop typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~` annotated with `expressionNoteIR`>>.
  ... Else `ctk~r_reduced~` does not match pattern `LCTK`:
   .... Let `ctk~reduced~` be `<<join_ctk, $join_ctk(ctk~l_reduced~, ctk~r_reduced~)>>`.
   .... Let `expressionNoteIR` be <<expressionNoteIR, type `typeIR~reduced~` and compile-time known-ness `ctk~reduced~`>>.
   .... Result in the typed expression <<typedExpressionIR, `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~ binop typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~` annotated with `expressionNoteIR`>>.
 .. Group binaryExpression-shift:
  ... Check that `binop` is in `[<<, >>]`.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~l~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~l~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~r~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~r~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)^?^` be `<<reduce_serenum_binary, $reduce_serenum_binary(typedExpressionIR~l~, typedExpressionIR~r~, $compat_shift)>>`.
  ... Check that `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)^?^` is Some value.
  ... Let `(typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~, typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~)` be `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)^?^`.
  ... Let `typeIR~l_reduced~` be <<type_of_typedExpressionIR, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~`>>.
  ... Let `ctk~l_reduced~` be <<ctk_of_typedExpressionIR, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~`>>.
  ... Let `typeIR~r_reduced~` be <<type_of_typedExpressionIR, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~`>>.
  ... Let `ctk~r_reduced~` be <<ctk_of_typedExpressionIR, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~`>>.
  ... Else if `<<is_fixedBitTypeIR, $is_fixedBitTypeIR(typeIR~r_reduced~)>>`:
   .... Let `ctk~reduced~` be `<<join_ctk, $join_ctk(ctk~l_reduced~, ctk~r_reduced~)>>`.
   .... Let `expressionNoteIR` be <<expressionNoteIR, type `typeIR~l_reduced~` and compile-time known-ness `ctk~reduced~`>>.
   .... Result in the typed expression <<typedExpressionIR, `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~ binop typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~` annotated with `expressionNoteIR`>>.
  ... Else if `ctk~r_reduced~` matches pattern `LCTK`:
   .... If `<<is_arbitraryIntTypeIR, $is_arbitraryIntTypeIR(typeIR~r_reduced~)>>`:
    ..... Let `ctk~reduced~` be `<<join_ctk, $join_ctk(ctk~l_reduced~, ctk~r_reduced~)>>`.
    ..... Let `expressionNoteIR` be <<expressionNoteIR, type `typeIR~l_reduced~` and compile-time known-ness `ctk~reduced~`>>.
    ..... Result in the typed expression <<typedExpressionIR, `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~ binop typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~` annotated with `expressionNoteIR`>>.
   .... Else if `<<is_fixedIntTypeIR, $is_fixedIntTypeIR(typeIR~r_reduced~)>>`:
    ..... Let `ctk~reduced~` be `<<join_ctk, $join_ctk(ctk~l_reduced~, ctk~r_reduced~)>>`.
    ..... Let `expressionNoteIR` be <<expressionNoteIR, type `typeIR~l_reduced~` and compile-time known-ness `ctk~reduced~`>>.
    ..... Result in the typed expression <<typedExpressionIR, `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~ binop typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~` annotated with `expressionNoteIR`>>.
 .. Group binaryExpression-equality:
  ... Check that `binop` is in `[==, !=]`.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~l~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~l~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~r~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~r~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)^?^` be <<coerce_binary, implicitly cast  `typedExpressionIR~l~`  and  `typedExpressionIR~r~`  to equal types>>.
  ... Check that `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)^?^` is Some value.
  ... Let `(typedExpressionIR~l_cast~, typedExpressionIR~r_cast~)` be `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)^?^`.
  ... Let `typeIR~cast~` be <<type_of_typedExpressionIR, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~l_cast~`>>.
  ... Let `ctk~l_cast~` be <<ctk_of_typedExpressionIR, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~l_cast~`>>.
  ... Let `ctk~r_cast~` be <<ctk_of_typedExpressionIR, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~r_cast~`>>.
  ... Check that `<<is_equalable_typeIR, $is_equalable_typeIR(typeIR~cast~)>>`.
  ... Let `ctk~cast~` be `<<join_ctk, $join_ctk(ctk~l_cast~, ctk~r_cast~)>>`.
  ... Let `expressionNoteIR` be <<expressionNoteIR, type `BOOL` and compile-time known-ness `ctk~cast~`>>.
  ... Result in the typed expression <<typedExpressionIR, `typedExpressionIR~l_cast~ binop typedExpressionIR~r_cast~` annotated with `expressionNoteIR`>>.
 .. Group binaryExpression-comparison:
  ... Check that `binop` is in `[<=, >=, <, >]`.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~l~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~l~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~r~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~r~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)^?^` be <<coerce_binary, implicitly cast  `typedExpressionIR~l~`  and  `typedExpressionIR~r~`  to equal types>>.
  ... Check that `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)^?^` is Some value.
  ... Let `(typedExpressionIR~l_cast~, typedExpressionIR~r_cast~)` be `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)^?^`.
  ... Let `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)'^?^` be `<<reduce_serenum_binary, $reduce_serenum_binary(typedExpressionIR~l_cast~, typedExpressionIR~r_cast~, $compat_compare)>>`.
  ... Check that `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)'^?^` is Some value.
  ... Let `(typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~, typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~)` be `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)'^?^`.
  ... Let `typeIR~reduced~` be <<type_of_typedExpressionIR, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~`>>.
  ... Let `ctk~l_reduced~` be <<ctk_of_typedExpressionIR, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~`>>.
  ... Let `ctk~r_reduced~` be <<ctk_of_typedExpressionIR, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~`>>.
  ... Let `ctk~reduced~` be `<<join_ctk, $join_ctk(ctk~l_reduced~, ctk~r_reduced~)>>`.
  ... Let `expressionNoteIR` be <<expressionNoteIR, type `BOOL` and compile-time known-ness `ctk~reduced~`>>.
  ... Result in the typed expression <<typedExpressionIR, `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~ binop typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~` annotated with `expressionNoteIR`>>.
 .. Group binaryExpression-bitwise:
  ... Check that `binop` is in `[&, ^, |]`.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~l~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~l~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~r~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~r~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)^?^` be <<coerce_binary, implicitly cast  `typedExpressionIR~l~`  and  `typedExpressionIR~r~`  to equal types>>.
  ... Check that `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)^?^` is Some value.
  ... Let `(typedExpressionIR~l_cast~, typedExpressionIR~r_cast~)` be `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)^?^`.
  ... Let `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)'^?^` be `<<reduce_serenum_binary, $reduce_serenum_binary(typedExpressionIR~l_cast~, typedExpressionIR~r_cast~, $compat_bitwise)>>`.
  ... Check that `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)'^?^` is Some value.
  ... Let `(typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~, typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~)` be `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)'^?^`.
  ... Let `typeIR~reduced~` be <<type_of_typedExpressionIR, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~`>>.
  ... Let `ctk~l_reduced~` be <<ctk_of_typedExpressionIR, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~`>>.
  ... Let `ctk~r_reduced~` be <<ctk_of_typedExpressionIR, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~`>>.
  ... Let `ctk~reduced~` be `<<join_ctk, $join_ctk(ctk~l_reduced~, ctk~r_reduced~)>>`.
  ... Let `expressionNoteIR` be <<expressionNoteIR, type `typeIR~reduced~` and compile-time known-ness `ctk~reduced~`>>.
  ... Result in the typed expression <<typedExpressionIR, `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~ binop typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~` annotated with `expressionNoteIR`>>.
 .. Check that `binop` matches pattern `++`.
 .. Group binaryExpression-concat:
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~l~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~l~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~r~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~r~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)^?^` be `<<reduce_serenum_binary, $reduce_serenum_binary(typedExpressionIR~l~, typedExpressionIR~r~, $compat_concat)>>`.
  ... Check that `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)^?^` is Some value.
  ... Let `(typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~, typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~)` be `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)^?^`.
  ... Let `typeIR~l_reduced~` be <<type_of_typedExpressionIR, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~`>>.
  ... Let `ctk~l_reduced~` be <<ctk_of_typedExpressionIR, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~`>>.
  ... Let `typeIR~r_reduced~` be <<type_of_typedExpressionIR, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~`>>.
  ... Let `ctk~r_reduced~` be <<ctk_of_typedExpressionIR, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~`>>.
  ... Let `typeIR^?^` be `<<result_concat, $result_concat(typeIR~l_reduced~, typeIR~r_reduced~)>>`.
  ... Check that `typeIR^?^` is Some value.
  ... Let `typeIR~reduced~` be `typeIR^?^`.
  ... Let `ctk~reduced~` be `<<join_ctk, $join_ctk(ctk~l_reduced~, ctk~r_reduced~)>>`.
  ... Let `expressionNoteIR` be <<expressionNoteIR, type `typeIR~reduced~` and compile-time known-ness `ctk~reduced~`>>.
  ... Result in the typed expression <<typedExpressionIR, `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~ ++ typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~` annotated with `expressionNoteIR`>>.
 .. Group binaryExpression-logical:
  ... Check that `binop` is in `[&&, ||]`.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~l~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~l~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~r~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~r~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)^?^` be <<coerce_binary, implicitly cast  `typedExpressionIR~l~`  and  `typedExpressionIR~r~`  to equal types>>.
  ... Check that `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)^?^` is Some value.
  ... Let `(typedExpressionIR~l_cast~, typedExpressionIR~r_cast~)` be `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)^?^`.
  ... Let `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)'^?^` be `<<reduce_serenum_binary, $reduce_serenum_binary(typedExpressionIR~l_cast~, typedExpressionIR~r_cast~, $compat_logical)>>`.
  ... Check that `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)'^?^` is Some value.
  ... Let `(typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~, typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~)` be `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)'^?^`.
  ... Let `typeIR~reduced~` be <<type_of_typedExpressionIR, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~`>>.
  ... Let `ctk~l_reduced~` be <<ctk_of_typedExpressionIR, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~`>>.
  ... Let `ctk~r_reduced~` be <<ctk_of_typedExpressionIR, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~`>>.
  ... Let `ctk~reduced~` be `<<join_ctk, $join_ctk(ctk~l_reduced~, ctk~r_reduced~)>>`.
  ... Let `expressionNoteIR` be <<expressionNoteIR, type `typeIR~reduced~` and compile-time known-ness `ctk~reduced~`>>.
  ... Result in the typed expression <<typedExpressionIR, `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~ binop typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~` annotated with `expressionNoteIR`>>.
. Else if let `expression~cond~ ? expression~true~ : expression~false~` be `expression'''`:
 .. Group ternaryExpression:
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~cond~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~cond~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let <<expressionNoteIR, type `typeIR` and compile-time known-ness `ctk~cond~`>> be the note of `typedExpressionIR~cond~`.
  ... Check that `typeIR` has type `boolTypeIR`.
  ... Let `boolTypeIR` be `typeIR`.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~true~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~true~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~false~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~false~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)^?^` be <<coerce_binary, implicitly cast  `typedExpressionIR~true~`  and  `typedExpressionIR~false~`  to equal types>>.
  ... Check that `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)^?^` is Some value.
  ... Let `(typedExpressionIR~true_cast~, typedExpressionIR~false_cast~)` be `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)^?^`.
  ... Let `typeIR~cast~` be <<type_of_typedExpressionIR, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~true_cast~`>>.
  ... Let `ctk~true_cast~` be <<ctk_of_typedExpressionIR, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~true_cast~`>>.
  ... Let `ctk~false_cast~` be <<ctk_of_typedExpressionIR, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~false_cast~`>>.
  ... Check that `<<is_arbitraryIntTypeIR, $is_arbitraryIntTypeIR(typeIR~cast~)>>` *implies* `ctk~cond~ =/= DYN`.
  ... Let `ctk` be `<<joins_ctk, $joins_ctk([ctk~cond~, ctk~true_cast~, ctk~false_cast~])>>`.
  ... Let `expressionNoteIR` be <<expressionNoteIR, type `typeIR~cast~` and compile-time known-ness `ctk`>>.
  ... Result in the typed expression <<typedExpressionIR, `typedExpressionIR~cond~ ? typedExpressionIR~true_cast~ : typedExpressionIR~false_cast~` annotated with `expressionNoteIR`>>.
. Else if let `( type~t~ ) expression` be `expression'''`:
 .. Group castExpression:
  ... Let `typeIR~t~` and `tid^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Type_ok, typing `type~t~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Check that `tid^{asterisk}^` is an empty list.
  ... Check that <<Type_wf, `typeIR~t~` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `$bound(p, TC)`>>.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `typeIR` be <<type_of_typedExpressionIR, the type of  `typedExpressionIR`>>.
  ... Let `ctk` be <<ctk_of_typedExpressionIR, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR`>>.
  ... Check that <<Sub_expl, `typeIR` can be explicitly cast to `typeIR~t~`>>.
  ... Let `expressionNoteIR` be <<expressionNoteIR, type `typeIR~t~` and compile-time known-ness `ctk`>>.
  ... Result in the typed expression <<typedExpressionIR, `( typeIR~t~ ) typedExpressionIR` annotated with `expressionNoteIR`>>.
. Else if let `dataExpression` be `expression'''`:
 .. If `dataExpression` matches pattern `{#}`:
  ... Group dataExpression-invalid:
   .... Let `expressionNoteIR` be <<expressionNoteIR, type `HEADER_INVALID` and compile-time known-ness `LCTK`>>.
   .... Result in the typed expression <<typedExpressionIR, `{#}` annotated with `expressionNoteIR`>>.
 .. Else let `{ dataElementExpression ++_++ }` be `dataExpression`:
  ... If let `expressionList` be `dataElementExpression`:
   .... Group dataExpression-sequence:
    ..... Let `expression~e~^{asterisk}^` be <<flatten_expressionList, the list of expressions in `expressionList`>>.
    ..... If `...` is not in `expression~e~^{asterisk}^`:
     ...... Check that `expression~e~^{asterisk}^` is equal to <<flatten_expressionList, the list of expressions in `expressionList`>>.
     ...... Let `typedExpressionIR~e~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `typedExpressionIR~e~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
            * Let `typedExpressionIR~e~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~e~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
--
+
for each `expression~e~` in `expression~e~^{asterisk}^`
     ...... Let `typeIR~e~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `typeIR~e~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
            * Let `typeIR~e~` be <<type_of_typedExpressionIR, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~e~`>>.
--
+
for each `typedExpressionIR~e~` in `typedExpressionIR~e~^{asterisk}^`
     ...... Let `ctk~e~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `ctk~e~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
            * Let `ctk~e~` be <<ctk_of_typedExpressionIR, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~e~`>>.
--
+
for each `typedExpressionIR~e~` in `typedExpressionIR~e~^{asterisk}^`
     ...... Let `typeIR` be `SEQ < typeIR~e~^{asterisk}^ >`.
     ...... Let `ctk` be `<<joins_ctk, $joins_ctk(ctk~e~^{asterisk}^)>>`.
     ...... Let `expressionNoteIR` be <<expressionNoteIR, type `typeIR` and compile-time known-ness `ctk`>>.
     ...... Result in the typed expression <<typedExpressionIR, `SEQ { typedExpressionIR~e~^{asterisk}^ }` annotated with `expressionNoteIR`>>.
    ..... Else `...` is in `expression~e~^{asterisk}^`:
     ...... Let `expression''^{asterisk}^` be `<<rev_, $rev_<expression>(expression~e~^{asterisk}^)>>`.
     ...... Check that `expression''^{asterisk}^` is a non-empty list.
     ...... Let `expression' {two-colons} expression~e_h_rev~^{asterisk}^` be `expression''^{asterisk}^`.
     ...... Check that `expression'` has type `defaultExpression`.
     ...... Let `defaultExpression` be `expression'`.
     ...... Let `expression~e_h~^{asterisk}^` be `<<rev_, $rev_<expression>(expression~e_h_rev~^{asterisk}^)>>`.
     ...... Check that `...` is not in `expression~e_h~^{asterisk}^`.
     ...... Let `typedExpressionIR~e_h~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `typedExpressionIR~e_h~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
            * Let `typedExpressionIR~e_h~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~e_h~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
--
+
for each `expression~e_h~` in `expression~e_h~^{asterisk}^`
     ...... Let `typeIR~e_h~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `typeIR~e_h~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
            * Let `typeIR~e_h~` be <<type_of_typedExpressionIR, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~e_h~`>>.
--
+
for each `typedExpressionIR~e_h~` in `typedExpressionIR~e_h~^{asterisk}^`
     ...... Let `ctk~e_h~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `ctk~e_h~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
            * Let `ctk~e_h~` be <<ctk_of_typedExpressionIR, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~e_h~`>>.
--
+
for each `typedExpressionIR~e_h~` in `typedExpressionIR~e_h~^{asterisk}^`
     ...... Let `typeIR` be `SEQ < typeIR~e_h~^{asterisk}^ , ... >`.
     ...... Let `ctk` be `<<joins_ctk, $joins_ctk(ctk~e_h~^{asterisk}^)>>`.
     ...... Let `expressionNoteIR` be <<expressionNoteIR, type `typeIR` and compile-time known-ness `ctk`>>.
     ...... Result in the typed expression <<typedExpressionIR, `SEQ { typedExpressionIR~e_h~^{asterisk}^ , ... }` annotated with `expressionNoteIR`>>.
  ... Else let `recordElementExpression` be `dataElementExpression`:
   .... Group dataExpression-record:
    ..... If let `name~f~ = expression~f~` be `recordElementExpression`:
     ...... Let `nameIR~f~` be <<name, the name of `name~f~`>>.
     ...... Let `typedExpressionIR~f~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~f~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
     ...... Let `typeIR~f~` be <<type_of_typedExpressionIR, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~f~`>>.
     ...... Let `ctk~f~` be <<ctk_of_typedExpressionIR, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~f~`>>.
     ...... Let `typeIR` be `RECORD { [typeIR~f~ nameIR~f~ ;] }`.
     ...... Let `expressionNoteIR` be <<expressionNoteIR, type `typeIR` and compile-time known-ness `ctk~f~`>>.
     ...... Result in the typed expression <<typedExpressionIR, `RECORD { [nameIR~f~ = typedExpressionIR~f~] }` annotated with `expressionNoteIR`>>.
    ..... Else if let `name~f~ = expression~f~ , ...` be `recordElementExpression`:
     ...... Let `nameIR~f~` be <<name, the name of `name~f~`>>.
     ...... Let `typedExpressionIR~f~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~f~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
     ...... Let `typeIR~f~` be <<type_of_typedExpressionIR, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~f~`>>.
     ...... Let `ctk~f~` be <<ctk_of_typedExpressionIR, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~f~`>>.
     ...... Let `typeIR` be `RECORD { [typeIR~f~ nameIR~f~ ;] , ... }`.
     ...... Let `expressionNoteIR` be <<expressionNoteIR, type `typeIR` and compile-time known-ness `ctk~f~`>>.
     ...... Result in the typed expression <<typedExpressionIR, `RECORD { [nameIR~f~ = typedExpressionIR~f~] , ... }` annotated with `expressionNoteIR`>>.
    ..... Else if let `name~f_h~ = expression~f_h~ , namedExpressionList~t~` be `recordElementExpression`:
     ...... Let `(name~f_t~ = expression~f_t~)^{asterisk}^` be <<flatten_namedExpressionList, the list of named expressions in `namedExpressionList~t~`>>.
     ...... Let `name~f~^{asterisk}^` be `name~f_h~ {two-colons} name~f_t~^{asterisk}^`.
     ...... Let `nameIR~f~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `nameIR~f~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
            * Let `nameIR~f~` be <<name, the name of `name~f~`>>.
--
+
for each `name~f~` in `name~f~^{asterisk}^`
     ...... Let `expression~f~^{asterisk}^` be `expression~f_h~ {two-colons} expression~f_t~^{asterisk}^`.
     ...... Let `typedExpressionIR~f~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `typedExpressionIR~f~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
            * Let `typedExpressionIR~f~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~f~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
--
+
for each `expression~f~` in `expression~f~^{asterisk}^`
     ...... Let `typeIR~f~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `typeIR~f~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
            * Let `typeIR~f~` be <<type_of_typedExpressionIR, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~f~`>>.
--
+
for each `typedExpressionIR~f~` in `typedExpressionIR~f~^{asterisk}^`
     ...... Let `ctk~f~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `ctk~f~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
            * Let `ctk~f~` be <<ctk_of_typedExpressionIR, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~f~`>>.
--
+
for each `typedExpressionIR~f~` in `typedExpressionIR~f~^{asterisk}^`
     ...... Let `typeIR` be `RECORD { (typeIR~f~ nameIR~f~ ;)^{asterisk}^ }`.
     ...... Let `ctk` be `<<joins_ctk, $joins_ctk(ctk~f~^{asterisk}^)>>`.
     ...... Let `expressionNoteIR` be <<expressionNoteIR, type `typeIR` and compile-time known-ness `ctk`>>.
     ...... Result in the typed expression <<typedExpressionIR, `RECORD { (nameIR~f~ = typedExpressionIR~f~)^{asterisk}^ }` annotated with `expressionNoteIR`>>.
    ..... Else let `name~f_h~ = expression~f_h~ , namedExpressionList~t~ , ...` be `recordElementExpression`:
     ...... Let `(name~f_t~ = expression~f_t~)^{asterisk}^` be <<flatten_namedExpressionList, the list of named expressions in `namedExpressionList~t~`>>.
     ...... Let `name~f~^{asterisk}^` be `name~f_h~ {two-colons} name~f_t~^{asterisk}^`.
     ...... Let `nameIR~f~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `nameIR~f~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
            * Let `nameIR~f~` be <<name, the name of `name~f~`>>.
--
+
for each `name~f~` in `name~f~^{asterisk}^`
     ...... Let `expression~f~^{asterisk}^` be `expression~f_h~ {two-colons} expression~f_t~^{asterisk}^`.
     ...... Let `typedExpressionIR~f~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `typedExpressionIR~f~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
            * Let `typedExpressionIR~f~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~f~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
--
+
for each `expression~f~` in `expression~f~^{asterisk}^`
     ...... Let `typeIR~f~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `typeIR~f~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
            * Let `typeIR~f~` be <<type_of_typedExpressionIR, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~f~`>>.
--
+
for each `typedExpressionIR~f~` in `typedExpressionIR~f~^{asterisk}^`
     ...... Let `ctk~f~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `ctk~f~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
            * Let `ctk~f~` be <<ctk_of_typedExpressionIR, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~f~`>>.
--
+
for each `typedExpressionIR~f~` in `typedExpressionIR~f~^{asterisk}^`
     ...... Let `typeIR` be `RECORD { (typeIR~f~ nameIR~f~ ;)^{asterisk}^ , ... }`.
     ...... Let `ctk` be `<<joins_ctk, $joins_ctk(ctk~f~^{asterisk}^)>>`.
     ...... Let `expressionNoteIR` be <<expressionNoteIR, type `typeIR` and compile-time known-ness `ctk`>>.
     ...... Result in the typed expression <<typedExpressionIR, `RECORD { (nameIR~f~ = typedExpressionIR~f~)^{asterisk}^ , ... }` annotated with `expressionNoteIR`>>.
. Else if let `ERROR . member` be `expression'''`:
 .. Group errorAccessExpression:
  ... Let `nameIR` be <<name, the name of `member`>>.
  ... Let `nameIR~error~` be `"error." {pp} nameIR`.
  ... Check that `ERROR . nameIR` is equal to `<<find_var_value_t, $find_var_value_t(p, TC, nameIR~error~)>>`.
  ... Let `expressionNoteIR` be <<expressionNoteIR, type `ERROR` and compile-time known-ness `LCTK`>>.
  ... Result in the typed expression <<typedExpressionIR, `ERROR . nameIR` annotated with `expressionNoteIR`>>.
. Else if let `memberAccessBase . member` be `expression'''`:
 .. If let `prefixedTypeName~base~` be `memberAccessBase`:
  ... Group memberAccessExpression-type:
   .... Let `prefixedNameIR~base~` be <<prefixedTypeName, the prefixed name of  `prefixedTypeName~base~`>>.
   .... Let `typeDefIR^?^` be `<<find_typeDef_t, $find_typeDef_t(p, TC, prefixedNameIR~base~)>>`.
   .... Check that `typeDefIR^?^` is Some value.
   .... Let `typeDefIR~base~` be `typeDefIR^?^`.
   .... Check that `<<is_monomorphic_typeDefIR, $is_monomorphic_typeDefIR(typeDefIR~base~)>>`.
   .... Let `typeIR~base~` be `<<type_of_typeDefIR, $type_of_typeDefIR(typeDefIR~base~)>>`.
   .... Let `typeIR` be <<canon_typeIR, the canonicalized form of `typeIR~base~`>>.
   .... Check that `typeIR` has type `enumTypeIR`.
   .... Let `enumTypeIR` be `typeIR`.
   .... If let `ENUM ++_++ { nameIR~field~^{asterisk}^ }` be `enumTypeIR`:
    ..... Let `nameIR` be <<name, the name of `member`>>.
    ..... Check that `nameIR` is in `nameIR~field~^{asterisk}^`.
    ..... Let `expressionNoteIR` be <<expressionNoteIR, type `typeIR~base~` and compile-time known-ness `LCTK`>>.
    ..... Result in the typed expression <<typedExpressionIR, `TYPE prefixedNameIR~base~ . nameIR` annotated with `expressionNoteIR`>>.
   .... Else let `ENUM ++_++ < ++_++ > { (nameIR~field~ = ++_++ ;)^{asterisk}^ }` be `enumTypeIR`:
    ..... Let `nameIR` be <<name, the name of `member`>>.
    ..... Check that `nameIR` is in `nameIR~field~^{asterisk}^`.
    ..... Let `expressionNoteIR` be <<expressionNoteIR, type `typeIR~base~` and compile-time known-ness `LCTK`>>.
    ..... Result in the typed expression <<typedExpressionIR, `TYPE prefixedNameIR~base~ . nameIR` annotated with `expressionNoteIR`>>.
 .. Else let `expression~base~` be `memberAccessBase`:
  ... Group memberAccessExpression-expression:
   .... If `"size"` is equal to <<name, the name of `member`>>:
    ..... Let `typedExpressionIR~base~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~base~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
    ..... Let `typeIR~base~` be <<type_of_typedExpressionIR, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~base~`>>.
    ..... Let `typeIR'` be <<canon_typeIR, the canonicalized form of `typeIR~base~`>>.
    ..... Check that `typeIR'` has type `headerStackTypeIR`.
    ..... Let `typeIR [ n~size~ ]` be `typeIR'`.
    ..... Let `expressionNoteIR` be <<expressionNoteIR, type `BIT < 32 >` and compile-time known-ness `LCTK`>>.
    ..... Result in the typed expression <<typedExpressionIR, `typedExpressionIR~base~ . "size"` annotated with `expressionNoteIR`>>.
   .... Else if `"lastIndex"` is equal to <<name, the name of `member`>>:
    ..... If `p = BLOCK` *and* `<<is_parser_blockKind, $is_parser_blockKind(TC.BLOCK.KIND)>>`:
