. Else if let `expression~base~ [ expression~index~ ]` be `expression'''`:
 .. Group indexAccessExpression:
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~base~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~base~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~index~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~index~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `typeIR~base~` be <<type_of_typedExpressionIR, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~base~`>>.
  ... Let `ctk~base~` be <<ctk_of_typedExpressionIR, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~base~`>>.
  ... Let `typeIR~index~` be <<type_of_typedExpressionIR, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~index~`>>.
  ... Let `ctk~index~` be <<ctk_of_typedExpressionIR, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~index~`>>.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR^?^` be `<<reduce_serenum_unary, $reduce_serenum_unary(typedExpressionIR~index~, $compat_array_index)>>`.
  ... Check that `typedExpressionIR^?^` is Some value.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~index_reduced~` be `typedExpressionIR^?^`.
  ... Let `typeIR'` be <<canon_typeIR, the canonicalized form of `typeIR~base~`>>.
  ... If let `TUPLE < typeIR~e~^{asterisk}^ >` be `typeIR'`:
   .... Check that `ctk~index~` matches pattern `LCTK`.
   .... Let `value~index~` be the result of <<Expr_eval_lctk, the local compile-time evaluation of `typedExpressionIR~index_reduced~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Let `int` be <<int_of_value, the integer representation of  `value~index~`>>.
   .... Check that `int` has type `nat`.
   .... Let `n~index~` be `int`.
   .... Check that `n~index~` is less than the length of `typeIR~e~^{asterisk}^`.
   .... Let `expressionNoteIR` be <<expressionNoteIR, type `typeIR~e~^{asterisk}^[n~index~]` and compile-time known-ness `DYN`>>.
