  ... Let `typedExpressionIR'^?^` be `<<reduce_serenum_unary, $reduce_serenum_unary(typedExpressionIR~hi~, $compat_bitslice_index)>>`.
  ... Check that `typedExpressionIR'^?^` is Some value.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~hi_reduced~` be `typedExpressionIR'^?^`.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR''^?^` be `<<reduce_serenum_unary, $reduce_serenum_unary(typedExpressionIR~lo~, $compat_bitslice_index)>>`.
  ... Check that `typedExpressionIR''^?^` is Some value.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~lo_reduced~` be `typedExpressionIR''^?^`.
  ... Let `typeIR~hi_reduced~` be <<type_of_typedExpressionIR, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~hi_reduced~`>>.
  ... Let `ctk~hi_reduced~` be <<ctk_of_typedExpressionIR, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~hi_reduced~`>>.
  ... Let `typeIR~lo_reduced~` be <<type_of_typedExpressionIR, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~lo_reduced~`>>.
  ... Let `ctk~lo_reduced~` be <<ctk_of_typedExpressionIR, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~lo_reduced~`>>.
  ... Check that `ctk~hi_reduced~` matches pattern `LCTK`.
  ... Let `value~hi~` be the result of <<Expr_eval_lctk, the local compile-time evaluation of `typedExpressionIR~hi_reduced~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `int` be <<int_of_value, the integer representation of  `value~hi~`>>.
  ... Check that `int` has type `nat`.
  ... Let `n~hi~` be `int`.
  ... Check that `ctk~lo_reduced~` matches pattern `LCTK`.
  ... Let `value~lo~` be the result of <<Expr_eval_lctk, the local compile-time evaluation of `typedExpressionIR~lo_reduced~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `int'` be <<int_of_value, the integer representation of  `value~lo~`>>.
  ... Check that `int'` has type `nat`.
  ... Let `n~lo~` be `int'`.
  ... Check that `<<is_valid_bitslice, $is_valid_bitslice(typeIR~base_reduced~, n~lo~, n~hi~)>>`.
  ... Let `int''` be `n~hi~ - n~lo~ + 1`.
  ... Check that `int''` has type `nat`.
  ... Let `n~slice~` be `int''`.
  ... Let `typeIR` be `BIT < n~slice~ >`.
  ... Let `expressionNoteIR` be <<expressionNoteIR, type `typeIR` and compile-time known-ness `ctk~base_reduced~`>>.
  ... Result in the typed expression <<typedExpressionIR, `typedExpressionIR~base~ [ typedExpressionIR~hi_reduced~ : typedExpressionIR~lo_reduced~ ]` annotated with `expressionNoteIR`>>.
. Else if let `callExpression` be `expression'''`:
 .. Group callExpression-callable:
  ... If let `callTarget ( argumentList )` be `callExpression`:
   .... Check that `callTarget` has type `callableTarget`.
   .... Let `callableTarget` be `callTarget`.
   .... Let `callableTargetIR` be the result of <<CallableTarget_ok, typing `callableTarget`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Let `argument^{asterisk}^` be <<flatten_argumentList, the list of arguments in `argumentList`>>.
   .... Let `argumentIR^{asterisk}^` be the list of `argumentIR`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
        * Let `argumentIR` be the result of <<Argument_ok, typing `argument`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
--
+
for each `argument` in `argument^{asterisk}^`
   .... Let <<CallableType_ok, `p TC |- callableTargetIR < [ ] > ( argumentIR^{asterisk}^ ) : callableTypeIR < # tid~inserted~^{asterisk}^ > ( # id~default~^{asterisk}^ )`>>.
   .... Let `tid~infer~^{asterisk}^` be `tid~inserted~^{asterisk}^`.
   .... Let <<Call_ok, `p TC |- callableTypeIR < [ ] # tid~infer~^{asterisk}^ > ( argumentIR^{asterisk}^ # id~default~^{asterisk}^ ) : typeIR~ret~ < typeArgumentIR~inferred~^{asterisk}^ > ( argumentIR~cast~^{asterisk}^ )`>>.
   .... Check that `typeIR~ret~` is not equal to `VOID`.
   .... Let `ctk` be `<<is_static_callableTarget, $is_static_callableTarget(callableTargetIR)>>`.
   .... Let `callExpressionIR` be `callableTargetIR < typeArgumentIR~inferred~^{asterisk}^ > ( argumentIR~cast~^{asterisk}^ )`.
   .... Let `expressionNoteIR` be <<expressionNoteIR, type `typeIR~ret~` and compile-time known-ness `ctk`>>.
   .... Result in the typed expression <<typedExpressionIR, `callExpressionIR` annotated with `expressionNoteIR`>>.
  ... Else let `callableTarget < realTypeArgumentList > ( argumentList )` be `callExpression`:
   .... Let `callableTargetIR` be the result of <<CallableTarget_ok, typing `callableTarget`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Let `realTypeArgument^{asterisk}^` be <<flatten_realTypeArgumentList, the list of real type arguments in `realTypeArgumentList`>>.
   .... Let `typeArgumentIR^{asterisk}^` and `tid~impl~^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<TypeArguments_ok, typing `realTypeArgument^{asterisk}^`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Let `argument^{asterisk}^` be <<flatten_argumentList, the list of arguments in `argumentList`>>.
   .... Let `argumentIR^{asterisk}^` be the list of `argumentIR`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
        * Let `argumentIR` be the result of <<Argument_ok, typing `argument`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
--
+
for each `argument` in `argument^{asterisk}^`
   .... Let <<CallableType_ok, `p TC |- callableTargetIR < typeArgumentIR^{asterisk}^ > ( argumentIR^{asterisk}^ ) : callableTypeIR < # tid~inserted~^{asterisk}^ > ( # id~default~^{asterisk}^ )`>>.
   .... Let `tid~infer~^{asterisk}^` be `tid~impl~^{asterisk}^ {pp} tid~inserted~^{asterisk}^`.
   .... Let <<Call_ok, `p TC |- callableTypeIR < typeArgumentIR^{asterisk}^ # tid~infer~^{asterisk}^ > ( argumentIR^{asterisk}^ # id~default~^{asterisk}^ ) : typeIR~ret~ < typeArgumentIR~inferred~^{asterisk}^ > ( argumentIR~cast~^{asterisk}^ )`>>.
   .... Check that `typeIR~ret~` is not equal to `VOID`.
   .... Let `ctk` be `<<is_static_callableTarget, $is_static_callableTarget(callableTargetIR)>>`.
   .... Let `callExpressionIR` be `callableTargetIR < typeArgumentIR~inferred~^{asterisk}^ > ( argumentIR~cast~^{asterisk}^ )`.
   .... Let `expressionNoteIR` be <<expressionNoteIR, type `typeIR~ret~` and compile-time known-ness `ctk`>>.
   .... Result in the typed expression <<typedExpressionIR, `callExpressionIR` annotated with `expressionNoteIR`>>.
 .. Check that `callExpression` matches pattern `% ( % )`.
 .. Let `callTarget ( argumentList )` be `callExpression`.
 .. Group callExpression-constructor:
  ... If let `prefixedTypeName` be `callTarget`:
   .... Let `argument^{asterisk}^` be <<flatten_argumentList, the list of arguments in `argumentList`>>.
   .... Let `argumentIR^{asterisk}^` be the list of `argumentIR`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
        * Let `argumentIR` be the result of <<Argument_ok, typing `argument`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
--
+
for each `argument` in `argument^{asterisk}^`
   .... Let `prefixedNameIR` be <<prefixedTypeName, the prefixed name of  `prefixedTypeName`>>.
   .... Let <<ConstructorType_ok, `p TC |- prefixedNameIR < [ ] > ( argumentIR^{asterisk}^ ) : constructorTypeIR < # tid~impl~^{asterisk}^ > ( # id~default~^{asterisk}^ )`>>.
   .... Let <<Inst_ok, `p TC ANON |- constructorTypeIR < [ ] # tid~impl~^{asterisk}^ > ( argumentIR^{asterisk}^ # id~default~^{asterisk}^ ) : typeIR~object~ < typeArgumentIR~inferred~^{asterisk}^ > ( argumentIR~cast~^{asterisk}^ )`>>.
   .... Check that `<<is_concrete_extern_object, $is_concrete_extern_object(typeIR~object~)>>`.
   .... Let `callExpressionIR` be `prefixedNameIR < typeArgumentIR~inferred~^{asterisk}^ > ( argumentIR~cast~^{asterisk}^ )`.
   .... Let `expressionNoteIR` be <<expressionNoteIR, type `typeIR~object~` and compile-time known-ness `CTK`>>.
   .... Result in the typed expression <<typedExpressionIR, `callExpressionIR` annotated with `expressionNoteIR`>>.
  ... Else if let `prefixedTypeName < typeArgumentList >` be `callTarget`:
   .... Let `typeArgument^{asterisk}^` be <<flatten_typeArgumentList, the list of type arguments in `typeArgumentList`>>.
   .... Let `typeArgumentIR^{asterisk}^` and `tid~impl~^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<TypeArguments_ok, typing `typeArgument^{asterisk}^`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Let `argument^{asterisk}^` be <<flatten_argumentList, the list of arguments in `argumentList`>>.
   .... Let `argumentIR^{asterisk}^` be the list of `argumentIR`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
        * Let `argumentIR` be the result of <<Argument_ok, typing `argument`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
--
+
for each `argument` in `argument^{asterisk}^`
   .... Let `prefixedNameIR` be <<prefixedTypeName, the prefixed name of  `prefixedTypeName`>>.
   .... Let <<ConstructorType_ok, `p TC |- prefixedNameIR < typeArgumentIR^{asterisk}^ > ( argumentIR^{asterisk}^ ) : constructorTypeIR < # tid~inserted~^{asterisk}^ > ( # id~default~^{asterisk}^ )`>>.
   .... Let `tid~infer~^{asterisk}^` be `tid~impl~^{asterisk}^ {pp} tid~inserted~^{asterisk}^`.
   .... Let <<Inst_ok, `p TC ANON |- constructorTypeIR < typeArgumentIR^{asterisk}^ # tid~infer~^{asterisk}^ > ( argumentIR^{asterisk}^ # id~default~^{asterisk}^ ) : typeIR~object~ < typeArgumentIR~inferred~^{asterisk}^ > ( argumentIR~cast~^{asterisk}^ )`>>.
   .... Check that `<<is_concrete_extern_object, $is_concrete_extern_object(typeIR~object~)>>`.
   .... Let `callExpressionIR` be `prefixedNameIR < typeArgumentIR~inferred~^{asterisk}^ > ( argumentIR~cast~^{asterisk}^ )`.
   .... Let `expressionNoteIR` be <<expressionNoteIR, type `typeIR~object~` and compile-time known-ness `CTK`>>.
   .... Result in the typed expression <<typedExpressionIR, `callExpressionIR` annotated with `expressionNoteIR`>>.
. Else if let `( expression )` be `expression'''`:
 .. Group parenthesizedExpression:
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `typeIR` be <<type_of_typedExpressionIR, the type of  `typedExpressionIR`>>.
  ... Let `ctk` be <<ctk_of_typedExpressionIR, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR`>>.
  ... Let `expressionNoteIR` be <<expressionNoteIR, type `typeIR` and compile-time known-ness `ctk`>>.
  ... Result in the typed expression <<typedExpressionIR, `( typedExpressionIR )` annotated with `expressionNoteIR`>>.


relation Argument_ok: `p`, `TC`, and `argument`


. Check that `argument` has type `expression`.
. Let `expression` be `argument`.
. Group expression:
 .. Let `typedExpressionIR` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
 .. Result in the typed argument `typedExpressionIR`.
. If let `name = expression` be `argument`:
 .. Group name-expression:
  ... Let `nameIR` be <<name, the name of `name`>>.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Result in the typed argument `nameIR = typedExpressionIR`.
. Else if let `name = _` be `argument`:
 .. Group name-dontcare:
  ... Let `nameIR` be <<name, the name of `name`>>.
  ... Result in the typed argument `nameIR = _`.
. Else if `argument` matches pattern `_`:
 .. Group dontcare:
  ... Result in the typed argument `_`.


relation Lvalue_ok: `p`, `TC`, and `lvalue`


. Check that `lvalue` has type `prefixedNonTypeName`.
. Let `prefixedNonTypeName` be `lvalue`.
. Group referenceExpression-prefixedNonTypeName:
 .. Let `prefixedNameIR` be <<prefixedNonTypeName, the prefixed name of  `prefixedNonTypeName`>>.
 .. Let `varTypeIR^?^` be `<<find_var_t, $find_var_t(p, TC, prefixedNameIR)>>`.
 .. Check that `varTypeIR^?^` is Some value.
 .. Let `direction typeIR ctk value^?^` be `varTypeIR^?^`.
 .. Check that `ctk` matches pattern `DYN`.
 .. Check that `value^?^` is None.
 .. If `direction` matches pattern `OUT`:
  ... Result in the typed lvalue <<typedLvalueIR, `prefixedNameIR` with note `( typeIR )`>>.
 .. Else if `direction` matches pattern `INOUT`:
  ... Result in the typed lvalue <<typedLvalueIR, `prefixedNameIR` with note `( typeIR )`>>.
. If let `lvalue~base~ . member` be `lvalue`:
 .. Group memberAccess:
  ... Let `typedLvalueIR~base~` be the result of <<Lvalue_ok, typing `lvalue~base~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `( typeIR~base~ )` be the note of `typedLvalueIR~base~`.
  ... Let `typeIR'` be <<canon_typeIR, the canonicalized form of `typeIR~base~`>>.
  ... If let `typeIR [ ++_++ ]` be `typeIR'`:
   .... Let `nameIR` be <<name, the name of `member`>>.
   .... If `nameIR` is equal to `"next"`:
    ..... If `p = BLOCK` *and* `<<is_parser_blockKind, $is_parser_blockKind(TC.BLOCK.KIND)>>`:
     ...... Let `typedLvalueIR` be <<typedLvalueIR, `typedLvalueIR~base~ . nameIR` with note `( typeIR )`>>.
     ...... Result in the typed lvalue `typedLvalueIR`.
    ..... Else if `p = LOCAL` *and* `<<is_parser_state_localKind, $is_parser_state_localKind(TC.LOCAL.KIND)>>`:
     ...... Let `typedLvalueIR` be <<typedLvalueIR, `typedLvalueIR~base~ . nameIR` with note `( typeIR )`>>.
     ...... Result in the typed lvalue `typedLvalueIR`.
   .... Else if `nameIR` is equal to `"last"`:
    ..... If `p = BLOCK` *and* `<<is_parser_blockKind, $is_parser_blockKind(TC.BLOCK.KIND)>>`:
     ...... Let `typedLvalueIR` be <<typedLvalueIR, `typedLvalueIR~base~ . nameIR` with note `( typeIR )`>>.
     ...... Result in the typed lvalue `typedLvalueIR`.
    ..... Else if `p = LOCAL` *and* `<<is_parser_state_localKind, $is_parser_state_localKind(TC.LOCAL.KIND)>>`:
     ...... Let `typedLvalueIR` be <<typedLvalueIR, `typedLvalueIR~base~ . nameIR` with note `( typeIR )`>>.
     ...... Result in the typed lvalue `typedLvalueIR`.
  ... Else if let `STRUCT ++_++ { (typeIR~field~ nameIR~field~ ;)^{asterisk}^ }` be `typeIR'`:
   .... Let `nameIR` be <<name, the name of `member`>>.
   .... Let `typeIR''^?^` be `<<assoc_, $assoc_<nameIR, typeIR>(nameIR, ((nameIR~field~, typeIR~field~))^{asterisk}^)>>`.
   .... Check that `typeIR''^?^` is Some value.
   .... Let `typeIR` be `typeIR''^?^`.
   .... Let `typedLvalueIR` be <<typedLvalueIR, `typedLvalueIR~base~ . nameIR` with note `( typeIR )`>>.
   .... Result in the typed lvalue `typedLvalueIR`.
  ... Else if let `HEADER ++_++ { (typeIR~field~ nameIR~field~ ;)^{asterisk}^ }` be `typeIR'`:
   .... Let `nameIR` be <<name, the name of `member`>>.
   .... Let `typeIR''^?^` be `<<assoc_, $assoc_<nameIR, typeIR>(nameIR, ((nameIR~field~, typeIR~field~))^{asterisk}^)>>`.
   .... Check that `typeIR''^?^` is Some value.
   .... Let `typeIR` be `typeIR''^?^`.
   .... Let `typedLvalueIR` be <<typedLvalueIR, `typedLvalueIR~base~ . nameIR` with note `( typeIR )`>>.
   .... Result in the typed lvalue `typedLvalueIR`.
  ... Else if let `HEADER_UNION ++_++ { (typeIR~field~ nameIR~field~ ;)^{asterisk}^ }` be `typeIR'`:
   .... Let `nameIR` be <<name, the name of `member`>>.
   .... Let `typeIR''^?^` be `<<assoc_, $assoc_<nameIR, typeIR>(nameIR, ((nameIR~field~, typeIR~field~))^{asterisk}^)>>`.
   .... Check that `typeIR''^?^` is Some value.
   .... Let `typeIR` be `typeIR''^?^`.
   .... Let `typedLvalueIR` be <<typedLvalueIR, `typedLvalueIR~base~ . nameIR` with note `( typeIR )`>>.
   .... Result in the typed lvalue `typedLvalueIR`.
. Else if let `lvalue~base~ [ expression~index~ ]` be `lvalue`:
 .. Group indexAccess:
  ... Let `typedLvalueIR~base~` be the result of <<Lvalue_ok, typing `lvalue~base~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `( typeIR~base~ )` be the note of `typedLvalueIR~base~`.
  ... Let `typeIR'` be <<canon_typeIR, the canonicalized form of `typeIR~base~`>>.
  ... Check that `typeIR'` has type `headerStackTypeIR`.
  ... Let `typeIR [ n~size~ ]` be `typeIR'`.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~index~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~index~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let <<expressionNoteIR, type `typeIR~index~` and compile-time known-ness `ctk~index~`>> be the note of `typedExpressionIR~index~`.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR^?^` be `<<reduce_serenum_unary, $reduce_serenum_unary(typedExpressionIR~index~, $compat_array_index)>>`.
  ... Check that `typedExpressionIR^?^` is Some value.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~index_reduced~` be `typedExpressionIR^?^`.
  ... If `ctk~index~` matches pattern `LCTK`:
   .... Let `value~index~` be the result of <<Expr_eval_lctk, the local compile-time evaluation of `typedExpressionIR~index_reduced~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Let `int` be <<int_of_value, the integer representation of  `value~index~`>>.
   .... Check that `int` has type `nat`.
   .... Let `n~index~` be `int`.
   .... Check that `n~index~` is less than `n~size~`.
   .... Let `typedLvalueIR` be <<typedLvalueIR, `typedLvalueIR~base~ [ typedExpressionIR~index_reduced~ ]` with note `( typeIR )`>>.
   .... Result in the typed lvalue `typedLvalueIR`.
  ... Else `ctk~index~` does not match pattern `LCTK`:
   .... Let `typedLvalueIR` be <<typedLvalueIR, `typedLvalueIR~base~ [ typedExpressionIR~index_reduced~ ]` with note `( typeIR )`>>.
   .... Result in the typed lvalue `typedLvalueIR`.
. Else if let `lvalue~base~ [ expression~hi~ : expression~lo~ ]` be `lvalue`:
 .. Group sliceAccess:
  ... Let `typedLvalueIR~base~` be the result of <<Lvalue_ok, typing `lvalue~base~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `( typeIR~base~ )` be the note of `typedLvalueIR~base~`.
  ... Check that `<<compat_bitslice_base, $compat_bitslice_base(typeIR~base~)>>`.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~hi~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~hi~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~lo~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~lo~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR^?^` be `<<reduce_serenum_unary, $reduce_serenum_unary(typedExpressionIR~hi~, $compat_bitslice_index)>>`.
  ... Check that `typedExpressionIR^?^` is Some value.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~hi_reduced~` be `typedExpressionIR^?^`.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR'^?^` be `<<reduce_serenum_unary, $reduce_serenum_unary(typedExpressionIR~lo~, $compat_bitslice_index)>>`.
  ... Check that `typedExpressionIR'^?^` is Some value.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~lo_reduced~` be `typedExpressionIR'^?^`.
  ... Let <<expressionNoteIR, type `typeIR~hi_reduced~` and compile-time known-ness `ctk~hi_reduced~`>> be the note of `typedExpressionIR~hi_reduced~`.
  ... Let <<expressionNoteIR, type `typeIR~lo_reduced~` and compile-time known-ness `ctk~lo_reduced~`>> be the note of `typedExpressionIR~lo_reduced~`.
  ... Check that `ctk~hi_reduced~` matches pattern `LCTK`.
  ... Let `value~hi~` be the result of <<Expr_eval_lctk, the local compile-time evaluation of `typedExpressionIR~hi_reduced~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `int` be <<int_of_value, the integer representation of  `value~hi~`>>.
  ... Check that `int` has type `nat`.
  ... Let `n~hi~` be `int`.
  ... Check that `ctk~lo_reduced~` matches pattern `LCTK`.
  ... Let `value~lo~` be the result of <<Expr_eval_lctk, the local compile-time evaluation of `typedExpressionIR~lo_reduced~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `int'` be <<int_of_value, the integer representation of  `value~lo~`>>.
  ... Check that `int'` has type `nat`.
  ... Let `n~lo~` be `int'`.
  ... Check that `<<is_valid_bitslice, $is_valid_bitslice(typeIR~base~, n~lo~, n~hi~)>>`.
  ... Let `int''` be `n~hi~ - n~lo~ + 1`.
  ... Check that `int''` has type `nat`.
  ... Let `n~slice~` be `int''`.
  ... Let `typeIR` be `BIT < n~slice~ >`.
  ... Let `typedLvalueIR` be <<typedLvalueIR, `typedLvalueIR~base~ [ typedExpressionIR~hi_reduced~ : typedExpressionIR~lo_reduced~ ]` with note `( typeIR )`>>.
  ... Result in the typed lvalue `typedLvalueIR`.
. Else if let `( lvalue~base~ )` be `lvalue`:
 .. Group parenthesized:
  ... Let `typedLvalueIR~base~` be the result of <<Lvalue_ok, typing `lvalue~base~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `( typeIR~base~ )` be the note of `typedLvalueIR~base~`.
  ... Let `typedLvalueIR` be <<typedLvalueIR, `( typedLvalueIR~base~ )` with note `( typeIR~base~ )`>>.
  ... Result in the typed lvalue `typedLvalueIR`.


relation Stmt_ok: `p'`, `TC'`, `f'`, and `statement`


. If let `emptyStatement` be `statement`:
 .. Group emptyStatement:
  ... Result in 
* the typing context `TC'`,
* the abstract control flow `f'`,
* and the typed statement `;`.
. Else if let `lvalue assignop expression ;` be `statement`:
 .. Check that `assignop` matches pattern `=`.
 .. Group assignmentStatement-eq:
  ... Let `typedLvalueIR` be the result of <<Lvalue_ok, typing `lvalue`, under cursor `p'` and typing context `TC'`>>.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression`, under cursor `p'` and typing context `TC'`>>.
  ... Let `typeIR~l~` be <<type_of_typedLvalueIR, the type of lvalue  `typedLvalueIR`>>.
  ... Let `typeIR~r~` be <<type_of_typedExpressionIR, the type of  `typedExpressionIR`>>.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR'^?^` be <<coerce_unary, implicitly cast  `typedExpressionIR`  to  `typeIR~l~`>>.
  ... Check that `typedExpressionIR'^?^` is Some value.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~cast~` be `typedExpressionIR'^?^`.
  ... Result in 
* the typing context `TC'`,
* the abstract control flow `f'`,
* and the typed statement `typedLvalueIR = typedExpressionIR~cast~ ;`.
. Else if let `callStatement` be `statement`:
 .. Group callStatement:
  ... If let `lvalue~callable~ ( argumentList ) ;` be `callStatement`:
   .... Let `callableTargetIR` be the result of <<CallableTarget_lvalue_ok, typing `lvalue~callable~`, under cursor `p'` and typing context `TC'`>>.
   .... Let `argument^{asterisk}^` be <<flatten_argumentList, the list of arguments in `argumentList`>>.
   .... Let `argumentIR^{asterisk}^` be the list of `argumentIR`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
        * Let `argumentIR` be the result of <<Argument_ok, typing `argument`, under cursor `p'` and typing context `TC'`>>.
--
+
for each `argument` in `argument^{asterisk}^`
   .... Let <<CallableType_ok, `p' TC' |- callableTargetIR < [ ] > ( argumentIR^{asterisk}^ ) : callableTypeIR < # tid~impl~^{asterisk}^ > ( # id~default~^{asterisk}^ )`>>.
   .... Let <<Call_ok, `p' TC' |- callableTypeIR < [ ] # tid~impl~^{asterisk}^ > ( argumentIR^{asterisk}^ # id~default~^{asterisk}^ ) : typeIR~ret~ < typeArgumentIR~inferred~^{asterisk}^ > ( argumentIR~cast~^{asterisk}^ )`>>.
   .... Let `callStatementIR` be `callableTargetIR < typeArgumentIR~inferred~^{asterisk}^ > ( argumentIR~cast~^{asterisk}^ ) ;`.
   .... Result in 
* the typing context `TC'`,
* the abstract control flow `f'`,
* and the typed statement `callStatementIR`.
  ... Else let `lvalue~callable~ < typeArgumentList > ( argumentList ) ;` be `callStatement`:
   .... Let `callableTargetIR` be the result of <<CallableTarget_lvalue_ok, typing `lvalue~callable~`, under cursor `p'` and typing context `TC'`>>.
   .... Let `typeArgument^{asterisk}^` be <<flatten_typeArgumentList, the list of type arguments in `typeArgumentList`>>.
   .... Let `typeArgumentIR^{asterisk}^` and `tid~impl~^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<TypeArguments_ok, typing `typeArgument^{asterisk}^`, under cursor `p'` and typing context `TC'`>>.
   .... Let `argument^{asterisk}^` be <<flatten_argumentList, the list of arguments in `argumentList`>>.
   .... Let `argumentIR^{asterisk}^` be the list of `argumentIR`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
        * Let `argumentIR` be the result of <<Argument_ok, typing `argument`, under cursor `p'` and typing context `TC'`>>.
--
+
for each `argument` in `argument^{asterisk}^`
   .... Let <<CallableType_ok, `p' TC' |- callableTargetIR < typeArgumentIR^{asterisk}^ > ( argumentIR^{asterisk}^ ) : callableTypeIR < # tid~inserted~^{asterisk}^ > ( # id~default~^{asterisk}^ )`>>.
   .... Let `tid~infer~^{asterisk}^` be `tid~impl~^{asterisk}^ {pp} tid~inserted~^{asterisk}^`.
   .... Let <<Call_ok, `p' TC' |- callableTypeIR < [ ] # tid~infer~^{asterisk}^ > ( argumentIR^{asterisk}^ # id~default~^{asterisk}^ ) : typeIR~ret~ < typeArgumentIR~inferred~^{asterisk}^ > ( argumentIR~cast~^{asterisk}^ )`>>.
   .... Let `callStatementIR` be `callableTargetIR < typeArgumentIR~inferred~^{asterisk}^ > ( argumentIR~cast~^{asterisk}^ ) ;`.
   .... Result in 
* the typing context `TC'`,
* the abstract control flow `f'`,
* and the typed statement `callStatementIR`.
. Else if let `namedType . APPLY ( argumentList ) ;` be `statement`:
 .. Group directApplicationStatement:
  ... Let <<typedExpressionIR, `expressionIR` annotated with type `typeIR~object~` and compile-time known-ness `++_++`>> be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `namedType ( )`, under cursor `p'` and typing context `TC'`>>.
  ... Check that `expressionIR` has type `callExpressionIR`.
  ... Let `callExpressionIR` be `expressionIR`.
  ... Check that `callExpressionIR` matches pattern `% ( % )`.
  ... Let `prefixedNameIR < typeArgumentIR^{asterisk}^ > ( argumentIR^{asterisk}^ )` be `callExpressionIR`.
  ... Check that `typeArgumentIR^{asterisk}^` is an empty list.
  ... Check that `argumentIR^{asterisk}^` is an empty list.
  ... Check that `<<compat_direct_application, $compat_direct_application(typeIR~object~)>>`.
  ... Let `nameIR~object~` be `"__direct_application"`.
  ... Let `TC~1~` be <<add_var_t, the typing context `TC'` with a mapping from `nameIR~object~` to `typeIR~object~ CTK None` added to the `p'` layer>>.
  ... Let `lvalue` be `nameIR~object~ . "apply"`.
  ... Let `++_++`, `++_++`, and `statementIR` be the result of <<Stmt_ok, typing `lvalue ( argumentList ) ;`, under cursor `p'`, typing context `TC~1~`, and abstract control flow `f'`>>.
  ... Check that `statementIR` has type `callStatementIR`.
  ... Let `callStatementIR` be `statementIR`.
  ... Let `callableTargetIR < typeArgumentIR'^{asterisk}^ > ( argumentIR~cast~^{asterisk}^ ) ;` be `callStatementIR`.
  ... Check that `callableTargetIR` is equal to `nameIR~object~ # ( typeIR~object~ CTK ) . "apply"`.
  ... Check that `typeArgumentIR'^{asterisk}^` is an empty list.
  ... Let `directApplicationStatementIR` be `prefixedNameIR . APPLY ( argumentIR~cast~^{asterisk}^ ) ;`.
  ... Result in 
* the typing context `TC'`,
* the abstract control flow `f'`,
* and the typed statement `directApplicationStatementIR`.
. Else if let `exitStatement` be `statement`:
 .. Group exitStatement:
  ... Result in 
* the typing context `TC'`,
* the abstract control flow `f'`,
* and the typed statement `EXIT ;`.
. Else if let `conditionalStatement` be `statement`:
 .. Group conditionalStatement:
  ... If let `IF ( expression~cond~ ) statement~then~` be `conditionalStatement`:
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR~cond~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~cond~`, under cursor `p'` and typing context `TC'`>>.
   .... Let `typeIR~cond~` be <<type_of_typedExpressionIR, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~cond~`>>.
   .... Check that `BOOL` is equal to <<canon_typeIR, the canonicalized form of `typeIR~cond~`>>.
   .... Let `TC~then~`, `f~then~`, and `statementIR~then~` be the result of <<Stmt_ok, typing `statement~then~`, under cursor `p'`, typing context `TC'`, and abstract control flow `f'`>>.
   .... Result in 
* the typing context `TC'`,
* the abstract control flow `f'`,
* and the typed statement `IF ( typedExpressionIR~cond~ ) statementIR~then~`.
  ... Else let `IF ( expression~cond~ ) statement~then~ ELSE statement~else~` be `conditionalStatement`:
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR~cond~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~cond~`, under cursor `p'` and typing context `TC'`>>.
   .... Let `typeIR~cond~` be <<type_of_typedExpressionIR, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~cond~`>>.
   .... Check that `BOOL` is equal to <<canon_typeIR, the canonicalized form of `typeIR~cond~`>>.
   .... Let `TC~then~`, `f~then~`, and `statementIR~then~` be the result of <<Stmt_ok, typing `statement~then~`, under cursor `p'`, typing context `TC'`, and abstract control flow `f'`>>.
   .... Let `TC~else~`, `f~else~`, and `statementIR~else~` be the result of <<Stmt_ok, typing `statement~else~`, under cursor `p'`, typing context `TC'`, and abstract control flow `f'`>>.
   .... Let `f~post~` be <<join_flow, the merged control flow of `f~then~` and `f~else~`>>.
   .... Result in 
* the typing context `TC'`,
* the abstract control flow `f~post~`,
* and the typed statement `IF ( typedExpressionIR~cond~ ) statementIR~then~ ELSE statementIR~else~`.
. Check that `p'` matches pattern `LOCAL`.
. If let `returnStatement` be `statement`:
 .. Group returnStatement:
  ... If `returnStatement` matches pattern `RETURN ;`:
   .... Check that `VOID` is equal to `<<find_local_return_type_t, $find_local_return_type_t(TC')>>`.
   .... Result in 
* the typing context `TC'`,
* the abstract control flow `RET`,
* and the typed statement `RETURN ;`.
  ... Else let `RETURN expression ;` be `returnStatement`:
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC'`>>.
   .... Let `typeIR` be <<type_of_typedExpressionIR, the type of  `typedExpressionIR`>>.
   .... Let `typeIR'^?^` be `<<find_local_return_type_t, $find_local_return_type_t(TC')>>`.
   .... Check that `typeIR'^?^` is Some value.
   .... Let `typeIR~ret~` be `typeIR'^?^`.
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR'^?^` be <<coerce_unary, implicitly cast  `typedExpressionIR`  to  `typeIR~ret~`>>.
   .... Check that `typedExpressionIR'^?^` is Some value.
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR~cast~` be `typedExpressionIR'^?^`.
   .... Result in 
* the typing context `TC'`,
* the abstract control flow `RET`,
* and the typed statement `RETURN typedExpressionIR~cast~ ;`.
. Else if let `blockStatement` be `statement`:
 .. Group blockStatement:
  ... Let `TC~1~` be `<<enter_t, $enter_t(TC')>>`.
  ... Let `TC~2~`, `f~1~`, and `blockStatementIR` be the result of <<Block_ok, typing `blockStatement`, under typing context `TC~1~` and abstract control flow `f'`>>.
  ... Let `TC~3~` be `<<exit_t, $exit_t(TC~2~)>>`.
  ... Result in 
* the typing context `TC~3~`,
* the abstract control flow `f~1~`,
* and the typed statement `blockStatementIR`.
. Else if let `SWITCH ( expression~switch~ ) { switchCaseList }` be `statement`:
 .. Group switchStatement-table:
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~switch~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~switch~`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC'`>>.
  ... Let `typeIR~switch~` be <<type_of_typedExpressionIR, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~switch~`>>.
  ... Let `typeIR` be <<canon_typeIR, the canonicalized form of `typeIR~switch~`>>.
  ... Check that `typeIR` has type `tableMetadataEnumTypeIR`.
  ... Let `TABLE_ENUM tid~table_enum~ { ++_++^{asterisk}^ }` be `typeIR`.
  ... Let `text` be <<strip_suffix, the text `tid~table_enum~` with the suffix `")"` removed>>.
  ... Let `tid~table~` be <<strip_prefix, the text `text` with the prefix `"action_list("` removed>>.
  ... Let `switchCase^{asterisk}^` be <<flatten_switchCaseList, the list of switch cases in `switchCaseList`>>.
  ... Let <<SwitchCases_table_ok, `TC' f' tid~table~ |- switchCase^{asterisk}^ : f~post~ switchCaseIR^{asterisk}^ # switchLabel^{asterisk}^`>>.
  ... Check that <<distinct_, the elements of `switchLabel^{asterisk}^` are distinct>>.
  ... Let `switchStatementIR` be `SWITCH ( typedExpressionIR~switch~ ) { switchCaseIR^{asterisk}^ }`.
  ... Result in 
* the typing context `TC'`,
* the abstract control flow `f~post~`,
* and the typed statement `switchStatementIR`.
 .. Group switchStatement-general:
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~switch~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~switch~`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC'`>>.
  ... Let `typeIR~switch~` be <<type_of_typedExpressionIR, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~switch~`>>.
  ... Check that `<<compat_switch, $compat_switch(typeIR~switch~)>>`.
  ... Let `switchCase^{asterisk}^` be <<flatten_switchCaseList, the list of switch cases in `switchCaseList`>>.
  ... Let <<SwitchCases_general_ok, `TC' f' typeIR~switch~ |- switchCase^{asterisk}^ : f~post~ switchCaseIR^{asterisk}^ # switchLabel^{asterisk}^`>>.
  ... Check that <<distinct_, the elements of `switchLabel^{asterisk}^` are distinct>>.
  ... Let `switchStatementIR` be `SWITCH ( typedExpressionIR~switch~ ) { switchCaseIR^{asterisk}^ }`.
  ... Result in 
* the typing context `TC'`,
* the abstract control flow `f~post~`,
* and the typed statement `switchStatementIR`.


relation BlockElementStmt_ok: `TC~0~`, `f`, and `blockElementStatement`


. If let `constantDeclaration` be `blockElementStatement`:
 .. Group constantDeclaration:
  ... Let `TC~1~` and `declarationIR` be the result of <<Decl_ok, typing `constantDeclaration`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC~0~`>>.
  ... Check that `declarationIR` has type `constantDeclarationIR`.
  ... Let `constantDeclarationIR` be `declarationIR`.
  ... Result in 
* the typing context `TC~1~`,
* the abstract control flow `f`,
* and the typed block element statement `constantDeclarationIR`.
. Else if let `annotationList type name initializerOpt ;` be `blockElementStatement`:
 .. Group variableDeclaration:
  ... If `initializerOpt` matches pattern ``EMPTY`:
   .... Let `typeIR` and `tid^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Type_ok, typing `type`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC~0~`>>.
   .... Check that `tid^{asterisk}^` is an empty list.
   .... Check that <<Type_wf, `typeIR` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `$bound(LOCAL, TC~0~)`>>.
   .... Check that `<<is_assignable_typeIR, $is_assignable_typeIR(typeIR)>>`.
   .... Let `nameIR` be <<name, the name of `name`>>.
   .... Let `TC~1~` be <<add_var_t, the typing context `TC~0~` with a mapping from `nameIR` to `INOUT typeIR DYN None` added to the `LOCAL` layer>>.
   .... Let `variableDeclarationIR` be `annotationList typeIR nameIR None ;`.
   .... Result in 
* the typing context `TC~1~`,
* the abstract control flow `f`,
* and the typed block element statement `variableDeclarationIR`.
  ... Else if let `= expression~init~` be `initializerOpt`:
   .... Let `typeIR` and `tid^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Type_ok, typing `type`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC~0~`>>.
   .... Check that `tid^{asterisk}^` is an empty list.
   .... Check that <<Type_wf, `typeIR` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `$bound(LOCAL, TC~0~)`>>.
   .... Check that `<<is_assignable_typeIR, $is_assignable_typeIR(typeIR)>>`.
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR~init~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~init~`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC~0~`>>.
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR^?^` be <<coerce_unary, implicitly cast  `typedExpressionIR~init~`  to  `typeIR`>>.
   .... Check that `typedExpressionIR^?^` is Some value.
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR~init_cast~` be `typedExpressionIR^?^`.
   .... Let `nameIR` be <<name, the name of `name`>>.
   .... Let `TC~1~` be <<add_var_t, the typing context `TC~0~` with a mapping from `nameIR` to `INOUT typeIR DYN None` added to the `LOCAL` layer>>.
   .... Let `variableDeclarationIR` be `annotationList typeIR nameIR = typedExpressionIR~init_cast~ ;`.
   .... Result in 
* the typing context `TC~1~`,
* the abstract control flow `f`,
* and the typed block element statement `variableDeclarationIR`.
. Else let `statement` be `blockElementStatement`:
 .. Group statement:
  ... Let `TC~1~`, `f~post~`, and `statementIR` be the result of <<Stmt_ok, typing `statement`, under cursor `LOCAL`, typing context `TC~0~`, and abstract control flow `f`>>.
  ... Result in 
* the typing context `TC~1~`,
* the abstract control flow `f~post~`,
* and the typed block element statement `statementIR`.


relation BlockElementStmts_ok: `TC'`, `f'`, and `blockElementStatement^{asterisk}^`


. If `blockElementStatement^{asterisk}^` is an empty list:
 .. Group nil:
  ... Result in 
* the typing context `TC'`,
* the abstract control flow `f'`,
* and the typed block element statements `[ ]`.
. Else let `blockElementStatement~h~ {two-colons} blockElementStatement~t~^{asterisk}^` be `blockElementStatement^{asterisk}^`:
 .. Group cons:
  ... Let `TC~1~`, `f~1~`, and `blockElementStatementIR~h~` be the result of <<BlockElementStmt_ok, typing `blockElementStatement~h~`, under typing context `TC'` and abstract control flow `f'`>>.
  ... Let `TC~2~`, `f~2~`, and `blockElementStatementIR~t~^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<BlockElementStmts_ok, typing `blockElementStatement~t~^{asterisk}^`, under typing context `TC~1~` and abstract control flow `f~1~`>>.
  ... Result in 
* the typing context `TC~2~`,
* the abstract control flow `f~2~`,
* and the typed block element statements `blockElementStatementIR~h~ {two-colons} blockElementStatementIR~t~^{asterisk}^`.


relation Block_ok: `TC~0~`, `f`, and `annotationList { blockElementStatementList }`


. Group :
 .. Let `blockElementStatement^{asterisk}^` be <<flatten_blockElementStatementList, the list of block element statements in `blockElementStatementList`>>.
 .. Let `TC~1~`, `f~post~`, and `blockElementStatementIR^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<BlockElementStmts_ok, typing `blockElementStatement^{asterisk}^`, under typing context `TC~0~` and abstract control flow `f`>>.
 .. Let `blockStatementIR` be `annotationList { blockElementStatementIR^{asterisk}^ }`.
 .. Result in 
* the typing context `TC~1~`,
* the abstract control flow `f~post~`,
* and the typed block statement `blockStatementIR`.


relation Parameter_ok: `p`, `TC`, and `annotationList direction type name initializerOpt`


. Group :
 .. If `initializerOpt` matches pattern ``EMPTY`:
  ... Let `typeIR` and `tid~fresh~^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Type_ok, typing `type`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `bound'` be `<<bound, $bound(p, TC)>>`.
  ... Let `bound` be <<union_set, the union of the sets `bound'` and `{ tid~fresh~^{asterisk}^ }`>>.
  ... Check that <<Type_wf, `typeIR` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `bound`>>.
  ... Let `nameIR` be <<name, the name of `name`>>.
  ... Result in the parameter `annotationList direction typeIR nameIR None` and set of fresh type variables `tid~fresh~^{asterisk}^`.
 .. Else if let `= expression~init~` be `initializerOpt`:
  ... Let `typeIR` and `tid~fresh~^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Type_ok, typing `type`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `bound'` be `<<bound, $bound(p, TC)>>`.
  ... Let `bound` be <<union_set, the union of the sets `bound'` and `{ tid~fresh~^{asterisk}^ }`>>.
  ... Check that <<Type_wf, `typeIR` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `bound`>>.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~init~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~init~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `typeIR~init~` be <<type_of_typedExpressionIR, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~init~`>>.
  ... Check that `<<ctk_of_typedExpressionIR, $ctk_of_typedExpressionIR(typedExpressionIR~init~)>>` matches pattern `LCTK`.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR^?^` be <<coerce_unary, implicitly cast  `typedExpressionIR~init~`  to  `typeIR`>>.
  ... Check that `typedExpressionIR^?^` is Some value.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~init_cast~` be `typedExpressionIR^?^`.
  ... Let `nameIR` be <<name, the name of `name`>>.
  ... Let `value~init~` be the result of <<Expr_eval_lctk, the local compile-time evaluation of `typedExpressionIR~init_cast~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Result in the parameter `annotationList direction typeIR nameIR = value~init~` and set of fresh type variables `tid~fresh~^{asterisk}^`.


relation Parameters_ok: `p`, `TC`, and `parameter^{asterisk}^`


. If `parameter^{asterisk}^` is an empty list:
 .. Group nil:
  ... Result in the parameter list `[ ]` and set of fresh type variables `[ ]`.
. Else let `parameter~h~ {two-colons} parameter~t~^{asterisk}^` be `parameter^{asterisk}^`:
 .. Group cons:
  ... Let `parameterIR~h~` and `tid~fresh_h~^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Parameter_ok, typing `parameter~h~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `parameterIR~t~^{asterisk}^` and `tid~fresh_t~^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Parameters_ok, typing `parameter~t~^{asterisk}^`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Result in the parameter list `parameterIR~h~ {two-colons} parameterIR~t~^{asterisk}^` and set of fresh type variables `tid~fresh_h~^{asterisk}^ {pp} tid~fresh_t~^{asterisk}^`.


relation ConstructorParameter_ok: `p`, `TC`, and `constructorParameter`


. Group :
 .. Let `constructorParameterIR` and `tid~fresh~^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Parameter_ok, typing `constructorParameter`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
 .. Result in the constructor parameter `constructorParameterIR` and set of fresh type variables `tid~fresh~^{asterisk}^`.


relation ConstructorParameters_ok: `p`, `TC`, and `constructorParameter^{asterisk}^`


. Group :
 .. Let `constructorParameterIR^{asterisk}^` and `tid~fresh~^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Parameters_ok, typing `constructorParameter^{asterisk}^`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
 .. Result in the constructor parameter list `constructorParameterIR^{asterisk}^` and set of fresh type variables `tid~fresh~^{asterisk}^`.


relation ExternMethod_ok: `TC~0~`, `tid~extern~`, and `externMethodPrototype`


. If let `annotationList typeOrVoid name typeParameterListOpt ( parameterList ) ;` be `externMethodPrototype`:
 .. Group non-abstract:
  ... Let `nameIR` be <<name, the name of `name`>>.
  ... Check that `nameIR` is not equal to `tid~extern~`.
  ... Let `typeParameter^{asterisk}^` be <<flatten_typeParameterListOpt, the list of type parameters in `typeParameterListOpt`>>.
  ... Let `tid~expl~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `tid~expl~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
      * Let `tid~expl~` be <<name, the name of `typeParameter`>>.
--
+
for each `typeParameter` in `typeParameter^{asterisk}^`
  ... Let `TC~1~` be `<<add_typeDefs_t, $add_typeDefs_t(LOCAL, TC~0~, tid~expl~^{asterisk}^, (tid~expl~)^{asterisk}^)>>`.
  ... Let `typeIR~ret~` and `tid^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Type_ok, typing `typeOrVoid`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC~1~`>>.
  ... Check that `tid^{asterisk}^` is an empty list.
  ... Let `TC~2~` be `TC~1~[LOCAL.KIND = EXTERN_METHOD : typeIR~ret~]`.
  ... Let `parameter^{asterisk}^` be <<flatten_parameterList, the list of parameters in `parameterList`>>.
  ... Let `parameterIR^{asterisk}^` and `tid~impl~^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Parameters_ok, typing `parameter^{asterisk}^`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC~2~`>>.
  ... Let `parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^` be the list of `parameterTypeIR`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
      * Let `parameterTypeIR` be <<type_of_parameterIR, the type of  `parameterIR`>>.
--
+
for each `parameterIR` in `parameterIR^{asterisk}^`
  ... Let `TC~3~` be `<<add_parameters_t, $add_parameters_t(LOCAL, TC~2~, parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^)>>`.
  ... Let `cid` be `<<cid, $cid(name, parameterList)>>`.
  ... Let `externMethodTypeDefIR` be `EXTERN_METHOD < tid~expl~^{asterisk}^ , tid~impl~^{asterisk}^ > ( parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^ ) : typeIR~ret~`.
  ... Check that <<CallableTypeDef_wf, `externMethodTypeDefIR` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `$bound(BLOCK, TC~0~)`>>.
  ... Let `TC~4~` be `<<add_callableDef_overload_t, $add_callableDef_overload_t(BLOCK, TC~0~, cid, externMethodTypeDefIR)>>`.
  ... Let `externMethodPrototypeIR` be `annotationList typeIR~ret~ nameIR < tid~expl~^{asterisk}^ , tid~impl~^{asterisk}^ > ( parameterIR^{asterisk}^ ) ;`.
  ... Result in the updated typing context `TC~4~` and the typed method prototype `externMethodPrototypeIR`.
. Else let `annotationList ABSTRACT typeOrVoid name typeParameterListOpt ( parameterList ) ;` be `externMethodPrototype`:
 .. Group abstract:
  ... Let `nameIR` be <<name, the name of `name`>>.
  ... Check that `nameIR` is not equal to `tid~extern~`.
  ... Let `typeParameter^{asterisk}^` be <<flatten_typeParameterListOpt, the list of type parameters in `typeParameterListOpt`>>.
  ... Let `tid~expl~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `tid~expl~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
      * Let `tid~expl~` be <<name, the name of `typeParameter`>>.
--
+
for each `typeParameter` in `typeParameter^{asterisk}^`
  ... Let `TC~1~` be `<<add_typeDefs_t, $add_typeDefs_t(LOCAL, TC~0~, tid~expl~^{asterisk}^, (tid~expl~)^{asterisk}^)>>`.
  ... Let `typeIR~ret~` and `tid^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Type_ok, typing `typeOrVoid`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC~1~`>>.
  ... Check that `tid^{asterisk}^` is an empty list.
  ... Let `TC~2~` be `TC~1~[LOCAL.KIND = EXTERN_METHOD ABSTRACT : typeIR~ret~]`.
  ... Let `parameter^{asterisk}^` be <<flatten_parameterList, the list of parameters in `parameterList`>>.
  ... Let `parameterIR^{asterisk}^` and `tid~impl~^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Parameters_ok, typing `parameter^{asterisk}^`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC~2~`>>.
  ... Let `parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^` be the list of `parameterTypeIR`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
      * Let `parameterTypeIR` be <<type_of_parameterIR, the type of  `parameterIR`>>.
--
+
for each `parameterIR` in `parameterIR^{asterisk}^`
  ... Let `TC~3~` be `<<add_parameters_t, $add_parameters_t(LOCAL, TC~2~, parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^)>>`.
  ... Let `cid` be `<<cid, $cid(name, parameterList)>>`.
  ... Let `externMethodTypeDefIR` be `EXTERN_METHOD ABSTRACT < tid~expl~^{asterisk}^ , tid~impl~^{asterisk}^ > ( parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^ ) : typeIR~ret~`.
  ... Check that <<CallableTypeDef_wf, `externMethodTypeDefIR` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `$bound(BLOCK, TC~0~)`>>.
  ... Let `TC~4~` be `<<add_callableDef_overload_t, $add_callableDef_overload_t(BLOCK, TC~0~, cid, externMethodTypeDefIR)>>`.
  ... Let `externMethodPrototypeIR` be `annotationList ABSTRACT typeIR~ret~ nameIR < tid~expl~^{asterisk}^ , tid~impl~^{asterisk}^ > ( parameterIR^{asterisk}^ ) ;`.
  ... Result in the updated typing context `TC~4~` and the typed method prototype `externMethodPrototypeIR`.


relation ExternMethods_ok: `TC'`, `tid~extern~`, and `externMethodPrototype^{asterisk}^`


. If `externMethodPrototype^{asterisk}^` is an empty list:
 .. Group nil:
  ... Result in the updated typing context `TC'` and the typed method prototypes `[ ]`.
. Else let `externMethodPrototype~h~ {two-colons} externMethodPrototype~t~^{asterisk}^` be `externMethodPrototype^{asterisk}^`:
 .. Group cons:
  ... Let `TC~1~` and `externMethodPrototypeIR~h~` be the result of <<ExternMethod_ok, typing `externMethodPrototype~h~`, under typing context `TC'` for an extern object `tid~extern~`>>.
  ... Let `TC~2~` and `externMethodPrototypeIR~t~^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<ExternMethods_ok, typing `externMethodPrototype~t~^{asterisk}^`, under typing context `TC~1~` for an extern object `tid~extern~`>>.
  ... Result in the updated typing context `TC~2~` and the typed method prototypes `externMethodPrototypeIR~h~ {two-colons} externMethodPrototypeIR~t~^{asterisk}^`.


relation ExternConstructor_ok: `TC~0~`, `tid~extern~`, and `annotationList typeIdentifier ( parameterList ) ;`


. Group :
 .. Let `nameIR` be <<name, the name of `typeIdentifier`>>.
 .. Check that `nameIR` is equal to `tid~extern~`.
 .. Let `constructorParameter^{asterisk}^` be <<flatten_parameterList, the list of parameters in `parameterList`>>.
 .. Let `constructorParameterIR^{asterisk}^` and `tid~impl~^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<ConstructorParameters_ok, typing `constructorParameter^{asterisk}^`, under cursor `BLOCK` and typing context `TC~0~`>>.
 .. Let `constructorParameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^` be the list of `constructorParameterTypeIR`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
    * Let `constructorParameterTypeIR` be <<type_of_constructorParameterIR, the type of  `constructorParameterIR`>>.
--
+
for each `constructorParameterIR` in `constructorParameterIR^{asterisk}^`
 .. Let `typeDefIR^?^` be `<<find_typeDef_t, $find_typeDef_t(GLOBAL, TC~0~, tid~extern~)>>`.
 .. Check that `typeDefIR^?^` is Some value.
 .. Let `typeDefIR~extern~` be `typeDefIR^?^`.
 .. Let `(tid~expl~^{asterisk}^, tid^{asterisk}^)` be `<<type_parameters_of_typeDefIR, $type_parameters_of_typeDefIR(typeDefIR~extern~)>>`.
 .. Check that `tid^{asterisk}^` is an empty list.
 .. Let `cid` be `<<cid_, $cid_(typeIdentifier, ( parameterList ))>>`.
 .. Let `typeIR~extern_spec~` be `typeDefIR~extern~ < (tid~expl~)^{asterisk}^ >`.
 .. Let `constructorTypeDefIR` be `CONSTRUCTOR < tid~expl~^{asterisk}^ , tid~impl~^{asterisk}^ > ( constructorParameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^ ) : typeIR~extern_spec~`.
 .. Check that <<ConstructorTypeDef_wf, `constructorTypeDefIR` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `$bound(BLOCK, TC~0~)`>>.
 .. Let `TC~1~` be `<<add_constructorDef_t, $add_constructorDef_t(TC~0~, cid, constructorTypeDefIR)>>`.
 .. Let `externConstructorPrototypeIR` be `annotationList nameIR < , tid~impl~^{asterisk}^ > ( constructorParameterIR^{asterisk}^ ) ;`.
 .. Result in the updated typing context `TC~1~` and the typed constructor prototype `externConstructorPrototypeIR`.


relation ExternConstructors_ok: `TC'`, `tid~extern~`, and `externConstructorPrototype^{asterisk}^`


. If `externConstructorPrototype^{asterisk}^` is an empty list:
 .. Group nil:
  ... Result in the updated typing context `TC'` and the typed constructor prototypes `[ ]`.
. Else let `externConstructorPrototype~h~ {two-colons} externConstructorPrototype~t~^{asterisk}^` be `externConstructorPrototype^{asterisk}^`:
 .. Group cons:
  ... Let `TC~1~` and `externConstructorPrototypeIR~h~` be the result of <<ExternConstructor_ok, typing `externConstructorPrototype~h~`, under typing context `TC'` for an extern object `tid~extern~`>>.
  ... Let `TC~2~` and `externConstructorPrototypeIR~t~^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<ExternConstructors_ok, typing `externConstructorPrototype~t~^{asterisk}^`, under typing context `TC~1~` for an extern object `tid~extern~`>>.
  ... Result in the updated typing context `TC~2~` and the typed constructor prototypes `externConstructorPrototypeIR~h~ {two-colons} externConstructorPrototypeIR~t~^{asterisk}^`.


relation ParserTransition_ok: `TC~0~`, `nameIR~state~^{asterisk}^`, and `transitionStatement`


. If `transitionStatement` matches pattern ``EMPTY`:
 .. Group empty:
  ... Result in the typed transition statement `TRANSITION "reject" ;`.
. Else let `TRANSITION stateExpression` be `transitionStatement`:
 .. Else if let `name ;` be `stateExpression`:
  ... Group name:
   .... Let `nameIR` be <<name, the name of `name`>>.
   .... Check that `nameIR` is in `nameIR~state~^{asterisk}^`.
   .... Let `transitionStatementIR` be `TRANSITION nameIR ;`.
   .... Result in the typed transition statement `transitionStatementIR`.
 .. Else if let `SELECT ( expressionList~key~ ) { selectCaseList }` be `stateExpression`:
  ... Group select:
   .... Let `expression~key~^{asterisk}^` be <<flatten_expressionList, the list of expressions in `expressionList~key~`>>.
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR~key~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `typedExpressionIR~key~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
        * Let `typedExpressionIR~key~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~key~`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC~0~`>>.
--
+
for each `expression~key~` in `expression~key~^{asterisk}^`
   .... Let `typeIR~key~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `typeIR~key~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
        * Let `typeIR~key~` be <<type_of_typedExpressionIR, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~key~`>>.
--
+
for each `typedExpressionIR~key~` in `typedExpressionIR~key~^{asterisk}^`
   .... Check that <<Type_wf, `SET < [typeIR~key~] >` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `$bound(LOCAL, TC~0~)`>>, for all `typeIR~key~` in `typeIR~key~^{asterisk}^`.
   .... Let `selectCase^{asterisk}^` be <<flatten_selectCaseList, the list of select cases in `selectCaseList`>>.
   .... Let `selectCaseIR^{asterisk}^` be the list of `selectCaseIR`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
        * Let <<SelectCase_ok, `TC~0~ nameIR~state~^{asterisk}^ typeIR~key~^{asterisk}^ |- selectCase : selectCaseIR`>>.
--
+
for each `selectCase` in `selectCase^{asterisk}^`
   .... Let `transitionStatementIR` be `TRANSITION SELECT ( typedExpressionIR~key~^{asterisk}^ ) { selectCaseIR^{asterisk}^ }`.
   .... Result in the typed transition statement `transitionStatementIR`.


relation ParserStmt_ok: `TC~0'~` and `parserStatement''`


. If let `constantDeclaration` be `parserStatement''`:
 .. Group constantDeclaration:
  ... Let `TC~1~` and `declarationIR` be the result of <<Decl_ok, typing `constantDeclaration`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC~0'~`>>.
  ... Check that `declarationIR` has type `constantDeclarationIR`.
  ... Let `constantDeclarationIR` be `declarationIR`.
  ... Result in the updated typing context `TC~1~` and the typed parser statement `constantDeclarationIR`.
. Else if let `annotationList type name initializerOpt ;` be `parserStatement''`:
 .. Group variableDeclaration:
  ... If `initializerOpt` matches pattern ``EMPTY`:
   .... Let `typeIR` and `tid^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Type_ok, typing `type`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC~0'~`>>.
   .... Check that `tid^{asterisk}^` is an empty list.
   .... Check that <<Type_wf, `typeIR` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `$bound(LOCAL, TC~0'~)`>>.
   .... Check that `<<is_assignable_typeIR, $is_assignable_typeIR(typeIR)>>`.
   .... Let `nameIR` be <<name, the name of `name`>>.
   .... Let `TC~1~` be <<add_var_t, the typing context `TC~0'~` with a mapping from `nameIR` to `INOUT typeIR DYN None` added to the `LOCAL` layer>>.
   .... Let `variableDeclarationIR` be `annotationList typeIR nameIR None ;`.
   .... Result in the updated typing context `TC~1~` and the typed parser statement `variableDeclarationIR`.
  ... Else if let `= expression~init~` be `initializerOpt`:
   .... Let `typeIR` and `tid^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Type_ok, typing `type`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC~0'~`>>.
   .... Check that `tid^{asterisk}^` is an empty list.
   .... Check that <<Type_wf, `typeIR` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `$bound(LOCAL, TC~0'~)`>>.
   .... Check that `<<is_assignable_typeIR, $is_assignable_typeIR(typeIR)>>`.
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR~init~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~init~`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC~0'~`>>.
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR^?^` be <<coerce_unary, implicitly cast  `typedExpressionIR~init~`  to  `typeIR`>>.
   .... Check that `typedExpressionIR^?^` is Some value.
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR~init_cast~` be `typedExpressionIR^?^`.
   .... Let `nameIR` be <<name, the name of `name`>>.
   .... Let `TC~1~` be <<add_var_t, the typing context `TC~0'~` with a mapping from `nameIR` to `INOUT typeIR DYN None` added to the `LOCAL` layer>>.
   .... Let `variableDeclarationIR` be `annotationList typeIR nameIR = typedExpressionIR~init_cast~ ;`.
   .... Result in the updated typing context `TC~1~` and the typed parser statement `variableDeclarationIR`.
. Else if let `emptyStatement` be `parserStatement''`:
 .. Group emptyStatement:
  ... Let `typingContext`, `flow`, and `statementIR` be the result of <<Stmt_ok, typing `emptyStatement`, under cursor `LOCAL`, typing context `TC~0'~`, and abstract control flow `CONT`>>.
  ... Check that `typingContext` is equal to `TC~0'~`.
  ... Check that `flow` matches pattern `CONT`.
  ... Check that `statementIR` has type `emptyStatementIR`.
  ... Let `emptyStatementIR` be `statementIR`.
  ... Result in the updated typing context `TC~0'~` and the typed parser statement `emptyStatementIR`.
. Else if let `assignmentStatement` be `parserStatement''`:
 .. Group assignmentStatement:
  ... Let `TC~1~`, `flow`, and `statementIR` be the result of <<Stmt_ok, typing `assignmentStatement`, under cursor `LOCAL`, typing context `TC~0'~`, and abstract control flow `CONT`>>.
  ... Check that `flow` matches pattern `CONT`.
  ... Check that `statementIR` has type `assignmentStatementIR`.
  ... Let `assignmentStatementIR` be `statementIR`.
  ... Result in the updated typing context `TC~1~` and the typed parser statement `assignmentStatementIR`.
. Else if let `callStatement` be `parserStatement''`:
 .. Group callStatement:
  ... Let `TC~1~`, `flow`, and `statementIR` be the result of <<Stmt_ok, typing `callStatement`, under cursor `LOCAL`, typing context `TC~0'~`, and abstract control flow `CONT`>>.
  ... Check that `flow` matches pattern `CONT`.
  ... Check that `statementIR` has type `callStatementIR`.
  ... Let `callStatementIR` be `statementIR`.
  ... Result in the updated typing context `TC~1~` and the typed parser statement `callStatementIR`.
. Else if let `directApplicationStatement` be `parserStatement''`:
 .. Group directApplicationStatement:
  ... Let `TC~1~`, `flow`, and `statementIR` be the result of <<Stmt_ok, typing `directApplicationStatement`, under cursor `LOCAL`, typing context `TC~0'~`, and abstract control flow `CONT`>>.
  ... Check that `flow` matches pattern `CONT`.
  ... Check that `statementIR` has type `directApplicationStatementIR`.
  ... Let `directApplicationStatementIR` be `statementIR`.
  ... Result in the updated typing context `TC~1~` and the typed parser statement `directApplicationStatementIR`.
. Else if let `annotationList { parserStatementList }` be `parserStatement''`:
 .. Group parserBlockStatement:
  ... Let `parserStatement^{asterisk}^` be <<flatten_parserStatementList, the list of parser statements in `parserStatementList`>>.
  ... Let `TC~1~` be `<<enter_t, $enter_t(TC~0'~)>>`.
  ... Let `TC~2~` and `parserStatementIR^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<ParserStmts_ok, typing `parserStatement^{asterisk}^`, under typing context `TC~1~`>>.
  ... Let `TC~3~` be `<<exit_t, $exit_t(TC~2~)>>`.
  ... Let `parserBlockStatementIR` be `annotationList { parserStatementIR^{asterisk}^ }`.
  ... Result in the updated typing context `TC~1~` and the typed parser statement `parserBlockStatementIR`.
. Else let `parserConditionalStatement` be `parserStatement''`:
 .. Group parserConditionalStatement:
  ... If let `IF ( expression~cond~ ) parserStatement~then~` be `parserConditionalStatement`:
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR~cond~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~cond~`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC~0'~`>>.
   .... Let `typeIR~cond~` be <<type_of_typedExpressionIR, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~cond~`>>.
   .... Check that `BOOL` is equal to <<canon_typeIR, the canonicalized form of `typeIR~cond~`>>.
   .... Let `TC~then~` and `parserStatementIR~then~` be the result of <<ParserStmt_ok, typing `parserStatement~then~`, under typing context `TC~0'~`>>.
   .... Result in the updated typing context `TC~0'~` and the typed parser statement `IF ( typedExpressionIR~cond~ ) parserStatementIR~then~`.
  ... Else let `IF ( expression~cond~ ) parserStatement~then~ ELSE parserStatement~else~` be `parserConditionalStatement`:
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR~cond~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~cond~`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC~0'~`>>.
   .... Let `typeIR~cond~` be <<type_of_typedExpressionIR, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~cond~`>>.
   .... Check that `BOOL` is equal to <<canon_typeIR, the canonicalized form of `typeIR~cond~`>>.
   .... Let `TC~then~` and `parserStatementIR~then~` be the result of <<ParserStmt_ok, typing `parserStatement~then~`, under typing context `TC~0'~`>>.
   .... Let `TC~else~` and `parserStatementIR~else~` be the result of <<ParserStmt_ok, typing `parserStatement~else~`, under typing context `TC~0'~`>>.
   .... Result in the updated typing context `TC~0'~` and the typed parser statement `IF ( typedExpressionIR~cond~ ) parserStatementIR~then~ ELSE parserStatementIR~else~`.


relation ParserStmts_ok: `TC'` and `parserStatement^{asterisk}^`


. If `parserStatement^{asterisk}^` is an empty list:
 .. Group nil:
  ... Result in the updated typing context `TC'` and the typed parser statements `[ ]`.
. Else let `parserStatement~h~ {two-colons} parserStatement~t~^{asterisk}^` be `parserStatement^{asterisk}^`:
 .. Group cons:
  ... Let `TC~1~` and `parserStatementIR~h~` be the result of <<ParserStmt_ok, typing `parserStatement~h~`, under typing context `TC'`>>.
  ... Let `TC~2~` and `parserStatementIR~t~^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<ParserStmts_ok, typing `parserStatement~t~^{asterisk}^`, under typing context `TC~1~`>>.
  ... Result in the updated typing context `TC~2~` and the typed parser statements `parserStatementIR~h~ {two-colons} parserStatementIR~t~^{asterisk}^`.


relation ParserState_ok: `TC~0~`, `nameIR~state~^{asterisk}^`, and `annotationList STATE name { parserStatementList transitionStatement }`


. Group :
 .. Let `nameIR` be <<name, the name of `name`>>.
 .. Let `TC~1~` be `<<enter_t, $enter_t(TC~0~)>>`.
 .. Let `parserStatement^{asterisk}^` be <<flatten_parserStatementList, the list of parser statements in `parserStatementList`>>.
 .. Let `TC~2~` and `parserStatementIR^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<ParserStmts_ok, typing `parserStatement^{asterisk}^`, under typing context `TC~1~`>>.
 .. Let `transitionStatementIR` be the result of <<ParserTransition_ok, typing `transitionStatement`, under typing context `TC~2~` and parser state names `nameIR~state~^{asterisk}^`>>.
 .. Let `TC~3~` be `<<exit_t, $exit_t(TC~2~)>>`.
 .. Let `parserStateIR` be `annotationList STATE nameIR { parserStatementIR^{asterisk}^ transitionStatementIR }`.
 .. Result in the typed parser state `parserStateIR`.


relation ParserStates_ok: `TC` and `parserState^{asterisk}^`


. Group :
 .. Let `name~state~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `name~state~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
    * Let `++_++ STATE name~state~ { ++_++ ++_++ }` be `parserState`.
--
+
for each `parserState` in `parserState^{asterisk}^`
 .. Let `nameIR~state~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `nameIR~state~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
    * Let `nameIR~state~` be <<name, the name of `name~state~`>>.
--
+
for each `name~state~` in `name~state~^{asterisk}^`
 .. Check that <<distinct_, the elements of `nameIR~state~^{asterisk}^` are distinct>>.
 .. Check that `"start"` is in `nameIR~state~^{asterisk}^`.
 .. Check that `"accept" is not in nameIR~state~^{asterisk}^` *and* `"reject" is not in nameIR~state~^{asterisk}^`.
 .. Let `nameIR~state_impl~^{asterisk}^` be `"accept" {two-colons} "reject" {two-colons} nameIR~state~^{asterisk}^`.
 .. Let `parserStateIR^{asterisk}^` be the list of `parserStateIR`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
    * Let `parserStateIR` be the result of <<ParserState_ok, typing `parserState`, under typing context `TC` and parser state names `nameIR~state_impl~^{asterisk}^`>>.
--
+
for each `parserState` in `parserState^{asterisk}^`
 .. Result in the typed parser states `parserStateIR^{asterisk}^`.


relation ParserLocalDecl_ok: `TC~0~` and `parserLocalDeclaration`


. If let `constantDeclaration` be `parserLocalDeclaration`:
 .. Group constantDeclaration:
  ... Let `TC~1~` and `declarationIR` be the result of <<Decl_ok, typing `constantDeclaration`, under cursor `BLOCK` and typing context `TC~0~`>>.
  ... Check that `declarationIR` has type `constantDeclarationIR`.
  ... Let `constantDeclarationIR` be `declarationIR`.
  ... Result in the updated typing context `TC~1~` and the typed parser local declaration `constantDeclarationIR`.
. Else if let `instantiation` be `parserLocalDeclaration`:
 .. Group instantiation:
  ... Let `TC~1~` and `declarationIR` be the result of <<Decl_ok, typing `instantiation`, under cursor `BLOCK` and typing context `TC~0~`>>.
  ... Check that `declarationIR` has type `instantiationIR`.
  ... Let `instantiationIR` be `declarationIR`.
  ... Result in the updated typing context `TC~1~` and the typed parser local declaration `instantiationIR`.
. Else if let `annotationList type name initializerOpt ;` be `parserLocalDeclaration`:
 .. Group variableDeclaration:
  ... If `initializerOpt` matches pattern ``EMPTY`:
   .... Let `typeIR` and `tid^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Type_ok, typing `type`, under cursor `BLOCK` and typing context `TC~0~`>>.
   .... Check that `tid^{asterisk}^` is an empty list.
   .... Check that <<Type_wf, `typeIR` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `$bound(BLOCK, TC~0~)`>>.
   .... Check that `<<is_assignable_typeIR, $is_assignable_typeIR(typeIR)>>`.
   .... Let `nameIR` be <<name, the name of `name`>>.
   .... Let `varTypeIR` be `INOUT typeIR DYN None`.
   .... Let `TC~1~` be <<add_var_t, the typing context `TC~0~` with a mapping from `nameIR` to `varTypeIR` added to the `BLOCK` layer>>.
   .... Let `variableDeclarationIR` be `annotationList typeIR nameIR None ;`.
   .... Result in the updated typing context `TC~1~` and the typed parser local declaration `variableDeclarationIR`.
  ... Else if let `= expression~init~` be `initializerOpt`:
   .... Let `typeIR` and `tid^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Type_ok, typing `type`, under cursor `BLOCK` and typing context `TC~0~`>>.
   .... Check that `tid^{asterisk}^` is an empty list.
   .... Check that <<Type_wf, `typeIR` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `$bound(BLOCK, TC~0~)`>>.
   .... Check that `<<is_assignable_typeIR, $is_assignable_typeIR(typeIR)>>`.
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR~init~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~init~`, under cursor `BLOCK` and typing context `TC~0~`>>.
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR^?^` be <<coerce_unary, implicitly cast  `typedExpressionIR~init~`  to  `typeIR`>>.
   .... Check that `typedExpressionIR^?^` is Some value.
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR~init_cast~` be `typedExpressionIR^?^`.
   .... Let `nameIR` be <<name, the name of `name`>>.
   .... Let `varTypeIR` be `INOUT typeIR DYN None`.
   .... Let `TC~1~` be <<add_var_t, the typing context `TC~0~` with a mapping from `nameIR` to `varTypeIR` added to the `BLOCK` layer>>.
   .... Let `variableDeclarationIR` be `annotationList typeIR nameIR = typedExpressionIR~init_cast~ ;`.
   .... Result in the updated typing context `TC~1~` and the typed parser local declaration `variableDeclarationIR`.
. Else let `annotationList VALUE_SET < valueSetType > ( expression ) name ;` be `parserLocalDeclaration`:
 .. Group valueSetDeclaration:
  ... Let `typeIR` and `tid^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Type_ok, typing `valueSetType`, under cursor `BLOCK` and typing context `TC~0~`>>.
  ... Check that `tid^{asterisk}^` is an empty list.
  ... Check that <<Type_wf, `SET < [typeIR] >` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `$bound(BLOCK, TC~0~)`>>.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression`, under cursor `BLOCK` and typing context `TC~0~`>>.
  ... Check that `<<ctk_of_typedExpressionIR, $ctk_of_typedExpressionIR(typedExpressionIR)>>` does not match pattern `DYN`.
  ... Let `nameIR` be <<name, the name of `name`>>.
  ... Let `varTypeIR` be `SET < [typeIR] > CTK None`.
  ... Let `TC~1~` be <<add_var_t, the typing context `TC~0~` with a mapping from `nameIR` to `varTypeIR` added to the `BLOCK` layer>>.
  ... Let `valueSetDeclarationIR` be `annotationList VALUE_SET < typeIR > ( typedExpressionIR ) nameIR ;`.
  ... Result in the updated typing context `TC~1~` and the typed parser local declaration `valueSetDeclarationIR`.


relation ParserLocalDecls_ok: `TC'` and `parserLocalDeclaration^{asterisk}^`


. If `parserLocalDeclaration^{asterisk}^` is an empty list:
 .. Group nil:
  ... Result in the updated typing context `TC'` and the typed parser local declarations `[ ]`.
. Else let `parserLocalDeclaration~h~ {two-colons} parserLocalDeclaration~t~^{asterisk}^` be `parserLocalDeclaration^{asterisk}^`:
 .. Group cons:
  ... Let `TC~1~` and `parserLocalDeclarationIR~h~` be the result of <<ParserLocalDecl_ok, typing `parserLocalDeclaration~h~`, under typing context `TC'`>>.
  ... Let `TC~2~` and `parserLocalDeclarationIR~t~^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<ParserLocalDecls_ok, typing `parserLocalDeclaration~t~^{asterisk}^`, under typing context `TC~1~`>>.
  ... Result in the updated typing context `TC~2~` and the typed parser local declarations `parserLocalDeclarationIR~h~ {two-colons} parserLocalDeclarationIR~t~^{asterisk}^`.


relation TableKey_ok: `TC`, `TBLC~0~`, and `expression : name~matchkind~ annotationList ;`


. Group :
 .. Let `typedExpressionIR` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC`>>.
 .. Let `typeIR` be <<type_of_typedExpressionIR, the type of  `typedExpressionIR`>>.
 .. Check that <<Type_wf, `SET < [typeIR] >` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `$bound(LOCAL, TC)`>>.
 .. Let `nameIR~matchkind~` be <<name, the name of `name~matchkind~`>>.
 .. Check that `MATCH_KIND . nameIR~matchkind~` is equal to `<<find_var_value_t, $find_var_value_t(LOCAL, TC, nameIR~matchkind~)>>`.
 .. Check that `<<compat_table_key, $compat_table_key(nameIR~matchkind~, typeIR)>>`.
 .. Let `TBLC~1~` be `<<update_mode, $update_mode(TBLC~0~, nameIR~matchkind~, typeIR)>>`.
 .. Let `TBLC~2~` be `<<add_key, $add_key(TBLC~1~, nameIR~matchkind~, typeIR)>>`.
 .. Let `tableKeyIR` be `typedExpressionIR : nameIR~matchkind~ annotationList ;`.
 .. Result in the updated table context `TBLC~2~` and the typed table key `tableKeyIR`.


relation TableKeys_ok: `TC`, `TBLC'`, and `tableKey^{asterisk}^`


. If `tableKey^{asterisk}^` is an empty list:
 .. Group nil:
  ... Result in the updated table context `TBLC'` and the typed table keys `[ ]`.
. Else let `tableKey~h~ {two-colons} tableKey~t~^{asterisk}^` be `tableKey^{asterisk}^`:
 .. Group cons:
  ... Let `TBLC~1~` and `tableKeyIR~h~` be the result of <<TableKey_ok, typing `tableKey~h~`, under typing context `TC` and table context `TBLC'`>>.
  ... Let `TBLC~2~` and `tableKeyIR~t~^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<TableKeys_ok, typing `tableKey~t~^{asterisk}^`, under typing context `TC` and table context `TBLC~1~`>>.
  ... Result in the updated table context `TBLC~2~` and the typed table keys `tableKeyIR~h~ {two-colons} tableKeyIR~t~^{asterisk}^`.


relation Call_action_partial_ok: `TC`, `parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^`, and `argumentIR^{asterisk}^`


. Group :
 .. Let `(parameterTypeIR~data~^{asterisk}^, parameterTypeIR~control~^{asterisk}^)` be `<<split_dataplane_parameters, $split_dataplane_parameters(parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^)>>`.
 .. Check that the length of `parameterTypeIR~data~^{asterisk}^` is equal to the length of `argumentIR^{asterisk}^`.
 .. Let `argumentIR~cast~^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Call_convention_ok, checking the calling convention of `argumentIR^{asterisk}^` applied to parameter types `parameterTypeIR~data~^{asterisk}^`, under cursor `LOCAL`, typing context `TC`, and action context `ACTION`>>.
 .. Result in the typed argument list `parameterTypeIR~data~^{asterisk}^`.


relation TableAction_ok: `TC`, `TBLC~0~`, and `annotationList tableActionReference ;`


. If let `prefixedNonTypeName` be `tableActionReference`:
 .. Group prefixedNonTypeName:
  ... Let `prefixedNameIR` be <<prefixedNonTypeName, the prefixed name of  `prefixedNonTypeName`>>.
  ... Let `callableTypeDefIR'^?^` be `<<find_callableDef_non_overloaded_t, $find_callableDef_non_overloaded_t(LOCAL, TC, prefixedNameIR)>>`.
  ... Check that `callableTypeDefIR'^?^` is Some value.
  ... Let `callableTypeDefIR` be `callableTypeDefIR'^?^`.
  ... Check that `callableTypeDefIR` has type `actionTypeIR`.
  ... Let `ACTION ( parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^ )` be `callableTypeDefIR`.
  ... Let `parameterTypeIR~data~^{asterisk}^`, `parameterTypeIR~control~^{asterisk}^`, and `argumentIR^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Call_action_partial_ok, typing `[ ]`, under typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Check that `argumentIR^{asterisk}^` is an empty list.
  ... Let `TBLC~1~` be `<<add_action, $add_action(TBLC~0~, prefixedNameIR, parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^, [ ])>>`.
  ... Let `tableActionIR` be `annotationList prefixedNameIR ( [ ] ) ;`.
  ... Result in the updated table context `TBLC~1~` and the typed table action `tableActionIR`.
. Else if let `prefixedNonTypeName ( argumentList )` be `tableActionReference`:
 .. Group prefixedNonTypeName-argumentList:
  ... Let `prefixedNameIR` be <<prefixedNonTypeName, the prefixed name of  `prefixedNonTypeName`>>.
  ... Let `callableTypeDefIR'^?^` be `<<find_callableDef_non_overloaded_t, $find_callableDef_non_overloaded_t(LOCAL, TC, prefixedNameIR)>>`.
  ... Check that `callableTypeDefIR'^?^` is Some value.
  ... Let `callableTypeDefIR` be `callableTypeDefIR'^?^`.
  ... Check that `callableTypeDefIR` has type `actionTypeIR`.
  ... Let `ACTION ( parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^ )` be `callableTypeDefIR`.
  ... Let `argument^{asterisk}^` be <<flatten_argumentList, the list of arguments in `argumentList`>>.
  ... Let `argumentIR^{asterisk}^` be the list of `argumentIR`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
      * Let `argumentIR` be the result of <<Argument_ok, typing `argument`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC`>>.
--
+
for each `argument` in `argument^{asterisk}^`
  ... Let `parameterTypeIR~data~^{asterisk}^`, `parameterTypeIR~control~^{asterisk}^`, and `argumentIR~cast~^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Call_action_partial_ok, typing `argumentIR^{asterisk}^`, under typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `TBLC~1~` be `<<add_action, $add_action(TBLC~0~, prefixedNameIR, parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^, argumentIR~cast~^{asterisk}^)>>`.
  ... Let `tableActionIR` be `annotationList prefixedNameIR ( argumentIR~cast~^{asterisk}^ ) ;`.
  ... Result in the updated table context `TBLC~1~` and the typed table action `tableActionIR`.


relation TableActions_ok: `TC`, `TBLC'`, and `tableAction^{asterisk}^`


. If `tableAction^{asterisk}^` is an empty list:
 .. Group nil:
  ... Result in the updated table context `TBLC'` and the typed table actions `[ ]`.
. Else let `tableAction~h~ {two-colons} tableAction~t~^{asterisk}^` be `tableAction^{asterisk}^`:
 .. Group cons:
  ... Let `TBLC~1~` and `tableActionIR~h~` be the result of <<TableAction_ok, typing `tableAction~h~`, under typing context `TC` and table context `TBLC'`>>.
  ... Let `TBLC~2~` and `tableActionIR~t~^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<TableActions_ok, typing `tableAction~t~^{asterisk}^`, under typing context `TC` and table context `TBLC~1~`>>.
  ... Result in the updated table context `TBLC~2~` and the typed table actions `tableActionIR~h~ {two-colons} tableActionIR~t~^{asterisk}^`.


relation Call_action_default_ok: `TC`, `parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^`, and `argumentIR^{asterisk}^`


. Group :
 .. Let `(parameterTypeIR~data~^{asterisk}^, parameterTypeIR~control~^{asterisk}^)` be `<<split_dataplane_parameters, $split_dataplane_parameters(parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^)>>`.
 .. Let `argumentIR~cast~^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Call_convention_ok, checking the calling convention of `argumentIR^{asterisk}^` applied to parameter types `parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^`, under cursor `LOCAL`, typing context `TC`, and action context `ACTION`>>.
 .. Result in the typed argument list `parameterTypeIR~data~^{asterisk}^`.


relation TableDefaultAction_ok: `TC`, `TBLC`, and `= expression`


. If let `prefixedNonTypeName` be `expression`:
 .. Group prefixedNonTypeName:
  ... Let `prefixedNameIR` be <<prefixedNonTypeName, the prefixed name of  `prefixedNonTypeName`>>.
  ... Check that (`[ ]`, `[ ]`) is equal to `<<find_action, $find_action(TBLC, prefixedNameIR)>>`.
  ... Result in the typed default action `prefixedNameIR ( [ ] )`.
. Else if let `callExpression` be `expression`:
 .. Check that `callExpression` matches pattern `% ( % )`.
 .. Let `callTarget ( argumentList )` be `callExpression`.
 .. Check that `callTarget` has type `prefixedNonTypeName`.
 .. Let `prefixedNonTypeName` be `callTarget`.
 .. Group prefixedNonTypeName-argumentList:
  ... Let `prefixedNameIR` be <<prefixedNonTypeName, the prefixed name of  `prefixedNonTypeName`>>.
  ... Let `(parameterTypeIR*, argumentListIR)^?^` be `<<find_action, $find_action(TBLC, prefixedNameIR)>>`.
  ... Check that `(parameterTypeIR*, argumentListIR)^?^` is Some value.
  ... Let `(parameterTypeIR~action~^{asterisk}^, argumentIR~action~^{asterisk}^)` be `(parameterTypeIR*, argumentListIR)^?^`.
  ... Let `argument^{asterisk}^` be <<flatten_argumentList, the list of arguments in `argumentList`>>.
  ... Let `argumentIR^{asterisk}^` be the list of `argumentIR`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
      * Let `argumentIR` be the result of <<Argument_ok, typing `argument`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC`>>.
--
+
for each `argument` in `argument^{asterisk}^`
  ... Let `parameterTypeIR~action_data~^{asterisk}^`, `parameterTypeIR~action_control~^{asterisk}^`, and `argumentIR~cast~^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Call_action_default_ok, typing `argumentIR^{asterisk}^`, under typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `argumentIR~action_data~^{asterisk}^` be `argumentIR~action~^{asterisk}^[0 : the length of parameterTypeIR~action_data~^{asterisk}^]`.
  ... Let `argumentIR~cast_data~^{asterisk}^` be `argumentIR~cast~^{asterisk}^[0 : the length of parameterTypeIR~action_data~^{asterisk}^]`.
  ... Check that `argumentIR~action_data~` is equal to `argumentIR~cast_data~`, for all `argumentIR~action_data~` in `argumentIR~action_data~^{asterisk}^` and `argumentIR~cast_data~` in `argumentIR~cast_data~^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Result in the typed default action `prefixedNameIR ( argumentIR~cast~^{asterisk}^ )`.


relation TableEntry_keyset_ok: `TC`, `TBLC`, and `keysetExpression`


. If let `expression` be `keysetExpression`:
 .. Group simpleKeysetExpression-expression:
  ... Check that the length of `TBLC.KEYS` is equal to `1`.
  ... Let <<TableEntry_keysets_simple_ok, `TC TBLC NOLPM |- TBLC.KEYS @ [expression] : TBLS simpleKeysetExpressionIR'^{asterisk}^`>>.
  ... Check that `simpleKeysetExpressionIR'^{asterisk}^` is a list of length 1.
  ... Let `[simpleKeysetExpressionIR]` be `simpleKeysetExpressionIR'^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Result in the updated table context `TBLS` and the typed keyset expression `simpleKeysetExpressionIR`.
. Else if let `tupleKeysetExpression` be `keysetExpression`:
 .. If let `( expression~l~ &&& expression~r~ )` be `tupleKeysetExpression`:
  ... Group tupleKeysetExpression-mask:
   .... Check that the length of `TBLC.KEYS` is equal to `1`.
   .... Let <<TableEntry_keysets_simple_ok, `TC TBLC NOLPM |- TBLC.KEYS @ [expression~l~ &&& expression~r~] : TBLS simpleKeysetExpressionIR'^{asterisk}^`>>.
   .... Check that `simpleKeysetExpressionIR'^{asterisk}^` is a list of length 1.
   .... Let `[simpleKeysetExpressionIR]` be `simpleKeysetExpressionIR'^{asterisk}^`.
   .... Result in the updated table context `TBLS` and the typed keyset expression `( [simpleKeysetExpressionIR] )`.
 .. Else if let `( expression~l~ .. expression~r~ )` be `tupleKeysetExpression`:
  ... Group tupleKeysetExpression-range:
   .... Check that the length of `TBLC.KEYS` is equal to `1`.
   .... Let <<TableEntry_keysets_simple_ok, `TC TBLC NOLPM |- TBLC.KEYS @ [expression~l~ .. expression~r~] : TBLS simpleKeysetExpressionIR'^{asterisk}^`>>.
   .... Check that `simpleKeysetExpressionIR'^{asterisk}^` is a list of length 1.
   .... Let `[simpleKeysetExpressionIR]` be `simpleKeysetExpressionIR'^{asterisk}^`.
