  ... Let `typeIR~parser_spec~` be `parserObjectTypeDefIR < [ ] >`.
  ... Let `constructorTypeDefIR` be `CONSTRUCTOR < [ ] , [ ] > ( constructorParameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^ ) : typeIR~parser_spec~`.
  ... Check that <<ConstructorTypeDef_wf, `constructorTypeDefIR` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `$bound(GLOBAL, TC~0~)`>>.
  ... Let `TC~6~` be `<<add_constructorDef_t, $add_constructorDef_t(TC~0~, cid, constructorTypeDefIR)>>`.
  ... Let `nameIR` be <<name, the name of `name`>>.
  ... Let `parserDeclarationIR` be `annotationList PARSER nameIR < [ ] > ( parameterIR^{asterisk}^ ) ( constructorParameterIR^{asterisk}^ ) { parserLocalDeclarationIR^{asterisk}^ parserStateIR^{asterisk}^ }`.
  ... Result in the modified typing context `TC~6~` and the typed declaration `parserDeclarationIR`.
. Else if let `annotationList CONTROL name typeParameterListOpt ( parameterList ) constructorParameterListOpt { controlLocalDeclarationList APPLY controlBody }` be `declaration`:
 .. Check that `typeParameterListOpt` matches pattern ``EMPTY`.
 .. Group controlDeclaration:
  ... Let `TC~1~` be `TC~0~[BLOCK.KIND = CONTROL]`.
