relation Decls_ok: `p`, `TC'`, and `declaration^{asterisk}^`


. If `declaration^{asterisk}^` is an empty list:
 .. Group nil:
  ... Result in the modified typing context `TC'` and the typed declarations `[ ]`.
. Else let `declaration~h~ {two-colons} declaration~t~^{asterisk}^` be `declaration^{asterisk}^`:
 .. Group cons:
  ... Let `TC~1~` and `declarationIR~h~` be the result of <<Decl_ok, typing `declaration~h~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC'`>>.
  ... Let `TC~2~` and `declarationIR~t~^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Decls_ok, typing `declaration~t~^{asterisk}^`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC~1~`,
* and the modified typing context>>.
  ... Result in the modified typing context `TC~2~` and the typed declarations `declarationIR~h~ {two-colons} declarationIR~t~^{asterisk}^`.


relation Program_ok: `p4program`


. Group :
 .. Let `declaration^{asterisk}^` be <<flatten_p4program, the list of declarations in `p4program`>>.
 .. Let `TC~0~` be <<empty_typingContext, an empty typing context>>.
 .. Let `TC~1~` and `declarationIR^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Decls_ok, typing `declaration^{asterisk}^`, under cursor `GLOBAL` and typing context `TC~0~`,
* and the modified typing context>>.
 .. Result in the typed P4 program `declarationIR^{asterisk}^ ;`.


relation Call_convention_expr_ok: `p`, `TC`, `actctxt`, `direction typeIR~param~ ++_++ ++_++^?^`, and `typedExpressionIR~arg~`


. If `direction` matches pattern `IN`:
 .. Group in:
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR^?^` be <<coerce_unary, implicitly cast  `typedExpressionIR~arg~`  to  `typeIR~param~`>>.
  ... Check that `typedExpressionIR^?^` is Some value.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~arg_cast~` be `typedExpressionIR^?^`.
  ... Result in `typedExpressionIR~arg_cast~`.
. Group out-inout:
 .. If `direction` matches pattern `OUT`:
  ... Let `typeIR~arg~` be <<type_of_typedExpressionIR, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~arg~`>>.
  ... Check that <<Type_alpha, `typeIR~param~` and `typeIR~arg~` are the same type>>.
  ... Check that <<Expr_lvalue_ok, `p TC |- typedExpressionIR~arg~`>>.
  ... Result in `typedExpressionIR~arg~`.
 .. Else if `direction` matches pattern `INOUT`:
  ... Let `typeIR~arg~` be <<type_of_typedExpressionIR, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~arg~`>>.
  ... Check that <<Type_alpha, `typeIR~param~` and `typeIR~arg~` are the same type>>.
  ... Check that <<Expr_lvalue_ok, `p TC |- typedExpressionIR~arg~`>>.
  ... Result in `typedExpressionIR~arg~`.
. Else if `direction` matches pattern ``EMPTY`:
 .. Group empty:
  ... If `actctxt` matches pattern `ACTION`:
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR^?^` be <<coerce_unary, implicitly cast  `typedExpressionIR~arg~`  to  `typeIR~param~`>>.
   .... Check that `typedExpressionIR^?^` is Some value.
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR~arg_cast~` be `typedExpressionIR^?^`.
   .... Result in `typedExpressionIR~arg_cast~`.
  ... Else `actctxt` matches pattern `NOACTION`:
   .... Let `typeIR~arg~` be <<type_of_typedExpressionIR, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~arg~`>>.
   .... Let `ctk~arg~` be <<ctk_of_typedExpressionIR, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~arg~`>>.
   .... Check that <<Type_alpha, `typeIR~param~` and `typeIR~arg~` are the same type>>.
   .... Check that `ctk~arg~` does not match pattern `DYN`.
   .... Result in `typedExpressionIR~arg~`.


relation Call_convention_argument_ok: `p`, `TC`, `actctxt`, `parameterTypeIR`, and `argumentIR`


. Check that `argumentIR` has type `typedExpressionIR`.
. Let `typedExpressionIR` be `argumentIR`.
. Group typedExpression:
 .. Let `typedExpressionIR~cast~` be the result of <<Call_convention_expr_ok, checking the calling convention of `typedExpressionIR` applied to parameter type `parameterTypeIR`, under cursor `p`, typing context `TC`, and action context `actctxt`>>.
 .. Result in `typedExpressionIR~cast~`.
. If let `nameIR = typedExpressionIR` be `argumentIR`:
 .. Group nameIR-typedExpression:
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~cast~` be the result of <<Call_convention_expr_ok, checking the calling convention of `typedExpressionIR` applied to parameter type `parameterTypeIR`, under cursor `p`, typing context `TC`, and action context `actctxt`>>.
  ... Result in `nameIR = typedExpressionIR~cast~`.
. Else if let `nameIR = _` be `argumentIR`:
 .. Group nameIR-dontcare:
  ... Let `direction` be the direction of `parameterTypeIR`.
  ... Check that `direction` matches pattern `OUT`.
  ... Result in `nameIR = _`.
. Else if `argumentIR` matches pattern `_`:
 .. Group dontcare:
  ... Let `direction` be the direction of `parameterTypeIR`.
  ... Check that `direction` matches pattern `OUT`.
  ... Result in `_`.


relation Call_convention_ok: `p`, `TC`, `actctxt`, `parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^`, and `argumentIR^{asterisk}^`


. If `parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^` is an empty list:
 .. Check that `argumentIR^{asterisk}^` is an empty list.
 .. Group nil:
  ... Result in `[ ]`.
. Else let `parameterTypeIR~h~ {two-colons} parameterTypeIR~t~^{asterisk}^` be `parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^`:
 .. Check that `argumentIR^{asterisk}^` is a non-empty list.
 .. Let `argumentIR~h~ {two-colons} argumentIR~t~^{asterisk}^` be `argumentIR^{asterisk}^`.
 .. Group cons:
  ... Let `argumentIR~h_cast~` be the result of <<Call_convention_argument_ok, checking the calling convention of `argumentIR~h~` applied to parameter type `parameterTypeIR~h~`, under cursor `p`, typing context `TC`, and action context `actctxt`>>.
  ... Let `argumentIR~t_cast~^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Call_convention_ok, checking the calling convention of `argumentIR~t~^{asterisk}^` applied to parameter types `parameterTypeIR~t~^{asterisk}^`, under cursor `p`, typing context `TC`, and action context `actctxt`>>.
  ... Result in `argumentIR~h_cast~ {two-colons} argumentIR~t_cast~^{asterisk}^`.


relation CallableTarget_ok: `p`, `TC`, and `callableTarget`


. Group referenceExpression:
 .. If let `prefixedNonTypeName` be `callableTarget`:
  ... Let `prefixedNameIR` be <<prefixedNonTypeName, the prefixed name of  `prefixedNonTypeName`>>.
  ... Check that `prefixedNameIR = "verify" \/ prefixedNameIR = . "verify"` *implies* `p = BLOCK /\ <<is_parser_blockKind, $is_parser_blockKind(TC.BLOCK.KIND)>> \/ p = LOCAL /\ <<is_parser_state_localKind, $is_parser_state_localKind(TC.LOCAL.KIND)>>`.
  ... Result in the typed callable target `prefixedNameIR`.
 .. Else if `callableTarget` is equal to `THIS`:
  ... Result in the typed callable target `"this"`.
. If let `memberAccessBase . member` be `callableTarget`:
 .. Group memberAccessExpression:
  ... If let `prefixedTypeName` be `memberAccessBase`:
   .... Let `prefixedNameIR` be <<prefixedTypeName, the prefixed name of  `prefixedTypeName`>>.
   .... Let `nameIR` be <<name, the name of `member`>>.
   .... Result in the typed callable target `TYPE prefixedNameIR . nameIR`.
  ... Else let `expression~base~` be `memberAccessBase`:
   .... Let `nameIR` be <<name, the name of `member`>>.
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR~base~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~base~`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Result in the typed callable target `typedExpressionIR~base~ . nameIR`.
. Else if let `( expression )` be `callableTarget`:
 .. Group parenthesizedExpression:
  ... Let `callableTargetIR` be the result of <<CallableTarget_ok, typing `expression`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Result in the typed callable target `( callableTargetIR )`.


relation CallableTarget_lvalue_ok: `p`, `TC`, and `lvalue`


. Group :
 .. Let `expression` be <<lvalue_as_expression, the expression corresponding to `lvalue`>>.
 .. Let `callableTargetIR` be the result of <<CallableTarget_ok, typing `expression`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC`>>.
 .. Result in the typed callable target `callableTargetIR`.


relation CallableType_ok: `p`, `TC`, `callableTargetIR''`, `typeArgumentIR''^{asterisk}^`, and `argumentIR''^{asterisk}^`


. Check that `callableTargetIR''` has type `prefixedNameIR`.
. Let `prefixedNameIR` be `callableTargetIR''`.
. Group referenceExpressionIR:
 .. If `typeArgumentIR''^{asterisk}^` is equal to `[ ]`:
  ... Let `(cid, callableTypeDefIR, id*)'^?^` be `<<find_callableDef_overloaded_t, $find_callableDef_overloaded_t(p, TC, prefixedNameIR, argumentIR''^{asterisk}^)>>`.
  ... Check that `(cid, callableTypeDefIR, id*)'^?^` is Some value.
  ... Let `(cid, callableTypeDefIR, id*)` be `(cid, callableTypeDefIR, id*)'^?^`.
  ... Check that `(cid, callableTypeDefIR, id*)` has type `(cid, actionTypeIR, id*)`.
  ... Let `(cid, actionTypeIR, id~default~^{asterisk}^)` be `(cid, callableTypeDefIR, id*)`.
  ... Check that <<CallableType_wf, `actionTypeIR` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `$bound(p, TC)`>>.
  ... Result in `actionTypeIR`, `[ ]`, and `id~default~^{asterisk}^`.
 .. Let `typeArgumentIR^{asterisk}^` be `typeArgumentIR''^{asterisk}^`.
 .. Let `(cid, callableTypeDefIR, id*)'^?^` be `<<find_callableDef_overloaded_t, $find_callableDef_overloaded_t(p, TC, prefixedNameIR, argumentIR''^{asterisk}^)>>`.
 .. Else if let `(cid, callableTypeDefIR, id*)` be `(cid, callableTypeDefIR, id*)'^?^`:
  ... Check that `(cid, callableTypeDefIR, id*)` has type `(cid, functionTypeDefIR, id*)`.
  ... Let `(cid, functionTypeDefIR, id~default~^{asterisk}^)` be `(cid, callableTypeDefIR, id*)`.
  ... Let `(callableTypeIR, tid*)` be `<<specialize_callableTypeDefIR, $specialize_callableTypeDefIR(functionTypeDefIR, typeArgumentIR^{asterisk}^)>>`.
  ... Check that `(callableTypeIR, tid*)` has type `(functionTypeIR, tid*)`.
  ... Let `(functionTypeIR, tid~impl~^{asterisk}^)` be `(callableTypeIR, tid*)`.
  ... Let `bound'` be `<<bound, $bound(p, TC)>>`.
  ... Let `bound` be <<union_set, the union of the sets `bound'` and `{ tid~impl~^{asterisk}^ }`>>.
  ... Check that <<CallableType_wf, `functionTypeIR` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `bound`>>.
  ... Result in `functionTypeIR`, `tid~impl~^{asterisk}^`, and `id~default~^{asterisk}^`.
. If let `typedExpressionIR~base~ . nameIR` be `callableTargetIR''`:
 .. Else if `typeArgumentIR''^{asterisk}^` is an empty list:
  ... If `argumentIR''^{asterisk}^` is an empty list:
   .... Group typedExpressionIR-nameIR-builtin-method-minmax-SizeIn-BitsBytes:
    ..... Check that `nameIR` is in `["minSizeInBits", "minSizeInBytes", "maxSizeInBits", "maxSizeInBytes"]`.
    ..... Let `methodTypeIR` be `BUILTIN_METHOD ( [ ] ) : INT`.
    ..... Result in `methodTypeIR`, `[ ]`, and `[ ]`.
   .... Group typedExpressionIR-nameIR-builtin-method-header-isValid:
    ..... Check that `nameIR` is in `["isValid"]`.
    ..... Let `typeIR~base~` be <<type_of_typedExpressionIR, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~base~`>>.
    ..... Let `typeIR` be <<canon_typeIR, the canonicalized form of `typeIR~base~`>>.
    ..... Check that `typeIR` has type `headerTypeIR`.
    ..... Let `HEADER ++_++ { ++_++^{asterisk}^ }` be `typeIR`.
    ..... Let `methodTypeIR` be `BUILTIN_METHOD ( [ ] ) : BOOL`.
    ..... Result in `methodTypeIR`, `[ ]`, and `[ ]`.
   .... Group typedExpressionIR-nameIR-builtin-method-union-isValid:
    ..... Check that `nameIR` is in `["isValid"]`.
    ..... Let `typeIR~base~` be <<type_of_typedExpressionIR, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~base~`>>.
    ..... Let `typeIR` be <<canon_typeIR, the canonicalized form of `typeIR~base~`>>.
    ..... Check that `typeIR` has type `headerUnionTypeIR`.
    ..... Let `HEADER_UNION ++_++ { ++_++^{asterisk}^ }` be `typeIR`.
    ..... Let `methodTypeIR` be `BUILTIN_METHOD ( [ ] ) : BOOL`.
    ..... Result in `methodTypeIR`, `[ ]`, and `[ ]`.
   .... Group typedExpressionIR-nameIR-builtin-method-header-set-ValidInvalid:
    ..... Check that `nameIR` is in `["setValid", "setInvalid"]`.
    ..... Let `typeIR~base~` be <<type_of_typedExpressionIR, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~base~`>>.
    ..... Let `typeIR` be <<canon_typeIR, the canonicalized form of `typeIR~base~`>>.
    ..... Check that `typeIR` has type `headerTypeIR`.
    ..... Let `HEADER ++_++ { ++_++^{asterisk}^ }` be `typeIR`.
    ..... Let `methodTypeIR` be `BUILTIN_METHOD ( [ ] ) : VOID`.
    ..... Result in `methodTypeIR`, `[ ]`, and `[ ]`.
  ... Else if let `[argumentIR]` be `argumentIR''^{asterisk}^`:
   .... Group typedExpressionIR-nameIR-builtin-method-stack-push-pop-front:
    ..... Check that `nameIR` is in `["push_front", "pop_front"]`.
    ..... Let `typeIR~base~` be <<type_of_typedExpressionIR, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~base~`>>.
    ..... Let `typeIR'` be <<canon_typeIR, the canonicalized form of `typeIR~base~`>>.
    ..... Check that `typeIR'` has type `headerStackTypeIR`.
    ..... Let `typeIR [ ++_++ ]` be `typeIR'`.
    ..... Let `parameterTypeIR` be `INT "count" None`.
    ..... Let `methodTypeIR` be `BUILTIN_METHOD ( [parameterTypeIR] ) : INT`.
    ..... Result in `methodTypeIR`, `[ ]`, and `[ ]`.
 .. Group typedExpressionIR-nameIR-extern-method:
  ... Let `typeIR~base~` be <<type_of_typedExpressionIR, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~base~`>>.
  ... Let `typeIR` be <<canon_typeIR, the canonicalized form of `typeIR~base~`>>.
  ... Check that `typeIR` has type `externObjectTypeIR`.
  ... Let `EXTERN ++_++ { (cid~extern~ : externMethodTypeDefIR~extern~)^{asterisk}^ }` be `typeIR`.
  ... Let `(id~arg~^?^)^{asterisk}^` be `<<ids_arguments, $ids_arguments(argumentIR''^{asterisk}^)>>`.
  ... Let `(cid, externMethodTypeDefIR, id*)^?^` be `<<find_overloaded, $find_overloaded<externMethodTypeDefIR>({ (cid~extern~ : externMethodTypeDefIR~extern~)^{asterisk}^ }, nameIR, (id~arg~^?^)^{asterisk}^)>>`.
  ... Check that `(cid, externMethodTypeDefIR, id*)^?^` is Some value.
  ... Let `(++_++, externMethodTypeDefIR, id~default~^{asterisk}^)` be `(cid, externMethodTypeDefIR, id*)^?^`.
  ... Let `(callableTypeIR, tid*)` be `<<specialize_callableTypeDefIR, $specialize_callableTypeDefIR(externMethodTypeDefIR, typeArgumentIR''^{asterisk}^)>>`.
  ... Check that `(callableTypeIR, tid*)` has type `(externMethodTypeIR, tid*)`.
  ... Let `(externMethodTypeIR, tid~impl~^{asterisk}^)` be `(callableTypeIR, tid*)`.
  ... Let `bound'` be `<<bound, $bound(p, TC)>>`.
  ... Let `bound` be <<union_set, the union of the sets `bound'` and `{ tid~impl~^{asterisk}^ }`>>.
  ... Check that <<CallableType_wf, `externMethodTypeIR` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `bound`>>.
  ... Result in `externMethodTypeIR`, `tid~impl~^{asterisk}^`, and `id~default~^{asterisk}^`.
 .. Else if `nameIR` is equal to `"apply"`:
  ... Check that `typeArgumentIR''^{asterisk}^` is an empty list.
  ... Group typedExpressionIR-nameIR-parser-apply-method:
   .... Let `typeIR~base~` be <<type_of_typedExpressionIR, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~base~`>>.
   .... Let `typeIR` be <<canon_typeIR, the canonicalized form of `typeIR~base~`>>.
   .... Check that `typeIR` has type `parserObjectTypeIR`.
   .... Let `PARSER ( parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^ )` be `typeIR`.
   .... Let `parserApplyMethodTypeIR` be `PARSER_APPLY ( parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^ )`.
   .... Let `id~param~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `id~param~` and `value~param~^?^^{asterisk}^` be the list of `value~param~^?^`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
        * Let `id~param~` and `value~param~^?^` be the name and the default value of `parameterTypeIR`.
--
+
for each `parameterTypeIR` in `parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^`
   .... Let `pid^{asterisk}^` be the list of `pid`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
        * Let `pid` be `id~param~ # value~param~^?^ =/= None`.
--
+
for each `id~param~` in `id~param~^{asterisk}^` and `value~param~^?^` in `value~param~^?^^{asterisk}^`
   .... Let `cid` be `"apply" ( pid^{asterisk}^ )`.
   .... Let `(id~arg~^?^)^{asterisk}^` be `<<ids_arguments, $ids_arguments(argumentIR''^{asterisk}^)>>`.
   .... Let `(cid, parserApplyMethodTypeIR, id*)^?^` be `<<find_overloaded, $find_overloaded<parserApplyMethodTypeIR>({ [cid : parserApplyMethodTypeIR] }, "apply", (id~arg~^?^)^{asterisk}^)>>`.
   .... Check that `(cid, parserApplyMethodTypeIR, id*)^?^` is Some value.
   .... Let `(++_++, parserApplyMethodTypeIR', id~default~^{asterisk}^)` be `(cid, parserApplyMethodTypeIR, id*)^?^`.
   .... Check that `parserApplyMethodTypeIR'` is equal to `parserApplyMethodTypeIR`.
   .... Result in `parserApplyMethodTypeIR`, `[ ]`, and `id~default~^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Group typedExpressionIR-nameIR-control-apply-method:
   .... Let `typeIR~base~` be <<type_of_typedExpressionIR, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~base~`>>.
   .... Let `typeIR` be <<canon_typeIR, the canonicalized form of `typeIR~base~`>>.
   .... Check that `typeIR` has type `controlObjectTypeIR`.
   .... Let `CONTROL ( parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^ )` be `typeIR`.
   .... Let `controlApplyMethodTypeIR` be `CONTROL_APPLY ( parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^ )`.
   .... Let `id~param~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `id~param~` and `value~param~^?^^{asterisk}^` be the list of `value~param~^?^`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
        * Let `id~param~` and `value~param~^?^` be the name and the default value of `parameterTypeIR`.
--
+
for each `parameterTypeIR` in `parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^`
   .... Let `pid^{asterisk}^` be the list of `pid`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
        * Let `pid` be `id~param~ # value~param~^?^ =/= None`.
--
+
for each `id~param~` in `id~param~^{asterisk}^` and `value~param~^?^` in `value~param~^?^^{asterisk}^`
   .... Let `cid` be `"apply" ( pid^{asterisk}^ )`.
   .... Let `(id~arg~^?^)^{asterisk}^` be `<<ids_arguments, $ids_arguments(argumentIR''^{asterisk}^)>>`.
   .... Let `(cid, controlApplyMethodTypeDefIR, id*)^?^` be `<<find_overloaded, $find_overloaded<controlApplyMethodTypeDefIR>({ [cid : controlApplyMethodTypeIR] }, "apply", (id~arg~^?^)^{asterisk}^)>>`.
   .... Check that `(cid, controlApplyMethodTypeDefIR, id*)^?^` is Some value.
   .... Let `(++_++, controlApplyMethodTypeIR', id~default~^{asterisk}^)` be `(cid, controlApplyMethodTypeDefIR, id*)^?^`.
   .... Check that `controlApplyMethodTypeIR'` is equal to `controlApplyMethodTypeIR`.
   .... Result in `controlApplyMethodTypeIR`, `[ ]`, and `id~default~^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Check that `argumentIR''^{asterisk}^` is an empty list.
  ... Group typedExpressionIR-nameIR-table-apply-method:
   .... Let `typeIR~base~` be <<type_of_typedExpressionIR, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~base~`>>.
   .... Let `typeIR` be <<canon_typeIR, the canonicalized form of `typeIR~base~`>>.
   .... Check that `typeIR` has type `tableObjectTypeIR`.
   .... Let `TABLE ++_++ { tableMetadataStructTypeIR }` be `typeIR`.
   .... Let `tableApplyMethodTypeIR` be `TABLE_APPLY : tableMetadataStructTypeIR`.
   .... Result in `tableApplyMethodTypeIR`, `[ ]`, and `[ ]`.
. Else if let `( callableTargetIR )` be `callableTargetIR''`:
 .. Group parenthesized:
  ... Let <<CallableType_ok, `p TC |- callableTargetIR < typeArgumentIR''^{asterisk}^ > ( argumentIR''^{asterisk}^ ) : callableTypeIR < # tid~inserted~^{asterisk}^ > ( # id~default~^{asterisk}^ )`>>.
  ... Result in `callableTypeIR`, `tid~inserted~^{asterisk}^`, and `id~default~^{asterisk}^`.


relation Call_ok: `p`, `TC`, `callableTypeIR`, `typeArgumentIR^{asterisk}^`, `tid'^{asterisk}^`, `argumentIR^{asterisk}^`, and `id~default'~^{asterisk}^`


. If let `ACTION ( parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^ )` be `callableTypeIR`:
 .. Check that `typeArgumentIR^{asterisk}^` is an empty list.
 .. Check that `tid'^{asterisk}^` is an empty list.
 .. Group action:
  ... Let `parameterTypeIR~non_default~^{asterisk}^` be `<<filter_default_parameterTypeIRs, $filter_default_parameterTypeIRs(parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^, id~default'~^{asterisk}^)>>`.
  ... Check that the length of `parameterTypeIR~non_default~^{asterisk}^` is equal to the length of `argumentIR^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Let `parameterTypeIR~aligned~^{asterisk}^` be `<<align_parameterTypeIRs, $align_parameterTypeIRs(parameterTypeIR~non_default~^{asterisk}^, argumentIR^{asterisk}^)>>`.
  ... Check that `<<callable_action, $callable_action(p, TC)>>`.
  ... Let `argumentIR~cast~^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Call_convention_ok, checking the calling convention of `argumentIR^{asterisk}^` applied to parameter types `parameterTypeIR~aligned~^{asterisk}^`, under cursor `p`, typing context `TC`, and action context `ACTION`>>.
  ... Result in `VOID`, `[ ]`, and `argumentIR~cast~^{asterisk}^`.
. Else if let `FUNCTION ( parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^ ) : typeIR~ret~` be `callableTypeIR`:
 .. Group definedFunctionTypeIR:
  ... Let `parameterTypeIR~non_default~^{asterisk}^` be `<<filter_default_parameterTypeIRs, $filter_default_parameterTypeIRs(parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^, id~default'~^{asterisk}^)>>`.
  ... Check that the length of `parameterTypeIR~non_default~^{asterisk}^` is equal to the length of `argumentIR^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Let `parameterTypeIR~aligned~^{asterisk}^` be `<<align_parameterTypeIRs, $align_parameterTypeIRs(parameterTypeIR~non_default~^{asterisk}^, argumentIR^{asterisk}^)>>`.
  ... Let `inference` be `<<infer, $infer(tid'^{asterisk}^, parameterTypeIR~aligned~^{asterisk}^, argumentIR^{asterisk}^)>>`.
  ... Let `typeIR^?^^{asterisk}^` be the list of `typeIR^?^`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
      * Let `typeIR^?^` be `<<find_map, $find_map<tid, typeIR>(inference, tid')>>`.
--
+
for each `tid'` in `tid'^{asterisk}^`
  ... Check that `typeIR^?^` is Some value, for all `typeIR^?^` in `typeIR^?^^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Let `typeIR~inferred~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `typeIR~inferred~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
      * Let `typeIR~inferred~` be `typeIR^?^`.
--
+
for each `typeIR^?^` in `typeIR^?^^{asterisk}^`
  ... Let `typeArgumentIR~inferred~^{asterisk}^` be `typeArgumentIR^{asterisk}^ {pp} typeIR~inferred~^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Let `parameterTypeIR~aligned_inferred~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `parameterTypeIR~aligned_inferred~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
      * Let `parameterTypeIR~aligned_inferred~` be `<<subst_parameterTypeIR, $subst_parameterTypeIR(inference, parameterTypeIR~aligned~)>>`.
--
+
for each `parameterTypeIR~aligned~` in `parameterTypeIR~aligned~^{asterisk}^`
  ... Let `typeIR~ret_inferred~` be `<<subst_typeIR, $subst_typeIR(inference, typeIR~ret~)>>`.
  ... Let `functionTypeIR~inferred~` be `FUNCTION ( parameterTypeIR~aligned_inferred~^{asterisk}^ ) : typeIR~ret_inferred~`.
  ... Check that <<CallableType_wf, `functionTypeIR~inferred~` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `$bound(p, TC)`>>.
  ... Check that `<<callable_definedFunction, $callable_definedFunction(p, TC)>>`.
  ... Let `argumentIR~cast~^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Call_convention_ok, checking the calling convention of `argumentIR^{asterisk}^` applied to parameter types `parameterTypeIR~aligned_inferred~^{asterisk}^`, under cursor `p`, typing context `TC`, and action context `NOACTION`>>.
  ... Result in `typeIR~ret_inferred~`, `typeArgumentIR~inferred~^{asterisk}^`, and `argumentIR~cast~^{asterisk}^`.
. Else if let `EXTERN_FUNCTION ( parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^ ) : typeIR~ret~` be `callableTypeIR`:
 .. Group externFunctionTypeIR:
  ... Let `parameterTypeIR~non_default~^{asterisk}^` be `<<filter_default_parameterTypeIRs, $filter_default_parameterTypeIRs(parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^, id~default'~^{asterisk}^)>>`.
  ... Check that the length of `parameterTypeIR~non_default~^{asterisk}^` is equal to the length of `argumentIR^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Let `parameterTypeIR~aligned~^{asterisk}^` be `<<align_parameterTypeIRs, $align_parameterTypeIRs(parameterTypeIR~non_default~^{asterisk}^, argumentIR^{asterisk}^)>>`.
  ... Let `inference` be `<<infer, $infer(tid'^{asterisk}^, parameterTypeIR~aligned~^{asterisk}^, argumentIR^{asterisk}^)>>`.
  ... Let `typeIR^?^^{asterisk}^` be the list of `typeIR^?^`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
      * Let `typeIR^?^` be `<<find_map, $find_map<tid, typeIR>(inference, tid')>>`.
--
+
for each `tid'` in `tid'^{asterisk}^`
  ... Check that `typeIR^?^` is Some value, for all `typeIR^?^` in `typeIR^?^^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Let `typeIR~inferred~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `typeIR~inferred~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
      * Let `typeIR~inferred~` be `typeIR^?^`.
--
+
for each `typeIR^?^` in `typeIR^?^^{asterisk}^`
  ... Let `typeArgumentIR~inferred~^{asterisk}^` be `typeArgumentIR^{asterisk}^ {pp} typeIR~inferred~^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Let `parameterTypeIR~aligned_inferred~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `parameterTypeIR~aligned_inferred~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
      * Let `parameterTypeIR~aligned_inferred~` be `<<subst_parameterTypeIR, $subst_parameterTypeIR(inference, parameterTypeIR~aligned~)>>`.
--
+
for each `parameterTypeIR~aligned~` in `parameterTypeIR~aligned~^{asterisk}^`
