relation Inst_ok: `cursor'`, `TC`, `instctxt`, `constructorTypeIR`, `typeArgumentIR^{asterisk}^`, `tid~infer~^{asterisk}^`, `argumentIR^{asterisk}^`, and `id~default~^{asterisk}^`


. Check that `cursor'` matches pattern `GLOBAL`.
. Group package:
 .. Let `CONSTRUCTOR ( parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^ ) : typeIR~object~` be `constructorTypeIR`.
 .. Let `typeIR` be <<canon_typeIR, the canonicalized form of `typeIR~object~`>>.
 .. Check that `typeIR` has type `packageObjectTypeIR`.
 .. Let `PACKAGE { ++_++^{asterisk}^ }` be `typeIR`.
 .. Let `parameterTypeIR~non_default~^{asterisk}^` be `<<filter_default_parameterTypeIRs, $filter_default_parameterTypeIRs(parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^, id~default~^{asterisk}^)>>`.
 .. Check that the length of `parameterTypeIR~non_default~^{asterisk}^` is equal to the length of `argumentIR^{asterisk}^`.
 .. Let `parameterTypeIR~aligned~^{asterisk}^` be `<<align_parameterTypeIRs, $align_parameterTypeIRs(parameterTypeIR~non_default~^{asterisk}^, argumentIR^{asterisk}^)>>`.
 .. Let `inference` be `<<infer, $infer(tid~infer~^{asterisk}^, parameterTypeIR~aligned~^{asterisk}^, argumentIR^{asterisk}^)>>`.
 .. Let `typeIR'^?^^{asterisk}^` be the list of `typeIR'^?^`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
    * Let `typeIR'^?^` be `<<find_map, $find_map<tid, typeIR>(inference, tid~infer~)>>`.
--
+
for each `tid~infer~` in `tid~infer~^{asterisk}^`
 .. Check that `typeIR'^?^` is Some value, for all `typeIR'^?^` in `typeIR'^?^^{asterisk}^`.
 .. Let `typeIR~inferred~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `typeIR~inferred~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
    * Let `typeIR~inferred~` be `typeIR'^?^`.
--
+
for each `typeIR'^?^` in `typeIR'^?^^{asterisk}^`
 .. Let `typeArgumentIR~inferred~^{asterisk}^` be `typeArgumentIR^{asterisk}^ {pp} typeIR~inferred~^{asterisk}^`.
 .. Let `parameterTypeIR~aligned_inferred~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `parameterTypeIR~aligned_inferred~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
    * Let `parameterTypeIR~aligned_inferred~` be `<<subst_parameterTypeIR, $subst_parameterTypeIR(inference, parameterTypeIR~aligned~)>>`.
--
+
for each `parameterTypeIR~aligned~` in `parameterTypeIR~aligned~^{asterisk}^`
 .. Let `typeIR~object_inferred~` be `<<subst_typeIR, $subst_typeIR(inference, typeIR~object~)>>`.
 .. Let `constructorTypeIR~inferred~` be `CONSTRUCTOR ( parameterTypeIR~aligned_inferred~^{asterisk}^ ) : typeIR~object_inferred~`.
 .. Check that <<ConstructorType_wf, `constructorTypeIR~inferred~` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `$bound(GLOBAL, TC)`>>.
 .. Check that `<<instantiable, $instantiable(GLOBAL, TC, instctxt, typeIR~object_inferred~)>>`.
 .. Let `argumentIR~cast~^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Call_convention_ok, checking the calling convention of `argumentIR^{asterisk}^` applied to parameter types `parameterTypeIR~aligned_inferred~^{asterisk}^`, under cursor `BLOCK`, typing context `TC`, and action context `NOACTION`>>.
 .. Result in `typeIR~object_inferred~`, `typeArgumentIR~inferred~^{asterisk}^`, and `argumentIR~cast~^{asterisk}^`.
. Group non-package:
 .. Let `CONSTRUCTOR ( parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^ ) : typeIR~object~` be `constructorTypeIR`.
 .. Check that `~<<is_packageObjectTypeIR, $is_packageObjectTypeIR($canon_typeIR(typeIR~object~))>>`.
 .. Let `parameterTypeIR~non_default~^{asterisk}^` be `<<filter_default_parameterTypeIRs, $filter_default_parameterTypeIRs(parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^, id~default~^{asterisk}^)>>`.
 .. Check that the length of `parameterTypeIR~non_default~^{asterisk}^` is equal to the length of `argumentIR^{asterisk}^`.
 .. Let `parameterTypeIR~aligned~^{asterisk}^` be `<<align_parameterTypeIRs, $align_parameterTypeIRs(parameterTypeIR~non_default~^{asterisk}^, argumentIR^{asterisk}^)>>`.
 .. Let `inference` be `<<infer, $infer(tid~infer~^{asterisk}^, parameterTypeIR~aligned~^{asterisk}^, argumentIR^{asterisk}^)>>`.
 .. Let `typeIR^?^^{asterisk}^` be the list of `typeIR^?^`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
    * Let `typeIR^?^` be `<<find_map, $find_map<tid, typeIR>(inference, tid~infer~)>>`.
--
+
for each `tid~infer~` in `tid~infer~^{asterisk}^`
 .. Check that `typeIR^?^` is Some value, for all `typeIR^?^` in `typeIR^?^^{asterisk}^`.
 .. Let `typeIR~inferred~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `typeIR~inferred~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
    * Let `typeIR~inferred~` be `typeIR^?^`.
--
+
for each `typeIR^?^` in `typeIR^?^^{asterisk}^`
 .. Let `typeArgumentIR~inferred~^{asterisk}^` be `typeArgumentIR^{asterisk}^ {pp} typeIR~inferred~^{asterisk}^`.
 .. Let `parameterTypeIR~aligned_inferred~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `parameterTypeIR~aligned_inferred~`, obtained by repeating:
