relation SwitchLabel_table_ok: `TC`, `tid~table~`, `bool`, and `switchLabel`


. Group :
 .. If `bool` is equal to `true`:
  ... Check that `switchLabel` matches pattern `DEFAULT`.
  ... Result in `DEFAULT`.
 .. Else if let `prefixedNonTypeName` be `switchLabel`:
  ... Let `prefixedNameIR` be <<prefixedNonTypeName, the prefixed name of  `prefixedNonTypeName`>>.
  ... Check that `prefixedNameIR` matches pattern `` %`.
  ... Let `nameIR~label~` be `prefixedNameIR`.
  ... Let `tid~table_enum~` be `"action_list(" {pp} tid~table~ {pp} ")"`.
  ... Let `id~label~` be `tid~table_enum~ {pp} "." {pp} nameIR~label~`.
  ... Let `varTypeIR^?^` be `<<find_var_t, $find_var_t(LOCAL, TC, id~label~)>>`.
  ... Check that `varTypeIR^?^` is Some value.
  ... Let `++_++ typeIR~label~ ctk~label~ value^?^` be `varTypeIR^?^`.
  ... Check that `value^?^` is Some value.
  ... Let `value~label~` be `value^?^`.
  ... Check that `value~label~` is equal to `TABLE_ENUM tid~table_enum~ . nameIR~label~`.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~label~` be <<typedExpressionIR, `nameIR~label~` annotated with type `typeIR~label~` and compile-time known-ness `ctk~label~`>>.
  ... Result in `typedExpressionIR~label~`.


relation SwitchCase_table_ok: `TC`, `f`, `tid~table~`, `b~last~`, and `switchCase`


. Group :
 .. If let `switchLabel : blockStatement` be `switchCase`:
  ... Let <<SwitchLabel_table_ok, `TC tid~table~ b~last~ |- switchLabel : switchLabelIR`>>.
  ... Let `TC~post~`, `f~post~`, and `blockStatementIR` be the result of <<Block_ok, typing `blockStatement`, under typing context `TC` and abstract control flow `f`>>.
  ... Let `switchCaseIR` be `switchLabelIR : blockStatementIR`.
  ... Result in `f~post~`, `switchCaseIR`, and `switchLabel`.
 .. Else let `switchLabel :` be `switchCase`:
  ... Let <<SwitchLabel_table_ok, `TC tid~table~ b~last~ |- switchLabel : switchLabelIR`>>.
  ... Let `switchCaseIR` be `switchLabelIR :`.
  ... Result in `f`, `switchCaseIR`, and `switchLabel`.


relation SwitchCases_table_ok: `TC`, `f`, `tid~table~`, and `switchCase^{asterisk}^`


. If `switchCase^{asterisk}^` is an empty list:
 .. Group nil:
  ... Result in `f`, `[ ]`, and `[ ]`.
. Else let `switchCase~h~ {two-colons} switchCase~t~^{asterisk}^` be `switchCase^{asterisk}^`:
 .. Group cons:
  ... Let `b~last~` be `switchCase~t~^{asterisk}^` is equal to `[ ]`.
  ... Let <<SwitchCase_table_ok, `TC f tid~table~ b~last~ |- switchCase~h~ : f~h~ switchCaseIR~h~ # switchLabel~h~`>>.
  ... Let <<SwitchCases_table_ok, `TC f~h~ tid~table~ |- switchCase~t~^{asterisk}^ : f~t~ switchCaseIR~t~^{asterisk}^ # switchLabel~t~^{asterisk}^`>>.
  ... Result in `f~t~`, `switchCaseIR~h~ {two-colons} switchCaseIR~t~^{asterisk}^`, and `switchLabel~h~ {two-colons} switchLabel~t~^{asterisk}^`.


relation SwitchLabel_general_ok: `TC`, `typeIR`, `bool`, and `switchLabel`


. Group :
 .. If `bool` is equal to `true`:
  ... Check that `switchLabel` matches pattern `DEFAULT`.
  ... Result in `DEFAULT`.
 .. Else if let `expressionNonBrace~label~` be `switchLabel`:
  ... Let `expression~label~` be <<expressionNonBrace_as_expression, the expression corresponding to `expressionNonBrace~label~`>>.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~label~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~label~`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR^?^` be <<coerce_unary, implicitly cast  `typedExpressionIR~label~`  to  `typeIR`>>.
  ... Check that `typedExpressionIR^?^` is Some value.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~label_cast~` be `typedExpressionIR^?^`.
  ... Let <<expressionNoteIR, type `++_++` and compile-time known-ness `ctk`>> be the note of `typedExpressionIR~label_cast~`.
  ... Check that `ctk` matches pattern `LCTK`.
  ... Result in `typedExpressionIR~label_cast~`.


