relation Decl_object_ok: `p`, `TC~0~`, `typeFrame`, `externMethodTypeDefEnv`, and `objectDeclaration`


. If let `annotationList typeOrVoid name typeParameterListOpt ( parameterList ) blockStatement` be `objectDeclaration`:
 .. Group functionDeclaration:
  ... Let `TC~1~` be `TC~0~[BLOCK.KIND = EXTERN]`.
  ... Let `TC~2~` be `TC~1~[BLOCK.FRAME = typeFrame]`.
  ... Let `typeParameter^{asterisk}^` be <<flatten_typeParameterListOpt, the list of type parameters in `typeParameterListOpt`>>.
  ... Let `tid~expl~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `tid~expl~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
      * Let `tid~expl~` be <<name, the name of `typeParameter`>>.
--
+
for each `typeParameter` in `typeParameter^{asterisk}^`
  ... Let `TC~3~` be `<<add_typeDefs_t, $add_typeDefs_t(LOCAL, TC~2~, tid~expl~^{asterisk}^, (tid~expl~)^{asterisk}^)>>`.
  ... Let `typeIR~ret~` and `tid^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Type_ok, typing `typeOrVoid`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC~3~`>>.
  ... Check that `tid^{asterisk}^` is an empty list.
  ... Let `parameter^{asterisk}^` be <<flatten_parameterList, the list of parameters in `parameterList`>>.
  ... Let `parameterIR^{asterisk}^` and `tid~impl~^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Parameters_ok, typing `parameter^{asterisk}^`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC~3~`>>.
  ... Let `parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^` be the list of `parameterTypeIR`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
      * Let `parameterTypeIR` be <<type_of_parameterIR, the type of  `parameterIR`>>.
--
+
for each `parameterIR` in `parameterIR^{asterisk}^`
  ... Let `TC~4~` be `<<add_parameters_t, $add_parameters_t(LOCAL, TC~3~, parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^)>>`.
  ... Let `TC~5~` be `TC~4~[LOCAL.KIND = EXTERN_METHOD : typeIR~ret~]`.
  ... Let `++_++`, `f`, and `blockStatementIR` be the result of <<Block_ok, typing `blockStatement`, under typing context `TC~5~` and abstract control flow `CONT`>>.
  ... Else if `f` matches pattern `RET`:
   .... Let `cid` be `<<cid, $cid(name, parameterList)>>`.
   .... Let `externMethodTypeDefIR` be `EXTERN_METHOD < tid~expl~^{asterisk}^ , tid~impl~^{asterisk}^ > ( parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^ ) : typeIR~ret~`.
   .... Check that <<CallableTypeDef_wf, `externMethodTypeDefIR` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `$bound(p, TC~0~)`>>.
   .... Let `externMethodTypeDefEnv~init~` be <<update_map, the map `externMethodTypeDefEnv` with the value for key `cid` updated to `externMethodTypeDefIR`>>.
   .... Let `nameIR` be <<name, the name of `name`>>.
   .... Let `functionDeclarationIR` be `annotationList typeIR~ret~ nameIR < tid~expl~^{asterisk}^ , tid~impl~^{asterisk}^ > ( parameterIR^{asterisk}^ ) blockStatementIR`.
   .... Result in `typeFrame`, `externMethodTypeDefEnv~init~`, and `functionDeclarationIR`.
  ... Else if `typeIR~ret~` is equal to `VOID`:
   .... Let `cid` be `<<cid, $cid(name, parameterList)>>`.
   .... Let `externMethodTypeDefIR` be `EXTERN_METHOD < tid~expl~^{asterisk}^ , tid~impl~^{asterisk}^ > ( parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^ ) : typeIR~ret~`.
   .... Check that <<CallableTypeDef_wf, `externMethodTypeDefIR` is a well-formed type, assuming bound type ids `$bound(p, TC~0~)`>>.
   .... Let `externMethodTypeDefEnv~init~` be <<update_map, the map `externMethodTypeDefEnv` with the value for key `cid` updated to `externMethodTypeDefIR`>>.
   .... Let `nameIR` be <<name, the name of `name`>>.
   .... Let `functionDeclarationIR` be `annotationList typeIR~ret~ nameIR < tid~expl~^{asterisk}^ , tid~impl~^{asterisk}^ > ( parameterIR^{asterisk}^ ) blockStatementIR`.
   .... Result in `typeFrame`, `externMethodTypeDefEnv~init~`, and `functionDeclarationIR`.
. Else let `instantiation` be `objectDeclaration`:
 .. Group instantiation:
  ... Let `TC~1~` and `declarationIR` be the result of <<Decl_ok, typing `instantiation`, under cursor `p` and typing context `TC~0~`>>.
  ... Check that `declarationIR` has type `instantiationIR`.
  ... Let `instantiationIR` be `declarationIR`.
  ... Let `++_++ ++_++ ++_++ < ++_++ > ( ++_++ ) nameIR ++_++ ;` be `instantiationIR`.
  ... Let `varTypeIR'^?^` be `<<find_var_t, $find_var_t(p, TC~1~, nameIR)>>`.
  ... Check that `varTypeIR'^?^` is Some value.
  ... Let `varTypeIR` be `varTypeIR'^?^`.
  ... Let `typeFrame~init~` be <<update_map, the map `typeFrame` with the value for key `nameIR` updated to `varTypeIR`>>.
  ... Result in `typeFrame~init~`, `externMethodTypeDefEnv`, and `instantiationIR`.


relation Decls_object_ok: `p`, `TC`, `typeFrame'`, `externMethodTypeDefEnv'`, and `objectDeclaration^{asterisk}^`


. If `objectDeclaration^{asterisk}^` is an empty list:
 .. Group nil:
  ... Result in `typeFrame'`, `externMethodTypeDefEnv'`, and `[ ]`.
. Else let `objectDeclaration~h~ {two-colons} objectDeclaration~t~^{asterisk}^` be `objectDeclaration^{asterisk}^`:
 .. Group cons:
  ... Let <<Decl_object_ok, `p TC typeFrame' externMethodTypeDefEnv' |- objectDeclaration~h~ : typeFrame~1~ externMethodTypeDefEnv~1~ objectDeclarationIR~h~`>>.
  ... Let <<Decls_object_ok, `p TC typeFrame~1~ externMethodTypeDefEnv~1~ |- objectDeclaration~t~^{asterisk}^ : typeFrame~2~ externMethodTypeDefEnv~2~ objectDeclarationIR~t~^{asterisk}^`>>.
  ... Result in `typeFrame~2~`, `externMethodTypeDefEnv~2~`, and `objectDeclarationIR~h~ {two-colons} objectDeclarationIR~t~^{asterisk}^`.


relation Enum_serializable_field_ok: `TC~0~`, `nameIR~enum~`, `typeIR`, and `name = expression`


. Group :
 .. Let `typedExpressionIR` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression`, under cursor `BLOCK` and typing context `TC~0~`>>.
 .. Let `typedExpressionIR'^?^` be <<coerce_unary, implicitly cast  `typedExpressionIR`  to  `typeIR`>>.
 .. Check that `typedExpressionIR'^?^` is Some value.
 .. Let `typedExpressionIR~cast~` be `typedExpressionIR'^?^`.
 .. Check that `<<ctk_of_typedExpressionIR, $ctk_of_typedExpressionIR(typedExpressionIR~cast~)>>` matches pattern `LCTK`.
 .. Let `value` be the result of <<Expr_eval_lctk, the local compile-time evaluation of `typedExpressionIR~cast~`, under cursor `BLOCK` and typing context `TC~0~`>>.
 .. Let `nameIR` be <<name, the name of `name`>>.
 .. Let `enumTypeDefIR` be `ENUM nameIR~enum~ < typeIR > { [ ] }`.
 .. Let `value~enum~` be `nameIR~enum~ . nameIR . value`.
 .. Let `varTypeIR` be `enumTypeDefIR LCTK value~enum~`.
 .. Let `TC~1~` be <<add_var_t, the typing context `TC~0~` with a mapping from `nameIR` to `varTypeIR` added to the `BLOCK` layer>>.
 .. Result in `TC~1~`, `nameIR = typedExpressionIR~cast~`, and `value`.


relation Enum_serializable_fields_ok: `TC'`, `nameIR~enum~`, `typeIR`, and `namedExpression^{asterisk}^`


. If `namedExpression^{asterisk}^` is an empty list:
 .. Group nil:
  ... Result in `TC'`, `[ ]`, and `[ ]`.
. Else let `namedExpression~h~ {two-colons} namedExpression~t~^{asterisk}^` be `namedExpression^{asterisk}^`:
 .. Group cons:
  ... Let <<Enum_serializable_field_ok, `TC' nameIR~enum~ typeIR |- namedExpression~h~ : TC~1~ namedExpressionIR~h~ # value~field_h~`>>.
  ... Let <<Enum_serializable_fields_ok, `TC~1~ nameIR~enum~ typeIR |- namedExpression~t~^{asterisk}^ : TC~2~ namedExpressionIR~t~^{asterisk}^ # value~field_t~^{asterisk}^`>>.
  ... Let `namedExpressionIR^{asterisk}^` be `namedExpressionIR~h~ {two-colons} namedExpressionIR~t~^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Let `value~field~^{asterisk}^` be `value~field_h~ {two-colons} value~field_t~^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Result in `TC~2~`, `namedExpressionIR^{asterisk}^`, and `value~field~^{asterisk}^`.


relation SelectCase_keyset_simple_ok: `TC`, `typeIR~key~`, and `simpleKeysetExpression`


. Check that `simpleKeysetExpression` has type `expression`.
. Let `expression` be `simpleKeysetExpression`.
. Group expression-set-alpha:
 .. Let `typedExpressionIR` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC`>>.
 .. Let `typeIR` be <<type_of_typedExpressionIR, the type of  `typedExpressionIR`>>.
 .. Let `typeIR''` be <<canon_typeIR, the canonicalized form of `typeIR`>>.
 .. Check that `typeIR''` has type `setTypeIR`.
 .. Let `SET < typeIR'^{asterisk}^ >` be `typeIR''`.
 .. Check that `typeIR'^{asterisk}^` is a list of length 1.
 .. Let `[typeIR~base~]` be `typeIR'^{asterisk}^`.
 .. Check that <<Type_alpha, `typeIR~base~` and `typeIR~key~` are the same type>>.
 .. Result in `typedExpressionIR`.
. Group expression-set-subtype:
 .. Let `typedExpressionIR` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC`>>.
 .. Let `typeIR` be <<type_of_typedExpressionIR, the type of  `typedExpressionIR`>>.
 .. Let `typeIR''` be <<canon_typeIR, the canonicalized form of `typeIR`>>.
 .. Check that `typeIR''` has type `setTypeIR`.
 .. Let `SET < typeIR'^{asterisk}^ >` be `typeIR''`.
 .. Check that `typeIR'^{asterisk}^` is a list of length 1.
 .. Let `[typeIR~base~]` be `typeIR'^{asterisk}^`.
 .. Check that <<Type_alpha, `typeIR~base~` and `typeIR~key~` are not the same type>>.
 .. Check that <<Sub_impl, `typeIR~base~` can be implicitly cast to `typeIR~key~`>>.
 .. Let `typeIR~cast~` be `SET < [typeIR~key~] >`.
 .. Let `typedExpressionIR~cast~` be <<typedExpressionIR, `( typeIR~cast~ ) typedExpressionIR` annotated with type `typeIR~cast~` and compile-time known-ness `DYN`>>.
 .. Result in `typedExpressionIR~cast~`.
. Group expression-non-set:
 .. Let `typedExpressionIR` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC`>>.
 .. Let `typeIR` be <<type_of_typedExpressionIR, the type of  `typedExpressionIR`>>.
 .. Check that `~<<is_setTypeIR, $is_setTypeIR($canon_typeIR(typeIR))>>`.
 .. Check that <<Sub_impl, `typeIR` can be implicitly cast to `typeIR~key~`>>.
 .. Let `typeIR~cast~` be `SET < [typeIR~key~] >`.
 .. Let `typedExpressionIR~cast~` be <<typedExpressionIR, `( typeIR~cast~ ) typedExpressionIR` annotated with type `typeIR~cast~` and compile-time known-ness `DYN`>>.
 .. Result in `typedExpressionIR~cast~`.
. If let `expression~l~ &&& expression~r~` be `simpleKeysetExpression`:
 .. Group mask:
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~l~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~l~`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~r~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~r~`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)^?^` be <<coerce_binary, implicitly cast  `typedExpressionIR~l~`  and  `typedExpressionIR~r~`  to equal types>>.
  ... Check that `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)^?^` is Some value.
  ... Let `(typedExpressionIR~l_cast~, typedExpressionIR~r_cast~)` be `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)^?^`.
  ... Let `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)'^?^` be `<<reduce_serenum_binary, $reduce_serenum_binary(typedExpressionIR~l_cast~, typedExpressionIR~r_cast~, $compat_mask)>>`.
  ... Check that `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)'^?^` is Some value.
  ... Let `(typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~, typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~)` be `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)'^?^`.
  ... Let `typeIR~reduced~` be <<type_of_typedExpressionIR, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~`>>.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR^?^` be <<coerce_unary, implicitly cast  `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~`  to  `typeIR~key~`>>.
  ... Check that `typedExpressionIR^?^` is Some value.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~l_coerced~` be `typedExpressionIR^?^`.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR'^?^` be <<coerce_unary, implicitly cast  `typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~`  to  `typeIR~key~`>>.
  ... Check that `typedExpressionIR'^?^` is Some value.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~r_coerced~` be `typedExpressionIR'^?^`.
  ... Result in `typedExpressionIR~l_coerced~ &&& typedExpressionIR~r_coerced~`.
. Else if let `expression~l~ .. expression~r~` be `simpleKeysetExpression`:
 .. Group range:
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~l~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~l~`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~r~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~r~`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)^?^` be <<coerce_binary, implicitly cast  `typedExpressionIR~l~`  and  `typedExpressionIR~r~`  to equal types>>.
  ... Check that `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)^?^` is Some value.
  ... Let `(typedExpressionIR~l_cast~, typedExpressionIR~r_cast~)` be `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)^?^`.
  ... Let `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)'^?^` be `<<reduce_serenum_binary, $reduce_serenum_binary(typedExpressionIR~l_cast~, typedExpressionIR~r_cast~, $compat_range)>>`.
  ... Check that `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)'^?^` is Some value.
  ... Let `(typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~, typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~)` be `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)'^?^`.
  ... Let `typeIR~reduced~` be <<type_of_typedExpressionIR, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~`>>.
  ... Check that `typeIR~reduced~` is equal to <<type_of_typedExpressionIR, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~`>>.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR^?^` be <<coerce_unary, implicitly cast  `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~`  to  `typeIR~key~`>>.
  ... Check that `typedExpressionIR^?^` is Some value.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~l_coerced~` be `typedExpressionIR^?^`.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR'^?^` be <<coerce_unary, implicitly cast  `typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~`  to  `typeIR~key~`>>.
  ... Check that `typedExpressionIR'^?^` is Some value.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~r_coerced~` be `typedExpressionIR'^?^`.
  ... Result in `typedExpressionIR~l_coerced~ .. typedExpressionIR~r_coerced~`.
. Else if `simpleKeysetExpression` matches pattern `DEFAULT`:
 .. Group default:
  ... Result in `DEFAULT`.
. Else if `simpleKeysetExpression` matches pattern `_`:
 .. Group dontcare:
  ... Result in `_`.


relation SelectCase_keyset_ok: `TC`, `typeIR'''^{asterisk}^`, and `keysetExpression`


. Check that `typeIR'''^{asterisk}^` is a list of length 1.
. Let `[typeIR~key~]` be `typeIR'''^{asterisk}^`.
. If let `expression` be `keysetExpression`:
 .. Group simpleKeysetExpression-expression:
  ... Let <<SelectCase_keyset_simple_ok, `TC typeIR~key~ |- expression : simpleKeysetExpressionIR`>>.
  ... Result in `simpleKeysetExpressionIR`.
. Else if let `tupleKeysetExpression` be `keysetExpression`:
 .. If let `( expression~l~ &&& expression~r~ )` be `tupleKeysetExpression`:
  ... Group tupleKeysetExpression-mask:
   .... Let <<SelectCase_keyset_simple_ok, `TC typeIR~key~ |- expression~l~ &&& expression~r~ : simpleKeysetExpressionIR`>>.
   .... Result in `( [simpleKeysetExpressionIR] )`.
 .. Else if let `( expression~l~ .. expression~r~ )` be `tupleKeysetExpression`:
  ... Group tupleKeysetExpression-range:
   .... Let <<SelectCase_keyset_simple_ok, `TC typeIR~key~ |- expression~l~ .. expression~r~ : simpleKeysetExpressionIR`>>.
   .... Result in `( [simpleKeysetExpressionIR] )`.
. Check that `keysetExpression` has type `simpleKeysetExpression`.
. Let `simpleKeysetExpression` be `keysetExpression`.
. If let `expression~l~ &&& expression~r~` be `simpleKeysetExpression`:
 .. Group simpleKeysetExpression-mask:
  ... Let <<SelectCase_keyset_simple_ok, `TC typeIR~key~ |- expression~l~ &&& expression~r~ : simpleKeysetExpressionIR`>>.
  ... Result in `simpleKeysetExpressionIR`.
. Else if let `expression~l~ .. expression~r~` be `simpleKeysetExpression`:
 .. Group simpleKeysetExpression-range:
  ... Let <<SelectCase_keyset_simple_ok, `TC typeIR~key~ |- expression~l~ .. expression~r~ : simpleKeysetExpressionIR`>>.
  ... Result in `simpleKeysetExpressionIR`.
. If let `simpleKeysetExpression` be `keysetExpression`:
 .. If `simpleKeysetExpression` matches pattern `DEFAULT`:
  ... Group simpleKeysetExpression-default:
   .... If `typeIR'''^{asterisk}^` is equal to `[ ]`:
    ..... Result in `DEFAULT`.
   .... Let `typeIR''^{asterisk}^` be `typeIR'''^{asterisk}^`.
   .... Else if let `[typeIR~key~]` be `typeIR''^{asterisk}^`:
    ..... Let <<SelectCase_keyset_simple_ok, `TC typeIR~key~ |- DEFAULT : simpleKeysetExpressionIR`>>.
    ..... Result in `simpleKeysetExpressionIR`.
   .... Else if the length of `typeIR''^{asterisk}^` is greater than `1`:
    ..... Let <<SelectCase_keyset_simple_ok, `TC SEQ < typeIR''^{asterisk}^ > |- DEFAULT : simpleKeysetExpressionIR`>>.
    ..... Result in `simpleKeysetExpressionIR`.
 .. Else if `simpleKeysetExpression` matches pattern `_`:
  ... Group simpleKeysetExpression-dontcare:
   .... Let `typeIR'^{asterisk}^` be `typeIR'''^{asterisk}^`.
   .... Else if let `[typeIR~key~]` be `typeIR'^{asterisk}^`:
    ..... Let <<SelectCase_keyset_simple_ok, `TC typeIR~key~ |- _ : simpleKeysetExpressionIR`>>.
    ..... Result in `simpleKeysetExpressionIR`.
   .... Else if the length of `typeIR'^{asterisk}^` is greater than `1`:
    ..... Let <<SelectCase_keyset_simple_ok, `TC SEQ < typeIR'^{asterisk}^ > |- _ : simpleKeysetExpressionIR`>>.
    ..... Result in `simpleKeysetExpressionIR`.
. Else let `tupleKeysetExpression` be `keysetExpression`:
 .. If `tupleKeysetExpression` matches pattern `( DEFAULT )`:
  ... Group tupleKeysetExpression-default:
   .... Let `typeIR'^{asterisk}^` be `typeIR'''^{asterisk}^`.
   .... Else if let `[typeIR~key~]` be `typeIR'^{asterisk}^`:
    ..... Let <<SelectCase_keyset_simple_ok, `TC typeIR~key~ |- DEFAULT : simpleKeysetExpressionIR`>>.
    ..... Result in `( [simpleKeysetExpressionIR] )`.
   .... Else if the length of `typeIR'^{asterisk}^` is greater than `1`:
    ..... Let <<SelectCase_keyset_simple_ok, `TC SEQ < typeIR'^{asterisk}^ > |- DEFAULT : simpleKeysetExpressionIR`>>.
    ..... Result in `( [simpleKeysetExpressionIR] )`.
 .. Else if `tupleKeysetExpression` matches pattern `( _ )`:
  ... Group tupleKeysetExpression-dontcare:
   .... Let `typeIR'^{asterisk}^` be `typeIR'''^{asterisk}^`.
   .... Else if let `[typeIR~key~]` be `typeIR'^{asterisk}^`:
    ..... Let <<SelectCase_keyset_simple_ok, `TC typeIR~key~ |- _ : simpleKeysetExpressionIR`>>.
    ..... Result in `( [simpleKeysetExpressionIR] )`.
   .... Else if the length of `typeIR'^{asterisk}^` is greater than `1`:
    ..... Let <<SelectCase_keyset_simple_ok, `TC SEQ < typeIR'^{asterisk}^ > |- _ : simpleKeysetExpressionIR`>>.
    ..... Result in `( [simpleKeysetExpressionIR] )`.
 .. Else if let `( simpleKeysetExpression~h~ , simpleKeysetExpressionList~t~ )` be `tupleKeysetExpression`:
  ... Group tupleKeysetExpression-list:
   .... Let `simpleKeysetExpression~t~^{asterisk}^` be <<flatten_simpleKeysetExpressionList, the list of simple keyset expressions in `simpleKeysetExpressionList~t~`>>.
   .... Let `simpleKeysetExpression^{asterisk}^` be `simpleKeysetExpression~h~ {two-colons} simpleKeysetExpression~t~^{asterisk}^`.
   .... Check that the length of `typeIR'''^{asterisk}^` is equal to the length of `simpleKeysetExpression^{asterisk}^`.
   .... Let `simpleKeysetExpressionIR^{asterisk}^` be the list of `simpleKeysetExpressionIR`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
        * Let <<SelectCase_keyset_simple_ok, `TC typeIR''' |- simpleKeysetExpression : simpleKeysetExpressionIR`>>.
--
+
for each `simpleKeysetExpression` in `simpleKeysetExpression^{asterisk}^` and `typeIR'''` in `typeIR'''^{asterisk}^`
   .... Result in `( simpleKeysetExpressionIR^{asterisk}^ )`.


relation SelectCase_ok: `TC`, `nameIR~state~^{asterisk}^`, `typeIR~key~^{asterisk}^`, and `keysetExpression : name ;`


. Group :
 .. Let <<SelectCase_keyset_ok, `TC typeIR~key~^{asterisk}^ |- keysetExpression : keysetExpressionIR`>>.
 .. Let `nameIR` be <<name, the name of `name`>>.
 .. Check that `nameIR` is in `nameIR~state~^{asterisk}^`.
 .. Result in `keysetExpressionIR : nameIR ;`.


relation TableEntry_keyset_simple_ok: `TC`, `TBLC`, (`typeIR~key~`, `text`), and `simpleKeysetExpression`


. If let `expression` be `simpleKeysetExpression`:
 .. Group expression:
  ... If `text` is equal to `"lpm"`:
   .... Let `matchMode` be `TBLC.MODE`.
   .... Check that `matchMode` matches pattern `NOPRILPM %`.
   .... Let `NOPRILPM n` be `matchMode`.
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Let `typeIR` be <<type_of_typedExpressionIR, the type of  `typedExpressionIR`>>.
   .... Let `ctk` be <<ctk_of_typedExpressionIR, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR`>>.
   .... Check that <<Sub_impl, `typeIR` can be implicitly cast to `typeIR~key~`>>.
   .... Let `typeIR~set~` be `SET < [typeIR~key~] >`.
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR~set~` be <<typedExpressionIR, `( typeIR~set~ ) typedExpressionIR` annotated with type `typeIR~set~` and compile-time known-ness `ctk`>>.
   .... Result in `LPM n` and `typedExpressionIR~set~`.
  ... Else `text` is not equal to `"lpm"`:
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Let `typeIR` be <<type_of_typedExpressionIR, the type of  `typedExpressionIR`>>.
   .... Let `ctk` be <<ctk_of_typedExpressionIR, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR`>>.
   .... Check that <<Sub_impl, `typeIR` can be implicitly cast to `typeIR~key~`>>.
   .... Let `typeIR~set~` be `SET < [typeIR~key~] >`.
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR~set~` be <<typedExpressionIR, `( typeIR~set~ ) typedExpressionIR` annotated with type `typeIR~set~` and compile-time known-ness `ctk`>>.
   .... Result in `NOLPM` and `typedExpressionIR~set~`.
. If let `expression~l~ &&& expression~r~` be `simpleKeysetExpression`:
 .. Group mask:
  ... If `text` is equal to `"lpm"`:
   .... Let `matchMode` be `TBLC.MODE`.
   .... Check that `matchMode` matches pattern `NOPRILPM %`.
   .... Let `NOPRILPM n` be `matchMode`.
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR~l~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~l~`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR~r~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~r~`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Let `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)^?^` be <<coerce_binary, implicitly cast  `typedExpressionIR~l~`  and  `typedExpressionIR~r~`  to equal types>>.
   .... Check that `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)^?^` is Some value.
   .... Let `(typedExpressionIR~l_cast~, typedExpressionIR~r_cast~)` be `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)^?^`.
   .... Let `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)'^?^` be `<<reduce_serenum_binary, $reduce_serenum_binary(typedExpressionIR~l_cast~, typedExpressionIR~r_cast~, $compat_mask)>>`.
   .... Check that `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)'^?^` is Some value.
   .... Let `(typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~, typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~)` be `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)'^?^`.
   .... Let `typeIR~reduced~` be <<type_of_typedExpressionIR, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~`>>.
   .... Let `ctk~r_reduced~` be <<ctk_of_typedExpressionIR, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~`>>.
   .... Check that <<Sub_impl, `typeIR~reduced~` can be implicitly cast to `typeIR~key~`>>.
   .... Check that `ctk~r_reduced~` matches pattern `LCTK`.
   .... Let `value~r~` be the result of <<Expr_eval_lctk, the local compile-time evaluation of `typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Let `i~r~` be <<int_of_value, the integer representation of  `value~r~`>>.
   .... Let `int` be `<<int_to_bitstr, $int_to_bitstr(n, i~r~)>>`.
   .... Let `n~prefix~` be `<<tableEntry_lpm_prefix, $tableEntry_lpm_prefix(n W int)>>`.
   .... Result in `LPM n~prefix~` and `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~ &&& typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~`.
  ... Else if `text` is equal to `"ternary"`:
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR~l~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~l~`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Let `typedExpressionIR~r~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~r~`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC`>>.
   .... Let `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)^?^` be <<coerce_binary, implicitly cast  `typedExpressionIR~l~`  and  `typedExpressionIR~r~`  to equal types>>.
   .... Check that `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)^?^` is Some value.
   .... Let `(typedExpressionIR~l_cast~, typedExpressionIR~r_cast~)` be `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)^?^`.
   .... Let `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)'^?^` be `<<reduce_serenum_binary, $reduce_serenum_binary(typedExpressionIR~l_cast~, typedExpressionIR~r_cast~, $compat_mask)>>`.
   .... Check that `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)'^?^` is Some value.
   .... Let `(typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~, typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~)` be `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)'^?^`.
   .... Let `typeIR~reduced~` be <<type_of_typedExpressionIR, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~`>>.
   .... Let `ctk~r_reduced~` be <<ctk_of_typedExpressionIR, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~`>>.
   .... Check that <<Sub_impl, `typeIR~reduced~` can be implicitly cast to `typeIR~key~`>>.
   .... Result in `NOLPM` and `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~ &&& typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~`.
. Else if `simpleKeysetExpression` matches pattern `DEFAULT`:
 .. Group default:
  ... If `text` is equal to `"lpm"`:
   .... Let `matchMode` be `TBLC.MODE`.
   .... Check that `matchMode` matches pattern `NOPRILPM %`.
   .... Let `NOPRILPM n` be `matchMode`.
   .... Result in `LPM n` and `DEFAULT`.
  ... Else `text` is not equal to `"lpm"`:
   .... Check that `text` is not equal to `"exact"`.
   .... Result in `NOLPM` and `DEFAULT`.
. Else if `simpleKeysetExpression` matches pattern `_`:
 .. Group dontcare:
  ... If `text` is equal to `"lpm"`:
   .... Let `matchMode` be `TBLC.MODE`.
   .... Check that `matchMode` matches pattern `NOPRILPM %`.
   .... Let `NOPRILPM ++_++` be `matchMode`.
   .... Result in `LPM 0` and `_`.
  ... Else `text` is not equal to `"lpm"`:
   .... Check that `text` is not equal to `"exact"`.
   .... Result in `NOLPM` and `_`.
. Else if `text` is equal to `"range"`:
 .. Check that `simpleKeysetExpression` matches pattern `% .. %`.
 .. Let `expression~l~ .. expression~r~` be `simpleKeysetExpression`.
 .. Group range-range:
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~l~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~l~`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `typedExpressionIR~r~` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing `expression~r~`, under cursor `LOCAL` and typing context `TC`>>.
  ... Let `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)^?^` be <<coerce_binary, implicitly cast  `typedExpressionIR~l~`  and  `typedExpressionIR~r~`  to equal types>>.
  ... Check that `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)^?^` is Some value.
  ... Let `(typedExpressionIR~l_cast~, typedExpressionIR~r_cast~)` be `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)^?^`.
  ... Let `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)'^?^` be `<<reduce_serenum_binary, $reduce_serenum_binary(typedExpressionIR~l_cast~, typedExpressionIR~r_cast~, $compat_range)>>`.
  ... Check that `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)'^?^` is Some value.
  ... Let `(typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~, typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~)` be `(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)'^?^`.
  ... Let `typeIR~reduced~` be <<type_of_typedExpressionIR, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~`>>.
  ... Let `ctk~r_reduced~` be <<ctk_of_typedExpressionIR, the compile-time known-ness of  `typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~`>>.
  ... Check that <<Sub_impl, `typeIR~reduced~` can be implicitly cast to `typeIR~key~`>>.
  ... Result in `NOLPM` and `typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~ .. typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~`.


relation TableEntry_keysets_simple_ok: `TC`, `TBLC`, `TBLS'`, `matchKey^{asterisk}^`, and `simpleKeysetExpression^{asterisk}^`


. If `matchKey^{asterisk}^` is an empty list:
 .. Check that `simpleKeysetExpression^{asterisk}^` is an empty list.
 .. Group nil:
  ... Result in `TBLS'` and `[ ]`.
. Else let `matchKey~h~ {two-colons} matchKey~t~^{asterisk}^` be `matchKey^{asterisk}^`:
 .. Check that `simpleKeysetExpression^{asterisk}^` is a non-empty list.
 .. Let `simpleKeysetExpression~h~ {two-colons} simpleKeysetExpression~t~^{asterisk}^` be `simpleKeysetExpression^{asterisk}^`.
 .. Group cons:
  ... Let <<TableEntry_keyset_simple_ok, `TC TBLC |- matchKey~h~ @ simpleKeysetExpression~h~ : TBLS~1~ simpleKeysetExpressionIR~h~`>>.
  ... Let `TBLS~2~` be `<<join_tableEntryState, $join_tableEntryState(TBLS', TBLS~1~)>>`.
  ... Let <<TableEntry_keysets_simple_ok, `TC TBLC TBLS~2~ |- matchKey~t~^{asterisk}^ @ simpleKeysetExpression~t~^{asterisk}^ : TBLS~3~ simpleKeysetExpressionIR~t~^{asterisk}^`>>.
  ... Result in `TBLS~3~` and `simpleKeysetExpressionIR~h~ {two-colons} simpleKeysetExpressionIR~t~^{asterisk}^`.


relation Expr_lvalue_ok: `p`, `TC`, and <<typedExpressionIR, `expressionIR` annotated with type `++_++` and compile-time known-ness `++_++`>>


. If let `prefixedNameIR` be `expressionIR`:
 .. Group referenceExpressionIR:
  ... Let `varTypeIR^?^` be `<<find_var_t, $find_var_t(p, TC, prefixedNameIR)>>`.
  ... Check that `varTypeIR^?^` is Some value.
  ... Let `direction ++_++ ctk ++_++^?^` be `varTypeIR^?^`.
  ... Check that `ctk` matches pattern `DYN`.
  ... If `direction` matches pattern `OUT`:
   .... The relation holds.
  ... Else if `direction` matches pattern `INOUT`:
   .... The relation holds.
. Else if let `memberAccessBaseIR . nameIR` be `expressionIR`:
 .. Check that `memberAccessBaseIR` has type `typedExpressionIR`.
 .. Let `typedExpressionIR~base~` be `memberAccessBaseIR`.
 .. Group accessExpressionIR-memberAccessExpressionIR:
  ... Check that <<Expr_lvalue_ok, `p TC |- typedExpressionIR~base~`>>.
  ... Let `typeIR~base~` be <<type_of_typedExpressionIR, the type of  `typedExpressionIR~base~`>>.
  ... Let `typeIR'` be <<canon_typeIR, the canonicalized form of `typeIR~base~`>>.
  ... Else if let `typeIR [ ++_++ ]` be `typeIR'`:
   .... If `nameIR` is equal to `"next"`:
    ..... If `p = BLOCK` *and* `<<is_parser_blockKind, $is_parser_blockKind(TC.BLOCK.KIND)>>`:
     ...... The relation holds.
    ..... Else if `p = LOCAL` *and* `<<is_parser_state_localKind, $is_parser_state_localKind(TC.LOCAL.KIND)>>`:
     ...... The relation holds.
   .... Else if `nameIR` is equal to `"last"`:
    ..... If `p = BLOCK` *and* `<<is_parser_blockKind, $is_parser_blockKind(TC.BLOCK.KIND)>>`:
     ...... The relation holds.
    ..... Else if `p = LOCAL` *and* `<<is_parser_state_localKind, $is_parser_state_localKind(TC.LOCAL.KIND)>>`:
     ...... The relation holds.
  ... Else if `~<<is_headerStackTypeIR, $is_headerStackTypeIR($canon_typeIR(typeIR~base~))>>`:
   .... The relation holds.
. Else if let `typedExpressionIR~base~ [ typedExpressionIR~index~ ]` be `expressionIR`:
 .. Group accessExpressionIR-indexAccessExpressionIR:
  ... Check that <<Expr_lvalue_ok, `p TC |- typedExpressionIR~base~`>>.
  ... The relation holds.
. Else if let `typedExpressionIR~base~ [ typedExpressionIR~hi~ : typedExpressionIR~lo~ ]` be `expressionIR`:
 .. Group accessExpressionIR-indexAccessExpressionIR-bitslice:
  ... Check that <<Expr_lvalue_ok, `p TC |- typedExpressionIR~base~`>>.
  ... The relation holds.


relation Expr_inst: `p`, `IC`, `STO'`, and <<typedExpressionIR, `expressionIR` annotated with `++_++`>>


. If let `booleanLiteral` be `expressionIR`:
 .. Group literalExpressionIR-boolean:
  ... If `booleanLiteral` matches pattern `TRUE`:
   .... Result in `STO'` and `B true`.
  ... Else `booleanLiteral` matches pattern `FALSE`:
   .... Result in `STO'` and `B false`.
. Else if let `integerLiteral` be `expressionIR`:
 .. Group literalExpressionIR-number:
  ... If let `D i` be `integerLiteral`:
   .... Result in `STO'` and `D i`.
  ... Else if let `n W i` be `integerLiteral`:
   .... Result in `STO'` and `n W i`.
  ... Else let `n S i` be `integerLiteral`:
   .... Result in `STO'` and `n S i`.
. Else if let `" text "` be `expressionIR`:
 .. Group literalExpressionIR-stringLiteral:
  ... Result in `STO'` and `" text "`.
. Else if let `prefixedNameIR` be `expressionIR`:
 .. Group referenceExpressionIR:
  ... Let `value` be `<<find_var_i, $find_var_i(p, IC, prefixedNameIR)>>`.
  ... Result in `STO'` and `value`.
. Else if let `defaultExpression` be `expressionIR`:
 .. Group defaultExpressionIR:
  ... Result in `STO'` and `DEFAULT`.
. Else if let `unop typedExpressionIR` be `expressionIR`:
 .. Group unaryExpressionIR:
  ... Let <<Expr_inst, `p IC STO' |- typedExpressionIR : STO~1~ value`>>.
  ... Result in `STO~1~` and <<un_op, `unop` `value`>>.
. Else if let `typedExpressionIR~l~ binop' typedExpressionIR~r~` be `expressionIR`:
 .. Group binaryExpressionIR:
  ... Check that `binop'` is not in `[&&, ||]`.
  ... Let <<Expr_inst, `p IC STO' |- typedExpressionIR~l~ : STO~1~ value~l~`>>.
  ... Let <<Expr_inst, `p IC STO~1~ |- typedExpressionIR~r~ : STO~2~ value~r~`>>.
  ... Result in `STO~2~` and <<bin_op, `value~l~` `binop'` `value~r~`>>.
  ... If `binop'` matches pattern `&&`:
   .... Let <<Expr_inst, `p IC STO' |- typedExpressionIR~l~ : STO~1~ value`>>.
   .... Else if `value` is equal to `B false`:
    ..... Result in `STO~1~` and `B false`.
   .... Else if `value` is equal to `B true`:
    ..... Let <<Expr_inst, `p IC STO~1~ |- typedExpressionIR~r~ : STO~2~ value~r~`>>.
    ..... Result in `STO~2~` and `value~r~`.
  ... Else if `binop'` matches pattern `||`:
   .... Let <<Expr_inst, `p IC STO' |- typedExpressionIR~l~ : STO~1~ value`>>.
   .... Else if `value` is equal to `B true`:
    ..... Result in `STO~1~` and `B true`.
   .... Else if `value` is equal to `B false`:
    ..... Let <<Expr_inst, `p IC STO~1~ |- typedExpressionIR~r~ : STO~2~ value~r~`>>.
    ..... Result in `STO~2~` and `value~r~`.
. Else if let `typedExpressionIR~cond~ ? typedExpressionIR~true~ : typedExpressionIR~false~` be `expressionIR`:
 .. Group ternaryExpressionIR:
  ... Let <<Expr_inst, `p IC STO' |- typedExpressionIR~cond~ : STO~1~ value`>>.
  ... Else if `value` is equal to `B true`:
   .... Let <<Expr_inst, `p IC STO~1~ |- typedExpressionIR~true~ : STO~2~ value~true~`>>.
   .... Result in `STO~2~` and `value~true~`.
  ... Else if `value` is equal to `B false`:
   .... Let <<Expr_inst, `p IC STO~1~ |- typedExpressionIR~false~ : STO~2~ value~false~`>>.
   .... Result in `STO~2~` and `value~false~`.
. Else if let `( typeIR ) typedExpressionIR` be `expressionIR`:
 .. Group castExpressionIR:
  ... Let <<Expr_inst, `p IC STO' |- typedExpressionIR : STO~1~ value`>>.
  ... Let `value~cast~` be <<cast_op, cast `value` to type `typeIR`>>.
  ... Result in `STO~1~` and `value~cast~`.
. Else if let `dataExpressionIR` be `expressionIR`:
 .. Check that `dataExpressionIR` matches pattern `{#}`.
 .. Group dataExpressionIR-invalid:
  ... Result in `STO'` and `{#}`.
 .. Group dataExpressionIR-sequence:
  ... If let `SEQ { typedExpressionListIR }` be `dataExpressionIR`:
   .... Let <<Exprs_inst, `p IC STO' |- typedExpressionListIR : STO~1~ value^{asterisk}^`>>.
   .... Result in `STO~1~` and `SEQ ( value^{asterisk}^ )`.
  ... Else if let `SEQ { typedExpressionListIR , ... }` be `dataExpressionIR`:
   .... Let <<Exprs_inst, `p IC STO' |- typedExpressionListIR : STO~1~ value^{asterisk}^`>>.
   .... Result in `STO~1~` and `SEQ ( value^{asterisk}^ , ... )`.
 .. Group dataExpressionIR-record:
  ... If let `RECORD { (nameIR = typedExpressionIR)^{asterisk}^ }` be `dataExpressionIR`:
   .... Let <<Exprs_inst, `p IC STO' |- typedExpressionIR^{asterisk}^ : STO~1~ value^{asterisk}^`>>.
   .... Result in `STO~1~` and `RECORD { (value nameIR ;)^{asterisk}^ }`.
  ... Else if let `RECORD { (nameIR = typedExpressionIR)^{asterisk}^ , ... }` be `dataExpressionIR`:
   .... Let <<Exprs_inst, `p IC STO' |- typedExpressionIR^{asterisk}^ : STO~1~ value^{asterisk}^`>>.
   .... Result in `STO~1~` and `RECORD { (value nameIR ;)^{asterisk}^ , ... }`.
. Else if let `ERROR . nameIR` be `expressionIR`:
 .. Group errorAccessExpressionIR:
  ... Let `nameIR~error~` be `"error." {pp} nameIR`.
  ... Let `value~error~` be `<<find_var_i, $find_var_i(p, IC, nameIR~error~)>>`.
  ... Result in `STO'` and `value~error~`.
. Else if let `memberAccessBaseIR . nameIR` be `expressionIR`:
 .. Check that `memberAccessBaseIR` matches pattern `TYPE %`.
 .. Let `TYPE prefixedNameIR` be `memberAccessBaseIR`.
 .. Group memberAccessExpressionIR-type:
  ... Let `typeDefIR'^?^` be `<<find_typeDef_i, $find_typeDef_i(p, IC, prefixedNameIR)>>`.
  ... Check that `typeDefIR'^?^` is Some value.
  ... Let `typeDefIR` be `typeDefIR'^?^`.
  ... Check that `typeDefIR` has type `enumTypeIR`.
  ... Let `enumTypeIR` be `typeDefIR`.
  ... If let `ENUM tid { ++_++^{asterisk}^ }` be `enumTypeIR`:
   .... Result in `STO'` and `tid . nameIR`.
  ... Else let `ENUM tid < ++_++ > { (id~member~ = value~member~ ;)^{asterisk}^ }` be `enumTypeIR`:
   .... Let `value'^?^` be `<<assoc_, $assoc_<nameIR, value>(nameIR, ((id~member~, value~member~))^{asterisk}^)>>`.
   .... Check that `value'^?^` is Some value.
   .... Let `value` be `value'^?^`.
   .... Result in `STO'` and `tid . nameIR . value`.
. Let `typeIR~base~` be the type of `++_++`.
. If let `memberAccessBaseIR . text` be `expressionIR`:
 .. Check that `memberAccessBaseIR` has type `typedExpressionIR`.
 .. Let `typedExpressionIR~base~` be `memberAccessBaseIR`.
 .. Check that `text` is equal to `"size"`.
 .. Group memberAccessExpressionIR-expression-stack-size:
  ... Let <<expressionNoteIR, type `typeIR` and compile-time known-ness `++_++`>> be the note of `typedExpressionIR~base~`.
  ... Check that `typeIR` is equal to `typeIR~base~`.
  ... Let `typeIR'` be <<canon_typeIR, the canonicalized form of `typeIR~base~`>>.
  ... Check that `typeIR'` has type `headerStackTypeIR`.
  ... Let `++_++ [ n~size~ ]` be `typeIR'`.
  ... Result in `STO'` and `D n~size~`.
. Else if let `typedExpressionIR~base~ [ typedExpressionIR~hi~ : typedExpressionIR~lo~ ]` be `expressionIR`:
 .. Group sliceAccessExpressionIR:
  ... Let <<Expr_inst, `p IC STO' |- typedExpressionIR~base~ : STO~1~ value~base~`>>.
  ... Let <<Expr_inst, `p IC STO~1~ |- typedExpressionIR~hi~ : STO~2~ value~hi~`>>.
  ... Let <<Expr_inst, `p IC STO~2~ |- typedExpressionIR~lo~ : STO~3~ value~lo~`>>.
  ... Result in `STO~3~` and `<<bitacc_op, $bitacc_op(value~base~, value~hi~, value~lo~)>>`.
. Else if let `callExpressionIR` be `expressionIR`:
 .. If let `prefixedNameIR < typeArgumentListIR > ( argumentListIR )` be `callExpressionIR`:
  ... Group callExpressionIR-constructor:
   .... Let `(cid, constructorDef, id*)^?^` be `<<find_constructorDef_i, $find_constructorDef_i(IC, prefixedNameIR, argumentListIR)>>`.
   .... Check that `(cid, constructorDef, id*)^?^` is Some value.
   .... Let `(++_++, constructorDef, id~default~^{asterisk}^)` be `(cid, constructorDef, id*)^?^`.
   .... Let <<Constructor_inst, `p IC STO' |- constructorDef < typeArgumentListIR > ( argumentListIR # id~default~^{asterisk}^ ) : STO~1~ object`>>.
   .... Let `STO~2~` be `<<add_map, $add_map<oid, object>(STO~1~, IC.PATH, object)>>`.
   .... Let `value~ref~` be `! IC.PATH`.
   .... Result in `STO~2~` and `value~ref~`.
 .. Else let `callableTargetIR < typeArgumentIR^{asterisk}^ > ( argumentIR^{asterisk}^ )` be `callExpressionIR`:
  ... Else if `typeArgumentIR^{asterisk}^` is an empty list:
   .... Check that `argumentIR^{asterisk}^` is an empty list.
   .... Group callExpressionIR-builtin-size:
    ..... If let `typedExpressionIR~base~ . nameIR` be `callableTargetIR`:
     ...... Let <<expressionNoteIR, type `typeIR~base~` and compile-time known-ness `++_++`>> be the note of `typedExpressionIR~base~`.
     ...... Check that `nameIR` is in `["minSizeInBits", "minSizeInBytes", "maxSizeInBits", "maxSizeInBytes"]`.
     ...... Result in `STO'` and `<<sizeof, $sizeof(typeIR~base~, nameIR)>>`.
    ..... Else if let `TYPE prefixedNameIR . nameIR` be `callableTargetIR`:
     ...... Let `typeDefIR^?^` be `<<find_typeDef_i, $find_typeDef_i(p, IC, prefixedNameIR)>>`.
     ...... Check that `typeDefIR^?^` is Some value.
     ...... Let `typeDefIR~base~` be `typeDefIR^?^`.
     ...... If `<<is_monomorphic_typeDefIR, $is_monomorphic_typeDefIR(typeDefIR~base~)>>`:
      ....... Let `typeIR~base~` be `<<type_of_typeDefIR, $type_of_typeDefIR(typeDefIR~base~)>>`.
      ....... Check that `nameIR` is in `["minSizeInBits", "minSizeInBytes", "maxSizeInBits", "maxSizeInBytes"]`.
      ....... Result in `STO'` and `<<sizeof, $sizeof(typeIR~base~, nameIR)>>`.
     ...... Else `~<<is_monomorphic_typeDefIR, $is_monomorphic_typeDefIR(typeDefIR~base~)>>`:
      ....... Check that (`[ ]`, `[ ]`) is equal to `<<type_parameters_of_typeDefIR, $type_parameters_of_typeDefIR(typeDefIR~base~)>>`.
      ....... Let `typeIR~base~` be `<<type_of_typeDefIR, $type_of_typeDefIR(typeDefIR~base~)>>`.
      ....... Check that `nameIR` is in `["minSizeInBits", "minSizeInBytes", "maxSizeInBits", "maxSizeInBytes"]`.
      ....... Result in `STO'` and `<<sizeof, $sizeof(typeIR~base~, nameIR)>>`.
  ... Let `callableTargetIR' < typeArgumentListIR > ( argumentListIR )` be `callExpressionIR`.
  ... Else if let `( callableTargetIR )` be `callableTargetIR'`:
   .... Group callExpressionIR-parenthesized:
    ..... Let <<Expr_inst, `p IC STO' |- callableTargetIR < typeArgumentListIR > ( argumentListIR ) # ++_++ : STO~1~ value`>>.
    ..... Result in `STO~1~` and `value`.
. Else if let `( typedExpressionIR )` be `expressionIR`:
 .. Group parenthesizedExpressionIR:
  ... Let <<Expr_inst, `p IC STO' |- typedExpressionIR : STO~1~ value`>>.
  ... Result in `STO~1~` and `value`.


relation Exprs_inst: `p`, `IC`, `STO'`, and `typedExpressionIR^{asterisk}^`


. If `typedExpressionIR^{asterisk}^` is an empty list:
 .. Group nil:
