relation ParserStmt_inst: `IC~0'~`, `STO~0~`, and `parserStatementIR`


. If let `constantDeclarationIR` be `parserStatementIR`:
 .. Group constantDeclarationIR:
  ... Let <<Decl_inst, `LOCAL IC~0'~ STO~0~ |- constantDeclarationIR : IC~1~ STO~1~ declarationIR'^?^`>>.
  ... Check that `declarationIR'^?^` is Some value.
  ... Let `declarationIR` be `declarationIR'^?^`.
  ... Check that `declarationIR` has type `constantDeclarationIR`.
  ... Let `constantDeclarationIR~inst~` be `declarationIR`.
  ... Result in `IC~1~`, `STO~1~`, and `constantDeclarationIR~inst~`.
. Else if let `variableDeclarationIR` be `parserStatementIR`:
 .. Group variableDeclarationIR:
  ... Let <<BlockElementStmt_inst, `IC~0'~ STO~0~ |- variableDeclarationIR : IC~1~ STO~1~ blockElementStatementIR'^?^`>>.
  ... Check that `blockElementStatementIR'^?^` is Some value.
  ... Let `blockElementStatementIR` be `blockElementStatementIR'^?^`.
  ... Check that `blockElementStatementIR` has type `variableDeclarationIR`.
  ... Let `variableDeclarationIR~inst~` be `blockElementStatementIR`.
  ... Result in `IC~1~`, `STO~1~`, and `variableDeclarationIR~inst~`.
. Else if let `emptyStatementIR` be `parserStatementIR`:
 .. Group emptyStatementIR:
  ... Let `IC~1~`, `STO~1~`, and `statementIR` be the result of <<Stmt_inst, the compile-time evaluation of `emptyStatementIR`, under cursor `LOCAL`, instantiation context `IC~0'~`, and store `STO~0~`>>.
  ... Check that `statementIR` has type `emptyStatementIR`.
  ... Let `emptyStatementIR~inst~` be `statementIR`.
  ... Result in `IC~1~`, `STO~1~`, and `emptyStatementIR~inst~`.
. Else if let `assignmentStatementIR` be `parserStatementIR`:
 .. Group assignmentStatementIR:
  ... Let `IC~1~`, `STO~1~`, and `statementIR` be the result of <<Stmt_inst, the compile-time evaluation of `assignmentStatementIR`, under cursor `LOCAL`, instantiation context `IC~0'~`, and store `STO~0~`>>.
  ... Check that `statementIR` has type `assignmentStatementIR`.
  ... Let `assignmentStatementIR~inst~` be `statementIR`.
  ... Result in `IC~1~`, `STO~1~`, and `assignmentStatementIR~inst~`.
. Else if let `callStatementIR` be `parserStatementIR`:
 .. Group callStatementIR:
  ... Let `IC~1~`, `STO~1~`, and `statementIR` be the result of <<Stmt_inst, the compile-time evaluation of `callStatementIR`, under cursor `LOCAL`, instantiation context `IC~0'~`, and store `STO~0~`>>.
  ... Check that `statementIR` has type `callStatementIR`.
  ... Let `callStatementIR~inst~` be `statementIR`.
  ... Result in `IC~1~`, `STO~1~`, and `callStatementIR~inst~`.
. Else if let `prefixedNameIR . APPLY ( argumentListIR ) ;` be `parserStatementIR`:
 .. Group directApplicationStatementIR:
  ... Let `(cid, constructorDef, id*)^?^` be `<<find_constructorDef_i, $find_constructorDef_i(IC~0'~, prefixedNameIR, [ ])>>`.
  ... Check that `(cid, constructorDef, id*)^?^` is Some value.
  ... Let `(++_++, constructorDef, ++_++^{asterisk}^)` be `(cid, constructorDef, id*)^?^`.
  ... Let <<Constructor_inst, `LOCAL IC~0'~ STO~0~ |- constructorDef < [ ] > ( [ ] # [ ] ) : STO~1~ object`>>.
  ... Let `tid` be <<flatten_prefixedNameIR, the string form of  `prefixedNameIR`>>.
  ... Let `tid~fresh~` be <<fresh_tid, a fresh type variable>>.
  ... Let `nameIR` be `tid {pp} "_" {pp} tid~fresh~`.
  ... Let `oid` be `IC~0'~.PATH {pp} [nameIR]`.
  ... Let `STO~2~` be `<<add_map, $add_map<oid, object>(STO~1~, oid, object)>>`.
  ... Let `typeIR` be `tid`.
  ... Let `constantDeclarationIR` be `CONST typeIR nameIR = ! oid ;`.
  ... Let `callableTargetIR` be `tid # ( typeIR CTK ) . "apply"`.
  ... Let `callStatementIR` be `callableTargetIR < [ ] > ( argumentListIR ) ;`.
  ... Let `parserBlockStatementIR` be `{ [constantDeclarationIR, callStatementIR] }`.
  ... Result in `IC~0'~`, `STO~2~`, and `parserBlockStatementIR`.
. Else if let `annotationList { parserStatementListIR }` be `parserStatementIR`:
 .. Group parserBlockStatementIR:
  ... Let <<ParserStmts_inst, `IC~0'~ STO~0~ |- parserStatementListIR : IC~1~ STO~1~ parserStatementListIR~inst~`>>.
  ... Let `parserBlockStatementIR~inst~` be `annotationList { parserStatementListIR~inst~ }`.
  ... Result in `IC~1~`, `STO~1~`, and `parserBlockStatementIR~inst~`.
. Else let `parserConditionalStatementIR` be `parserStatementIR`:
 .. Group parserConditionalStatementIR:
  ... If let `IF ( typedExpressionIR~cond~ ) parserStatementIR~then~` be `parserConditionalStatementIR`:
   .... Let <<ParserStmt_inst, `IC~0'~ STO~0~ |- parserStatementIR~then~ : IC~then~ STO~1~ parserStatementIR~then_inst~`>>.
   .... Result in `IC~0'~`, `STO~1~`, and `IF ( typedExpressionIR~cond~ ) parserStatementIR~then_inst~`.
  ... Else let `IF ( typedExpressionIR~cond~ ) parserStatementIR~then~ ELSE parserStatementIR~else~` be `parserConditionalStatementIR`:
   .... Let <<ParserStmt_inst, `IC~0'~ STO~0~ |- parserStatementIR~then~ : IC~then~ STO~1~ parserStatementIR~then_inst~`>>.
   .... Let <<ParserStmt_inst, `IC~0'~ STO~1~ |- parserStatementIR~else~ : IC~else~ STO~2~ parserStatementIR~else_inst~`>>.
   .... Result in `IC~0'~`, `STO~2~`, and `IF ( typedExpressionIR~cond~ ) parserStatementIR~then_inst~ ELSE parserStatementIR~else_inst~`.


