. If let `constantDeclarationIR` be `controlLocalDeclarationIR`:
 .. Group constantDeclarationIR:
  ... Let <<Decl_inst, `BLOCK IC~0'~ STO~0'~ |- constantDeclarationIR : IC~1~ STO~1~ declarationIR'^?^`>>.
  ... Check that `declarationIR'^?^` is Some value.
  ... Let `declarationIR` be `declarationIR'^?^`.
  ... Check that `declarationIR` has type `constantDeclarationIR`.
  ... Let `constantDeclarationIR~inst~` be `declarationIR`.
  ... Result in `IC~1~`, `STO~1~`, and `constantDeclarationIR~inst~`.
. Else if let `instantiationIR` be `controlLocalDeclarationIR`:
 .. Group instantiationIR:
  ... Let <<Decl_inst, `BLOCK IC~0'~ STO~0'~ |- instantiationIR : IC~1~ STO~1~ declarationIR'^?^`>>.
  ... Check that `declarationIR'^?^` is Some value.
  ... Let `declarationIR` be `declarationIR'^?^`.
  ... Check that `declarationIR` has type `constantDeclarationIR`.
  ... Let `constantDeclarationIR` be `declarationIR`.
  ... Result in `IC~1~`, `STO~1~`, and `constantDeclarationIR`.
. Else if let `variableDeclarationIR` be `controlLocalDeclarationIR`:
 .. Group variableDeclarationIR:
  ... Result in `IC~0'~`, `STO~0'~`, and `variableDeclarationIR`.
. Else if let `actionDeclarationIR` be `controlLocalDeclarationIR`:
 .. Group actionDeclarationIR:
  ... Let <<Decl_inst, `BLOCK IC~0'~ STO~0'~ |- actionDeclarationIR : IC~1~ STO~1~ declarationIR^?^`>>.
  ... Check that `declarationIR^?^` is None.
  ... Result in `IC~1~`, `STO~1~`, and `None`.
. Else let `annotationList TABLE typeIR nameIR { tablePropertyListIR }` be `controlLocalDeclarationIR`:
 .. Group tableDeclarationIR:
  ... Let `IC~inner~` be `<<enter_path_i, $enter_path_i(IC~0'~, nameIR)>>`.
  ... Let <<Constructor_inst, `BLOCK IC~0'~ STO~0'~ |- TABLE nameIR { tablePropertyListIR } < [ ] > ( [ ] # [ ] ) : STO~1~ object~table~`>>.
  ... Let `oid` be `IC~0'~.PATH {pp} [nameIR]`.
  ... Let `STO~2~` be `<<add_map, $add_map<oid, object>(STO~1~, oid, object~table~)>>`.
  ... Let `IC~1~` be `<<add_var_i, $add_var_i(BLOCK, IC~0'~, nameIR, ! oid)>>`.
  ... Let `constantDeclarationIR` be `CONST typeIR nameIR = ! oid ;`.
  ... Result in `IC~1~`, `STO~2~`, and `constantDeclarationIR`.


