  ... Result in `IC~2~`, `STO~2~`, and `controlLocalDeclarationIR~h_inst~ {two-colons} controlLocalDeclarationIR~t_inst~^{asterisk}^`.


relation Decl_inst: `cursor'`, `IC~0~`, `STO'`, and `declarationIR`


. If let `annotationList CONST typeIR nameIR = value ;` be `declarationIR`:
 .. Group constantDeclarationIR:
  ... If `cursor'` matches pattern `GLOBAL`:
   .... Let `IC~1~` be `<<add_var_i, $add_var_i(GLOBAL, IC~0~, nameIR, value)>>`.
   .... Result in `IC~1~`, `STO'`, and `None`.
  ... Else `cursor'` does not match pattern `GLOBAL`:
   .... Let `IC~1~` be `<<add_var_i, $add_var_i(cursor', IC~0~, nameIR, value)>>`.
   .... Let `constantDeclarationIR` be `annotationList CONST typeIR nameIR = value ;`.
   .... Result in `IC~1~`, `STO'`, and `constantDeclarationIR`.
. Else if let `annotationList typeIR prefixedNameIR < typeArgumentListIR > ( argumentListIR ) nameIR objectInitializerOptIR ;` be `declarationIR`:
 .. Group instantiationIR:
  ... If `cursor'` matches pattern `GLOBAL`:
   .... Let `(cid, constructorDef, id*)^?^` be `<<find_constructorDef_i, $find_constructorDef_i(IC~0~, prefixedNameIR, argumentListIR)>>`.
   .... Check that `(cid, constructorDef, id*)^?^` is Some value.
   .... Let `(++_++, constructorDef, id~default~^{asterisk}^)` be `(cid, constructorDef, id*)^?^`.
   .... Let `IC~inner~` be `<<enter_path_i, $enter_path_i(IC~0~, nameIR)>>`.
   .... Let <<Constructor_inst, `GLOBAL IC~inner~ STO' |- constructorDef < typeArgumentListIR > ( argumentListIR # id~default~^{asterisk}^ ) : STO~1~ object`>>.
   .... Else if let `EXTERN tid < theta > { externState frame externMethodDefEnv }` be `object`:
    ..... Let `IC~decl~` be `<<empty_instContext, $empty_instContext>>[PATH = IC~0~.PATH][GLOBAL = IC~0~.GLOBAL]`.
    ..... Let `objectDeclarationListIR` be `<<flatten_objectInitializerOptIR, $flatten_objectInitializerOptIR(objectInitializerOptIR)>>`.
    ..... Let `IC~decl_post~`, `STO~2~`, and `++_++^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Decls_inst, instantiating `objectDeclarationListIR`, under cursor `BLOCK`, instantiation context `IC~decl~`, and store `STO~1~`>>.
    ..... Let `frame~merged~` be `<<merge_frames, $merge_frames(frame, IC~decl_post~.BLOCK.FRAME)>>`.
    ..... Let `externMethodDefEnv~merged~` be `<<merge_externMethodDefEnvs, $merge_externMethodDefEnvs(externMethodDefEnv, IC~decl_post~.BLOCK.CALLABLE)>>`.
    ..... Let `object~merged~` be `EXTERN tid < theta > { externState frame~merged~ externMethodDefEnv~merged~ }`.
    ..... Let `oid` be `IC~0~.PATH {pp} [nameIR]`.
    ..... Let `STO~3~` be `<<add_map, $add_map<oid, object>(STO~2~, oid, object~merged~)>>`.
    ..... Let `IC~1~` be `<<add_var_i, $add_var_i(GLOBAL, IC~0~, nameIR, ! oid)>>`.
    ..... Result in `IC~1~`, `STO~3~`, and `None`.
   .... Else if `~<<is_externObject, $is_externObject(object)>>`:
    ..... Let `oid` be `IC~0~.PATH {pp} [nameIR]`.
    ..... Let `STO~2~` be `<<add_map, $add_map<oid, object>(STO~1~, oid, object)>>`.
    ..... Let `IC~1~` be `<<add_var_i, $add_var_i(GLOBAL, IC~0~, nameIR, ! oid)>>`.
    ..... Result in `IC~1~`, `STO~2~`, and `None`.
  ... Else `cursor'` does not match pattern `GLOBAL`:
   .... Let `(cid, constructorDef, id*)^?^` be `<<find_constructorDef_i, $find_constructorDef_i(IC~0~, prefixedNameIR, argumentListIR)>>`.
   .... Check that `(cid, constructorDef, id*)^?^` is Some value.
   .... Let `(++_++, constructorDef, id~default~^{asterisk}^)` be `(cid, constructorDef, id*)^?^`.
   .... Let `IC~inner~` be `<<enter_path_i, $enter_path_i(IC~0~, nameIR)>>`.
   .... Let <<Constructor_inst, `cursor' IC~inner~ STO' |- constructorDef < typeArgumentListIR > ( argumentListIR # id~default~^{asterisk}^ ) : STO~1~ object`>>.
   .... Else if let `EXTERN tid < theta > { externState frame externMethodDefEnv }` be `object`:
    ..... Let `IC~decl~` be `<<empty_instContext, $empty_instContext>>[PATH = IC~0~.PATH][GLOBAL = IC~0~.GLOBAL]`.
    ..... Let `objectDeclarationListIR` be `<<flatten_objectInitializerOptIR, $flatten_objectInitializerOptIR(objectInitializerOptIR)>>`.
    ..... Let `IC~decl_post~`, `STO~2~`, and `++_++^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Decls_inst, instantiating `objectDeclarationListIR`, under cursor `BLOCK`, instantiation context `IC~decl~`, and store `STO~1~`>>.
    ..... Let `frame~merged~` be `<<merge_frames, $merge_frames(frame, IC~decl_post~.BLOCK.FRAME)>>`.
    ..... Let `externMethodDefEnv~merged~` be `<<merge_externMethodDefEnvs, $merge_externMethodDefEnvs(externMethodDefEnv, IC~decl_post~.BLOCK.CALLABLE)>>`.
    ..... Let `object~merged~` be `EXTERN tid < theta > { externState frame~merged~ externMethodDefEnv~merged~ }`.
    ..... Let `oid` be `IC~0~.PATH {pp} [nameIR]`.
    ..... Let `STO~3~` be `<<add_map, $add_map<oid, object>(STO~2~, oid, object~merged~)>>`.
    ..... Let `IC~1~` be `<<add_var_i, $add_var_i(GLOBAL, IC~0~, nameIR, ! oid)>>`.
    ..... Let `constantDeclarationIR` be `CONST typeIR nameIR = ! oid ;`.
    ..... Result in `IC~1~`, `STO~3~`, and `constantDeclarationIR`.
   .... Else if `~<<is_externObject, $is_externObject(object)>>`:
    ..... Let `oid` be `IC~0~.PATH {pp} [nameIR]`.
    ..... Let `STO~2~` be `<<add_map, $add_map<oid, object>(STO~1~, oid, object)>>`.
    ..... Let `IC~1~` be `<<add_var_i, $add_var_i(cursor', IC~0~, nameIR, ! oid)>>`.
    ..... Let `constantDeclarationIR` be `CONST typeIR nameIR = ! oid ;`.
    ..... Result in `IC~1~`, `STO~2~`, and `constantDeclarationIR`.
. Else if let `annotationList typeIR nameIR < typeParameterListIR , typeParameterListIR~inferred~ > ( parameterListIR ) blockStatementIR` be `declarationIR`:
 .. Group functionDeclarationIR:
  ... Let `cid` be `<<cid_IR, $cid_IR(nameIR, parameterListIR)>>`.
  ... Let `definedFunctionDef` be `FUNCTION nameIR < typeParameterListIR {pp} typeParameterListIR~inferred~ > ( parameterListIR ) blockStatementIR`.
  ... Let `IC~1~` be `<<add_callableDef_overload_i, $add_callableDef_overload_i(cursor', IC~0~, cid, definedFunctionDef)>>`.
  ... Result in `IC~1~`, `STO'`, and `None`.
. Else if let `annotationList ACTION nameIR ( parameterListIR ) blockStatementIR` be `declarationIR`:
 .. Group actionDeclarationIR:
  ... Let `cid` be `<<cid_IR, $cid_IR(nameIR, parameterListIR)>>`.
  ... Let `actionDef` be `ACTION nameIR ( parameterListIR ) blockStatementIR`.
  ... Let `IC~1~` be `<<add_callableDef_non_overload_i, $add_callableDef_non_overload_i(cursor', IC~0~, cid, actionDef)>>`.
  ... Result in `IC~1~`, `STO'`, and `None`.
. Check that `cursor'` matches pattern `GLOBAL`.
. If let `ERROR { nameIR^{asterisk}^ }` be `declarationIR`:
 .. Group errorDeclarationIR:
  ... Let `nameIR~error~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `nameIR~error~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
      * Let `nameIR~error~` be <<concat_text, the concatenation of `["error.", nameIR]`>>.
--
+
for each `nameIR` in `nameIR^{asterisk}^`
  ... Let `value~error~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `value~error~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
      * Let `value~error~` be `ERROR . nameIR`.
--
+
for each `nameIR` in `nameIR^{asterisk}^`
  ... Let `IC~1~` be `<<add_vars_i, $add_vars_i(GLOBAL, IC~0~, nameIR~error~^{asterisk}^, value~error~^{asterisk}^)>>`.
  ... Result in `IC~1~`, `STO'`, and `None`.
. Else if let `MATCH_KIND { nameIR^{asterisk}^ }` be `declarationIR`:
 .. Group matchKindDeclarationIR:
  ... Let `value~match_kind~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `value~match_kind~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
      * Let `value~match_kind~` be `MATCH_KIND . nameIR`.
--
+
for each `nameIR` in `nameIR^{asterisk}^`
  ... Let `IC~1~` be `<<add_vars_i, $add_vars_i(GLOBAL, IC~0~, nameIR^{asterisk}^, value~match_kind~^{asterisk}^)>>`.
  ... Result in `IC~1~`, `STO'`, and `None`.
. Else if let `annotationList EXTERN typeIR nameIR < typeParameterListIR , typeParameterListIR~inferred~ > ( parameterListIR ) ;` be `declarationIR`:
 .. Group externFunctionDeclarationIR:
  ... Let `cid` be `<<cid_IR, $cid_IR(nameIR, parameterListIR)>>`.
  ... Let `externFunctionDef` be `EXTERN_FUNCTION nameIR < typeParameterListIR {pp} typeParameterListIR~inferred~ > ( parameterListIR )`.
  ... Let `IC~1~` be `<<add_callableDef_overload_i, $add_callableDef_overload_i(GLOBAL, IC~0~, cid, externFunctionDef)>>`.
  ... Result in `IC~1~`, `STO'`, and `None`.
. Else if let `annotationList EXTERN nameIR < typeParameterListIR , > { externConstructorPrototypeIR'^{asterisk}^ externMethodPrototypeIR^{asterisk}^ }` be `declarationIR`:
 .. Group externObjectDeclarationIR:
  ... Check that `externConstructorPrototypeIR'^{asterisk}^` is equal to `[ ]`.
  ... Let `cid~method~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `cid~method~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
      * Let `cid~method~` be <<cid_of_externMethodPrototypeIR, the callable id of  `externMethodPrototypeIR`>>.
--
+
for each `externMethodPrototypeIR` in `externMethodPrototypeIR^{asterisk}^`
  ... Let `externMethodTypeDefIR^{asterisk}^` be the list of `externMethodTypeDefIR`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
      * Let `externMethodTypeDefIR` be <<type_of_externMethodPrototypeIR, the callable type definition of  `externMethodPrototypeIR`>>.
--
+
for each `externMethodPrototypeIR` in `externMethodPrototypeIR^{asterisk}^`
  ... Let `externMethodTypeDefEnv` be `{ (cid~method~ : externMethodTypeDefIR)^{asterisk}^ }`.
  ... Let `externObjectTypeDefIR` be `EXTERN nameIR < typeParameterListIR , [ ] > externMethodTypeDefEnv`.
  ... Let `IC~1~` be `<<add_typeDef_i, $add_typeDef_i(GLOBAL, IC~0~, nameIR, externObjectTypeDefIR)>>`.
  ... Let `cid~constructor~` be `<<cid_IR, $cid_IR(nameIR, [ ])>>`.
  ... Let `constructorDef` be `EXTERN nameIR < typeParameterListIR > ( [ ] ) { externMethodPrototypeIR^{asterisk}^ }`.
  ... Let `IC~2~` be `<<add_constructorDef_i, $add_constructorDef_i(IC~1~, cid~constructor~, constructorDef)>>`.
  ... Result in `IC~2~`, `STO'`, and `None`.
  ... Let `externConstructorPrototypeIR^{asterisk}^` be `externConstructorPrototypeIR'^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Let `cid~method~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `cid~method~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
      * Let `cid~method~` be <<cid_of_externMethodPrototypeIR, the callable id of  `externMethodPrototypeIR`>>.
--
+
for each `externMethodPrototypeIR` in `externMethodPrototypeIR^{asterisk}^`
  ... Let `externMethodTypeDefIR^{asterisk}^` be the list of `externMethodTypeDefIR`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
      * Let `externMethodTypeDefIR` be <<type_of_externMethodPrototypeIR, the callable type definition of  `externMethodPrototypeIR`>>.
--
+
for each `externMethodPrototypeIR` in `externMethodPrototypeIR^{asterisk}^`
  ... Let `externMethodTypeDefEnv` be `{ (cid~method~ : externMethodTypeDefIR)^{asterisk}^ }`.
  ... Let `externObjectTypeDefIR` be `EXTERN nameIR < typeParameterListIR , [ ] > externMethodTypeDefEnv`.
  ... Let `IC~1~` be `<<add_typeDef_i, $add_typeDef_i(GLOBAL, IC~0~, nameIR, externObjectTypeDefIR)>>`.
  ... Let `cid~constructor~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `cid~constructor~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
      * Let `cid~constructor~` be <<cid_of_externConstructorPrototypeIR, the constructor id of  `externConstructorPrototypeIR`>>.
--
+
for each `externConstructorPrototypeIR` in `externConstructorPrototypeIR^{asterisk}^`
  ... Let `constructorDef^{asterisk}^` be the list of `constructorDef`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
      * Let `constructorDef` be <<constructor_of_externConstructorPrototypeIR, the constructor of  `externConstructorPrototypeIR` with type parameters  `typeParameterListIR`  and methods  `externMethodPrototypeIR^{asterisk}^`>>.
--
+
for each `externConstructorPrototypeIR` in `externConstructorPrototypeIR^{asterisk}^`
  ... Let `IC~2~` be `<<add_constructorDefs_i, $add_constructorDefs_i(IC~1~, cid~constructor~^{asterisk}^, constructorDef^{asterisk}^)>>`.
  ... Result in `IC~2~`, `STO'`, and `None`.
. Else if let `annotationList PARSER nameIR < typeParameterIR^{asterisk}^ > ( parameterListIR ) ( constructorParameterListIR ) { parserLocalDeclarationListIR parserStateListIR }` be `declarationIR`:
 .. Check that `typeParameterIR^{asterisk}^` is an empty list.
 .. Group parserDeclarationIR:
  ... Let `cid` be `<<cid_IR, $cid_IR(nameIR, constructorParameterListIR)>>`.
  ... Let `constructorDef` be `PARSER ( parameterListIR ) ( constructorParameterListIR ) { parserLocalDeclarationListIR parserStateListIR }`.
  ... Let `IC~1~` be `<<add_constructorDef_i, $add_constructorDef_i(IC~0~, cid, constructorDef)>>`.
  ... Result in `IC~1~`, `STO'`, and `None`.
. Else if let `annotationList CONTROL nameIR < typeParameterIR^{asterisk}^ > ( parameterListIR ) ( constructorParameterListIR ) { controlLocalDeclarationListIR APPLY controlBodyIR }` be `declarationIR`:
 .. Check that `typeParameterIR^{asterisk}^` is an empty list.
 .. Group controlDeclarationIR:
  ... Let `cid` be `<<cid_IR, $cid_IR(nameIR, constructorParameterListIR)>>`.
  ... Let `constructorDef` be `CONTROL ( parameterListIR ) ( constructorParameterListIR ) { controlLocalDeclarationListIR APPLY controlBodyIR }`.
  ... Let `IC~1~` be `<<add_constructorDef_i, $add_constructorDef_i(IC~0~, cid, constructorDef)>>`.
  ... Result in `IC~1~`, `STO'`, and `None`.
. Else if let `enumTypeDeclarationIR` be `declarationIR`:
 .. If let `annotationList ENUM nameIR { nameIR~field~^{asterisk}^ }` be `enumTypeDeclarationIR`:
  ... Group enumTypeDeclarationIR-non-serializable:
   .... Let `nameIR~enum_field~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `nameIR~enum_field~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
        * Let `nameIR~enum_field~` be `nameIR {pp} "." {pp} nameIR~field~`.
--
+
for each `nameIR~field~` in `nameIR~field~^{asterisk}^`
   .... Let `value~enum_field~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `value~enum_field~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
        * Let `value~enum_field~` be `nameIR . nameIR~field~`.
--
+
for each `nameIR~field~` in `nameIR~field~^{asterisk}^`
   .... Let `IC~1~` be `<<add_vars_i, $add_vars_i(GLOBAL, IC~0~, nameIR~enum_field~^{asterisk}^, value~enum_field~^{asterisk}^)>>`.
   .... Let `enumTypeDefIR` be `ENUM nameIR { nameIR~field~^{asterisk}^ }`.
   .... Let `IC~2~` be `<<add_typeDef_i, $add_typeDef_i(GLOBAL, IC~1~, nameIR, enumTypeDefIR)>>`.
   .... Result in `IC~2~`, `STO'`, and `None`.
 .. Else let `annotationList ENUM typeIR nameIR { (nameIR~field~ = typedExpressionIR~field~)^{asterisk}^ }` be `enumTypeDeclarationIR`:
  ... Group enumTypeDeclarationIR-serializable:
   .... Let <<Exprs_inst, `GLOBAL IC~0~ STO' |- typedExpressionIR~field~^{asterisk}^ : STO~1~ value~field~^{asterisk}^`>>.
   .... Let `nameIR~serenum_field~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `nameIR~serenum_field~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
        * Let `nameIR~serenum_field~` be `nameIR {pp} "." {pp} nameIR~field~`.
--
+
for each `nameIR~field~` in `nameIR~field~^{asterisk}^`
   .... Let `value~serenum_field~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `value~serenum_field~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
        * Let `value~serenum_field~` be `nameIR . nameIR~field~ . value~field~`.
--
+
for each `nameIR~field~` in `nameIR~field~^{asterisk}^` and `value~field~` in `value~field~^{asterisk}^`
   .... Let `IC~1~` be `<<add_vars_i, $add_vars_i(GLOBAL, IC~0~, nameIR~serenum_field~^{asterisk}^, value~serenum_field~^{asterisk}^)>>`.
   .... Let `enumTypeDefIR` be `ENUM nameIR < typeIR > { (nameIR~field~ = value~field~ ;)^{asterisk}^ }`.
   .... Let `IC~2~` be `<<add_typeDef_i, $add_typeDef_i(GLOBAL, IC~1~, nameIR, enumTypeDefIR)>>`.
   .... Result in `IC~2~`, `STO~1~`, and `None`.
. Else if let `annotationList STRUCT nameIR < typeParameterListIR , typeParameterListIR~inferred~ > { typeFieldIR^{asterisk}^ }` be `declarationIR`:
 .. Group structTypeDeclarationIR:
  ... Let `annotationList~field~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `annotationList~field~`, `nameIR~field~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `nameIR~field~`, and `typeIR~field~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `typeIR~field~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
      * Let `annotationList~field~ typeIR~field~ nameIR~field~ ;` be `typeFieldIR`.
--
+
for each `typeFieldIR` in `typeFieldIR^{asterisk}^`
  ... Let `structTypeDefIR` be `STRUCT nameIR < typeParameterListIR , typeParameterListIR~inferred~ > { (typeIR~field~ nameIR~field~ ;)^{asterisk}^ }`.
  ... Let `IC~1~` be `<<add_typeDef_i, $add_typeDef_i(GLOBAL, IC~0~, nameIR, structTypeDefIR)>>`.
  ... Result in `IC~1~`, `STO'`, and `None`.
. Else if let `annotationList HEADER nameIR < typeParameterListIR , typeParameterListIR~inferred~ > { typeFieldIR^{asterisk}^ }` be `declarationIR`:
 .. Group headerTypeDeclarationIR:
  ... Let `annotationList~field~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `annotationList~field~`, `nameIR~field~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `nameIR~field~`, and `typeIR~field~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `typeIR~field~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
      * Let `annotationList~field~ typeIR~field~ nameIR~field~ ;` be `typeFieldIR`.
--
+
for each `typeFieldIR` in `typeFieldIR^{asterisk}^`
  ... Let `headerTypeDefIR` be `HEADER nameIR < typeParameterListIR , typeParameterListIR~inferred~ > { (typeIR~field~ nameIR~field~ ;)^{asterisk}^ }`.
  ... Let `IC~1~` be `<<add_typeDef_i, $add_typeDef_i(GLOBAL, IC~0~, nameIR, headerTypeDefIR)>>`.
  ... Result in `IC~1~`, `STO'`, and `None`.
. Else if let `annotationList HEADER_UNION nameIR < typeParameterListIR , typeParameterListIR~inferred~ > { typeFieldIR^{asterisk}^ }` be `declarationIR`:
 .. Group headerUnionTypeDeclarationIR:
  ... Let `annotationList~field~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `annotationList~field~`, `nameIR~field~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `nameIR~field~`, and `typeIR~field~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `typeIR~field~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
      * Let `annotationList~field~ typeIR~field~ nameIR~field~ ;` be `typeFieldIR`.
--
+
for each `typeFieldIR` in `typeFieldIR^{asterisk}^`
  ... Let `headerUnionTypeDefIR` be `HEADER_UNION nameIR < typeParameterListIR , typeParameterListIR~inferred~ > { (typeIR~field~ nameIR~field~ ;)^{asterisk}^ }`.
  ... Let `IC~1~` be `<<add_typeDef_i, $add_typeDef_i(GLOBAL, IC~0~, nameIR, headerUnionTypeDefIR)>>`.
  ... Result in `IC~1~`, `STO'`, and `None`.
. Else if let `typedefDeclarationIR` be `declarationIR`:
 .. If let `annotationList TYPEDEF typedefIR nameIR ;` be `typedefDeclarationIR`:
  ... Group typedefDeclarationIR-typedef:
   .... If let `typeIR` be `typedefIR`:
    ..... Let `aliasTypeDefIR` be `TYPEDEF nameIR typeIR`.
    ..... Let `IC~1~` be `<<add_typeDef_i, $add_typeDef_i(GLOBAL, IC~0~, nameIR, aliasTypeDefIR)>>`.
    ..... Result in `IC~1~`, `STO'`, and `None`.
   .... Else let `derivedTypeDeclarationIR` be `typedefIR`:
    ..... Let <<Decl_inst, `GLOBAL IC~0~ <<empty_store, $empty_store>> |- derivedTypeDeclarationIR : IC~local~ ++_++ ++_++^?^`>>.
    ..... Let `set<tid>` be <<dom_map, the domain of the map `IC~local~.GLOBAL.TYPE`>>.
    ..... Let `set<tid>'` be <<dom_map, the domain of the map `IC~0~.GLOBAL.TYPE`>>.
    ..... Let `{ tid^{asterisk}^ }` be <<diff_set, the difference of the sets `set<tid>` and `set<tid>'`>>.
    ..... Check that `tid^{asterisk}^` is a list of length 1.
    ..... Let `[tid~newtype~]` be `tid^{asterisk}^`.
    ..... Let `typeDefIR'^?^` be `<<find_typeDef_i, $find_typeDef_i(GLOBAL, IC~local~, . tid~newtype~)>>`.
    ..... Check that `typeDefIR'^?^` is Some value.
    ..... Let `typeDefIR` be `typeDefIR'^?^`.
    ..... If `<<is_monomorphic_typeDefIR, $is_monomorphic_typeDefIR(typeDefIR)>>`:
     ...... Let `typeIR` be `<<type_of_typeDefIR, $type_of_typeDefIR(typeDefIR)>>`.
     ...... Let `aliasTypeDefIR` be `TYPEDEF nameIR typeIR`.
     ...... Let `IC~1~` be `<<add_typeDef_i, $add_typeDef_i(GLOBAL, IC~0~, nameIR, aliasTypeDefIR)>>`.
     ...... Result in `IC~1~`, `STO'`, and `None`.
    ..... Else `~<<is_monomorphic_typeDefIR, $is_monomorphic_typeDefIR(typeDefIR)>>`:
     ...... Check that (`[ ]`, `[ ]`) is equal to `<<type_parameters_of_typeDefIR, $type_parameters_of_typeDefIR(typeDefIR)>>`.
     ...... Let `typeIR~spec~` be `typeDefIR < [ ] >`.
     ...... Let `aliasTypeDefIR` be `TYPEDEF nameIR typeIR~spec~`.
     ...... Let `IC~1~` be `<<add_typeDef_i, $add_typeDef_i(GLOBAL, IC~0~, nameIR, aliasTypeDefIR)>>`.
     ...... Result in `IC~1~`, `STO'`, and `None`.
 .. Else let `annotationList TYPE typeIR nameIR ;` be `typedefDeclarationIR`:
  ... Group typedefDeclarationIR-newtype:
   .... Let `aliasTypeDefIR` be `TYPE nameIR typeIR`.
   .... Let `IC~1~` be `<<add_typeDef_i, $add_typeDef_i(GLOBAL, IC~0~, nameIR, aliasTypeDefIR)>>`.
   .... Result in `IC~1~`, `STO'`, and `None`.
. Else if let `annotationList PARSER nameIR < typeParameterListIR , typeParameterListIR~inferred~ > ( parameterIR^{asterisk}^ ) ;` be `declarationIR`:
 .. Group parserTypeDeclarationIR:
  ... Let `parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^` be the list of `parameterTypeIR`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
      * Let `parameterTypeIR` be <<type_of_parameterIR, the type of  `parameterIR`>>.
--
+
for each `parameterIR` in `parameterIR^{asterisk}^`
  ... Let `parserObjectTypeDefIR` be `PARSER < typeParameterListIR , typeParameterListIR~inferred~ > ( parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^ )`.
  ... Let `IC~1~` be `<<add_typeDef_i, $add_typeDef_i(GLOBAL, IC~0~, nameIR, parserObjectTypeDefIR)>>`.
  ... Result in `IC~1~`, `STO'`, and `None`.
. Else if let `annotationList CONTROL nameIR < typeParameterListIR , typeParameterListIR~inferred~ > ( parameterIR^{asterisk}^ ) ;` be `declarationIR`:
 .. Group controlTypeDeclarationIR:
  ... Let `parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^` be the list of `parameterTypeIR`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
      * Let `parameterTypeIR` be <<type_of_parameterIR, the type of  `parameterIR`>>.
--
+
for each `parameterIR` in `parameterIR^{asterisk}^`
  ... Let `controlObjectTypeDefIR` be `CONTROL < typeParameterListIR , typeParameterListIR~inferred~ > ( parameterTypeIR^{asterisk}^ )`.
  ... Let `IC~1~` be `<<add_typeDef_i, $add_typeDef_i(GLOBAL, IC~0~, nameIR, controlObjectTypeDefIR)>>`.
  ... Result in `IC~1~`, `STO'`, and `None`.
. Else if let `annotationList PACKAGE nameIR < typeParameterListIR , typeParameterListIR~inferred~ > ( parameterIR^{asterisk}^ ) ;` be `declarationIR`:
 .. Group packageTypeDeclarationIR:
  ... Let `typeIR^{asterisk}^` be the list of `typeIR`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
      * Let `typeIR` be the type of `parameterIR`.
--
+
for each `parameterIR` in `parameterIR^{asterisk}^`
  ... Let `packageObjectTypeDefIR` be `PACKAGE < typeParameterListIR , typeParameterListIR~inferred~ > { typeIR^{asterisk}^ }`.
  ... Let `IC~1~` be `<<add_typeDef_i, $add_typeDef_i(GLOBAL, IC~0~, nameIR, packageObjectTypeDefIR)>>`.
  ... Let `cid` be `<<cid_IR, $cid_IR(nameIR, parameterIR^{asterisk}^)>>`.
  ... Let `constructorDef` be `PACKAGE < typeParameterListIR {pp} typeParameterListIR~inferred~ > ( parameterIR^{asterisk}^ )`.
  ... Let `IC~2~` be `<<add_constructorDef_i, $add_constructorDef_i(IC~1~, cid, constructorDef)>>`.
  ... Result in `IC~2~`, `STO'`, and `None`.


relation Decls_inst: `p`, `IC'`, `STO'`, and `declarationIR^{asterisk}^`


. If `declarationIR^{asterisk}^` is an empty list:
 .. Group nil:
  ... Result in 
* the modified instantiation context `IC'`,
* the updated store `STO'`, and the instantiated declarations `[ ]`.
. Else let `declarationIR~h~ {two-colons} declarationIR~t~^{asterisk}^` be `declarationIR^{asterisk}^`:
 .. Group cons-none:
  ... Let <<Decl_inst, `p IC' STO' |- declarationIR~h~ : IC~1~ STO~1~ declarationIR'^?^`>>.
  ... Check that `declarationIR'^?^` is None.
  ... Let `IC~2~`, `STO~2~`, and `declarationIR~t_inst~^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Decls_inst, instantiating `declarationIR~t~^{asterisk}^`, under cursor `p`, instantiation context `IC~1~`, and store `STO~1~`>>.
  ... Result in 
* the modified instantiation context `IC~2~`,
* the updated store `STO~2~`, and the instantiated declarations `declarationIR~t_inst~^{asterisk}^`.
 .. Group cons-some:
  ... Let <<Decl_inst, `p IC' STO' |- declarationIR~h~ : IC~1~ STO~1~ declarationIR'^?^`>>.
  ... Check that `declarationIR'^?^` is Some value.
  ... Let `declarationIR~h_inst~` be `declarationIR'^?^`.
  ... Let `IC~2~`, `STO~2~`, and `declarationIR~t_inst~^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Decls_inst, instantiating `declarationIR~t~^{asterisk}^`, under cursor `p`, instantiation context `IC~1~`, and store `STO~1~`>>.
  ... Result in 
* the modified instantiation context `IC~2~`,
* the updated store `STO~2~`, and the instantiated declarations `declarationIR~h_inst~ {two-colons} declarationIR~t_inst~^{asterisk}^`.


relation Program_inst: `p4program`


. Group :
 .. Let `declarationIR^{asterisk}^ ;` be the result of <<Program_ok, typing `p4program`>>.
 .. Let `IC~0~` be <<empty_instContext, an empty instantiation context>>.
 .. Let `STO~0~` be <<empty_store, an empty store>>.
 .. Let `IC~1~`, `STO~1~`, and `declarationIR'^{asterisk}^` be the result of <<Decls_inst, instantiating `declarationIR^{asterisk}^`, under cursor `GLOBAL`, instantiation context `IC~0~`, and store `STO~0~`>>.
 .. Check that `declarationIR'^{asterisk}^` is an empty list.
 .. Result in 
* the global instantiation layer `IC~1~.GLOBAL`, and the store `STO~1~`.


relation Bind_arg: `p~caller~`, `IC~caller~`, `p~callee~`, `IC~callee_0~`, `STO~0~`, `id`, and `argumentIR`


. Group :
 .. Let `IC~caller_inner~` be `<<enter_path_i, $enter_path_i(IC~caller~, id)>>`.
 .. Let <<Argument_inst, `p~caller~ IC~caller_inner~ STO~0~ |- argumentIR : STO~1~ value`>>.
 .. Let `IC~callee_1~` be `<<add_var_i, $add_var_i(p~callee~, IC~callee_0~, id, value)>>`.
 .. Result in `IC~callee_1~` and `STO~1~`.


relation Bind_args: `p~caller~`, `IC~caller~`, `p~callee~`, `IC~callee'~`, `STO'`, `id^{asterisk}^`, and `argumentIR^{asterisk}^`


. If `id^{asterisk}^` is an empty list:
 .. Check that `argumentIR^{asterisk}^` is an empty list.
 .. Group nil:
  ... Result in `IC~callee'~` and `STO'`.
. Else let `id~h~ {two-colons} id~t~^{asterisk}^` be `id^{asterisk}^`:
 .. Check that `argumentIR^{asterisk}^` is a non-empty list.
 .. Let `argumentIR~h~ {two-colons} argumentIR~t~^{asterisk}^` be `argumentIR^{asterisk}^`.
 .. Group cons:
  ... Let <<Bind_arg, `p~caller~ IC~caller~ | p~callee~ IC~callee'~ STO' |- id~h~ argumentIR~h~ : IC~callee_1~ STO~1~`>>.
  ... Let <<Bind_args, `p~caller~ IC~caller~ | p~callee~ IC~callee_1~ STO~1~ |- id~t~^{asterisk}^ argumentIR~t~^{asterisk}^ : IC~callee_2~ STO~2~`>>.
  ... Result in `IC~callee_2~` and `STO~2~`.


relation Constructor_inst: `p`, `IC`, `STO~0~`, `constructorDef`, `typeArgumentIR^{asterisk}^`, `argumentIR^{asterisk}^`, and `id~default'~^{asterisk}^`


