 .. Group defaultExpressionIR:
  ... Let `expressionResult` be `DEFAULT`.
  ... Result in the resulting evaluation context `EC'`, store `STO'` and expression result `expressionResult`.
. Else if let `unop typedExpressionIR` be `expressionIR`:
 .. Group unaryExpressionIR:
  ... Let `EC~1~`, `STO~1~`, and `expressionResult'` be the result of <<Expr_eval, evaluating `typedExpressionIR`, under cursor `p`, evaluation context `EC'`, and store `STO'`>>.
  ... If let `exitResult` be `expressionResult'`:
   .... Result in the resulting evaluation context `EC~1~`, store `STO~1~` and expression result `EXIT`.
  ... Else let `value` be `expressionResult'`:
   .... Let `value''` be <<un_op, `unop` `value`>>.
   .... Let `expressionResult` be `value''`.
   .... Result in the resulting evaluation context `EC~1~`, store `STO~1~` and expression result `expressionResult`.
. Else if let `typedExpressionIR~l~ binop' typedExpressionIR~r~` be `expressionIR`:
 .. Group binaryExpressionIR:
  ... Check that `binop'` is not in `[&&, ||]`.
  ... Let `EC~1~`, `STO~1~`, and `expressionListResult` be the result of <<Exprs_eval, evaluating `[typedExpressionIR~l~, typedExpressionIR~r~]`, under cursor `p`, evaluation context `EC'`, and store `STO'`>>.
  ... If let `exitResult` be `expressionListResult`:
   .... Result in the resulting evaluation context `EC~1~`, store `STO~1~` and expression result `EXIT`.
  ... Else let `value^{asterisk}^` be `expressionListResult`:
   .... Check that `value^{asterisk}^` is a list of length 2.
   .... Let `[value~l~, value~r~]` be `value^{asterisk}^`.
   .... Let `value''` be <<bin_op, `value~l~` `binop'` `value~r~`>>.
   .... Let `expressionResult` be `value''`.
   .... Result in the resulting evaluation context `EC~1~`, store `STO~1~` and expression result `expressionResult`.
  ... If `binop'` matches pattern `&&`:
   .... Let `EC~1~`, `STO~1~`, and `expressionResult'` be the result of <<Expr_eval, evaluating `typedExpressionIR~l~`, under cursor `p`, evaluation context `EC'`, and store `STO'`>>.
   .... Else if let `exitResult` be `expressionResult'`:
    ..... Result in the resulting evaluation context `EC~1~`, store `STO~1~` and expression result `EXIT`.
   .... Else if `expressionResult'` is equal to `B false`:
    ..... Let `expressionResult` be `B false`.
    ..... Result in the resulting evaluation context `EC~1~`, store `STO~1~` and expression result `expressionResult`.
   .... Else if `expressionResult'` is equal to `B true`:
    ..... Let `EC~2~`, `STO~2~`, and `expressionResult''` be the result of <<Expr_eval, evaluating `typedExpressionIR~r~`, under cursor `p`, evaluation context `EC~1~`, and store `STO~1~`>>.
    ..... Check that `expressionResult''` has type `exitResult`.
    ..... Let `exitResult` be `expressionResult''`.
    ..... Result in the resulting evaluation context `EC~2~`, store `STO~2~` and expression result `EXIT`.
    ..... Let `EC~2~`, `STO~2~`, and `expressionResult~r~` be the result of <<Expr_eval, evaluating `typedExpressionIR~r~`, under cursor `p`, evaluation context `EC~1~`, and store `STO~1~`>>.
    ..... Result in the resulting evaluation context `EC~2~`, store `STO~2~` and expression result `expressionResult~r~`.
  ... Else if `binop'` matches pattern `||`:
   .... Let `EC~1~`, `STO~1~`, and `expressionResult'` be the result of <<Expr_eval, evaluating `typedExpressionIR~l~`, under cursor `p`, evaluation context `EC'`, and store `STO'`>>.
   .... Else if let `exitResult` be `expressionResult'`:
    ..... Result in the resulting evaluation context `EC~1~`, store `STO~1~` and expression result `EXIT`.
   .... Else if `expressionResult'` is equal to `B true`:
    ..... Let `expressionResult` be `B true`.
    ..... Result in the resulting evaluation context `EC~1~`, store `STO~1~` and expression result `expressionResult`.
   .... Else if `expressionResult'` is equal to `B false`:
    ..... Let `EC~2~`, `STO~2~`, and `expressionResult''` be the result of <<Expr_eval, evaluating `typedExpressionIR~r~`, under cursor `p`, evaluation context `EC~1~`, and store `STO~1~`>>.
    ..... Check that `expressionResult''` has type `exitResult`.
    ..... Let `exitResult` be `expressionResult''`.
    ..... Result in the resulting evaluation context `EC~2~`, store `STO~2~` and expression result `EXIT`.
    ..... Let `EC~2~`, `STO~2~`, and `expressionResult~r~` be the result of <<Expr_eval, evaluating `typedExpressionIR~r~`, under cursor `p`, evaluation context `EC~1~`, and store `STO~1~`>>.
