relation Copy_in_argument: `STO~0~`, `p~caller~`, `EC~caller_0~`, `++_++ direction typeIR nameIR ++_++`, `p~callee~`, `EC~callee_0~`, and `argumentIR`


. Group directionless-in:
 .. If `direction` matches pattern ``EMPTY`:
  ... Let <<Argument_eval, `p~caller~ EC~caller_0~ STO~0~ |- argumentIR : EC~caller_1~ STO~1~ expressionResult`>>.
  ... If let `exitResult` be `expressionResult`:
   .... Result in `STO~1~`, `EC~caller_1~`, `EC~callee_0~`, and `EXIT`.
  ... Else let `value` be `expressionResult`:
   .... Let `EC~callee_1~` be `<<add_var_e, $add_var_e(p~callee~, EC~callee_0~, nameIR, value)>>`.
   .... Result in `STO~1~`, `EC~caller_1~`, `EC~callee_1~`, and `None`.
 .. Else if `direction` matches pattern `IN`:
  ... Let <<Argument_eval, `p~caller~ EC~caller_0~ STO~0~ |- argumentIR : EC~caller_1~ STO~1~ expressionResult`>>.
  ... If let `exitResult` be `expressionResult`:
   .... Result in `STO~1~`, `EC~caller_1~`, `EC~callee_0~`, and `EXIT`.
  ... Else let `value` be `expressionResult`:
   .... Let `EC~callee_1~` be `<<add_var_e, $add_var_e(p~callee~, EC~callee_0~, nameIR, value)>>`.
   .... Result in `STO~1~`, `EC~caller_1~`, `EC~callee_1~`, and `None`.
. If `direction` matches pattern `INOUT`:
 .. Group inout:
  ... Let <<Argument_eval_lvalue, `p~caller~ EC~caller_0~ STO~0~ |- argumentIR : EC~caller_1~ STO~1~ storageReferenceResult`>>.
  ... If let `exitResult` be `storageReferenceResult`:
   .... Result in `STO~1~`, `EC~caller_1~`, `EC~callee_0~`, and `EXIT`.
  ... Else let `storageReference'^?^` be `storageReferenceResult`:
   .... Check that `storageReference'^?^` is Some value.
   .... Let `storageReference` be `storageReference'^?^`.
   .... Let <<Lvalue_read, `p~caller~ EC~caller_1~ STO~1~ |- storageReference : value`>>.
   .... Let `EC~callee_1~` be `<<add_var_e, $add_var_e(p~callee~, EC~callee_0~, nameIR, value)>>`.
   .... Result in `STO~1~`, `EC~caller_1~`, `EC~callee_1~`, and `storageReference`.
. Else if `direction` matches pattern `OUT`:
 .. Group out:
  ... Let <<Argument_eval_lvalue, `p~caller~ EC~caller_0~ STO~0~ |- argumentIR : EC~caller_1~ STO~1~ storageReferenceResult`>>.
  ... If let `exitResult` be `storageReferenceResult`:
   .... Result in `STO~1~`, `EC~caller_1~`, `EC~callee_0~`, and `EXIT`.
  ... Else let `storageReference^?^` be `storageReferenceResult`:
   .... Let `typeIR~subst~` be `<<subst_type_e, $subst_type_e(p~callee~, EC~callee_0~, typeIR)>>`.
   .... Let `value~init~` be <<default, the default value for type `typeIR~subst~`>>.
   .... Let `EC~callee_1~` be `<<add_var_e, $add_var_e(p~callee~, EC~callee_0~, nameIR, value~init~)>>`.
   .... Result in `STO~1~`, `EC~caller_1~`, `EC~callee_1~`, and `storageReference^?^`.


relation Copy_in: `store`, `p~caller~`, `evalContext`, `parameterIR''^{asterisk}^`, `p~callee~`, `evalContext'`, and `argumentIR''^{asterisk}^`


. Group :
 .. If `parameterIR''^{asterisk}^` is equal to `[ ]`:
  ... Check that `argumentIR''^{asterisk}^` is equal to `[ ]`.
  ... Result in `store`, `evalContext`, `evalContext'`, and `[ ]`.
 .. Let `parameterIR'''^{asterisk}^` be `parameterIR''^{asterisk}^`.
 .. Else if let `parameterIR~h~ {two-colons} parameterIR~t~^{asterisk}^` be `parameterIR'''^{asterisk}^`:
  ... Let `argumentIR'''^{asterisk}^` be `argumentIR''^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Check that `argumentIR'''^{asterisk}^` is a non-empty list.
  ... Let `argumentIR~h~ {two-colons} argumentIR~t~^{asterisk}^` be `argumentIR'''^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Let <<Copy_in_argument, `store p~caller~ evalContext parameterIR~h~ @ p~callee~ evalContext' argumentIR~h~ ~> STO~1~ EC~caller_1~ @ EC~callee_1~ # copyInResult`>>.
  ... If let `exitResult` be `copyInResult`:
   .... Result in `STO~1~`, `EC~caller_1~`, `EC~callee_1~`, and `EXIT`.
  ... Else let `storageReference~h~^?^` be `copyInResult`:
   .... Let <<Copy_in, `STO~1~ p~caller~ EC~caller_1~ parameterIR~t~^{asterisk}^ @ p~callee~ EC~callee_1~ argumentIR~t~^{asterisk}^ ~> STO~2~ EC~caller_2~ @ EC~callee_2~ # copyInListResult`>>.
   .... If let `exitResult` be `copyInListResult`:
    ..... Result in `STO~2~`, `EC~caller_2~`, `EC~callee_2~`, and `EXIT`.
   .... Else let `(storageReference'^?^)^{asterisk}^` be `copyInListResult`:
    ..... Check that `(storageReference'^?^)^{asterisk}^` has type `storageReference*`.
    ..... Let `storageReference~t~^{asterisk}^` be `(storageReference'^?^)^{asterisk}^`.
    ..... Let `(storageReference^?^)^{asterisk}^` be `storageReference~h~^?^ {two-colons} storageReference~t~^{asterisk}^`.
    ..... Result in `STO~2~`, `EC~caller_2~`, `EC~callee_2~`, and `(storageReference^?^)^{asterisk}^`.


relation Copy_in_default: `parameterIR^{asterisk}^`, `p~callee~`, `EC~callee_0~`, and `value^{asterisk}^`


. Group :
 .. Let `nameIR^{asterisk}^` be the list of `nameIR`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
    * Let `nameIR` be the name of `parameterIR`.
--
+
for each `parameterIR` in `parameterIR^{asterisk}^`
 .. Let `EC~callee_1~` be `<<add_vars_e, $add_vars_e(p~callee~, EC~callee_0~, (nameIR)^{asterisk}^, value^{asterisk}^)>>`.
 .. Result in `EC~callee_1~`.


relation Copy_out_argument: `STO`, `p~caller~`, `EC~caller_0'~`, `++_++ direction typeIR nameIR ++_++`, `p~callee~`, `EC~callee~`, and `storageReference'''^?^`


. Check that `storageReference'''^?^` is None.
. Group in-directionless:
 .. If `direction` matches pattern `IN`:
  ... Result in `EC~caller_0'~`.
 .. Else if `direction` matches pattern ``EMPTY`:
  ... Result in `EC~caller_0'~`.
. Group out-inout:
 .. If `storageReference'''^?^` is equal to `None`:
  ... If `direction` matches pattern `OUT`:
   .... Result in `EC~caller_0'~`.
  ... Else if `direction` matches pattern `INOUT`:
   .... Result in `EC~caller_0'~`.
 .. Let `storageReference''^?^` be `storageReference'''^?^`.
 .. Else if let `storageReference` be `storageReference''^?^`:
  ... If `direction` matches pattern `OUT`:
   .... Let `value` be `<<find_var_e, $find_var_e(p~callee~, EC~callee~, nameIR)>>`.
   .... Let <<Lvalue_write, `p~caller~ EC~caller_0'~ STO |- storageReference -> value : EC~caller_1~`>>.
   .... Result in `EC~caller_1~`.
  ... Else if `direction` matches pattern `INOUT`:
   .... Let `value` be `<<find_var_e, $find_var_e(p~callee~, EC~callee~, nameIR)>>`.
   .... Let <<Lvalue_write, `p~caller~ EC~caller_0'~ STO |- storageReference -> value : EC~caller_1~`>>.
   .... Result in `EC~caller_1~`.


relation Copy_out: `STO`, `p~caller~`, `evalContext`, `parameterIR^{asterisk}^`, `p~callee~`, `EC~callee~`, and `(storageReference^?^)^{asterisk}^`


. Group :
 .. If `parameterIR^{asterisk}^` is equal to `[ ]`:
  ... Check that `(storageReference^?^)^{asterisk}^` is equal to `[ ]`.
  ... Result in `evalContext`.
 .. Let `parameterIR'^{asterisk}^` be `parameterIR^{asterisk}^`.
 .. Else if let `parameterIR~h~ {two-colons} parameterIR~t~^{asterisk}^` be `parameterIR'^{asterisk}^`:
  ... Let `(storageReference'^?^)^{asterisk}^` be `(storageReference^?^)^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Check that `(storageReference'^?^)^{asterisk}^` is a non-empty list.
  ... Let `storageReference~h~^?^ {two-colons} (storageReference~t~^?^)^{asterisk}^` be `(storageReference'^?^)^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Let <<Copy_out_argument, `STO p~caller~ evalContext parameterIR~h~ @ p~callee~ EC~callee~ storageReference~h~^?^ ~> EC~caller_1~`>>.
  ... Let <<Copy_out, `STO p~caller~ EC~caller_1~ parameterIR~t~^{asterisk}^ @ p~callee~ EC~callee~ (storageReference~t~^?^)^{asterisk}^ ~> EC~caller_2~`>>.
  ... Result in `EC~caller_2~`.


relation Call_eval: `p`, `EC~0'~`, `STO~0'~`, `callee`, `typeArgumentListIR'`, and `argumentListIR'`


. Let `typeArgumentIR^{asterisk}^` be `typeArgumentListIR'`.
. If let `actionCallee` be `callee`:
 .. Check that `typeArgumentIR^{asterisk}^` is an empty list.
 .. Group actionCallee:
  ... Let `ACTION cursor . nameIR ( parameterIR^{asterisk}^ # id~default~^{asterisk}^ ) blockStatementIR` be `actionCallee`.
  ... If `cursor` matches pattern `GLOBAL`:
   .... Let `EC~callee_0~` be `<<inherit_e, $inherit_e(GLOBAL, EC~0'~)>>`.
   .... Let `(parameterIR~aligned~^{asterisk}^, argumentIR~aligned~^{asterisk}^, parameterIR~default~^{asterisk}^, value~default~^{asterisk}^)` be `<<align_params_with_args, $align_params_with_args(parameterIR^{asterisk}^, argumentListIR', id~default~^{asterisk}^)>>`.
   .... Let <<Copy_in, `STO~0'~ p EC~0'~ parameterIR~aligned~^{asterisk}^ @ LOCAL EC~callee_0~ argumentIR~aligned~^{asterisk}^ ~> STO~1~ EC~1~ @ EC~callee_1~ # copyInListResult`>>.
   .... Check that `copyInListResult` has type `continueResult<storageReference?*>`.
   .... Let `(storageReference^?^)^{asterisk}^` be `copyInListResult`.
   .... Let <<Copy_in_default, `parameterIR~default~^{asterisk}^ @ LOCAL EC~callee_1~ value~default~^{asterisk}^ ~> @ EC~callee_2~`>>.
   .... Let <<ActionBody_eval, `EC~callee_2~ STO~1~ |- blockStatementIR : EC~callee_3~ STO~2~ actionResult`>>.
   .... Else if `actionResult` is equal to `RETURN None`:
    ..... Let `EC~2~` be `EC~1~[GLOBAL.FRAME = EC~callee_3~.GLOBAL.FRAME]`.
    ..... Let <<Copy_out, `STO~2~ p EC~2~ parameterIR~aligned~^{asterisk}^ @ LOCAL EC~callee_3~ (storageReference^?^)^{asterisk}^ ~> EC~3~`>>.
    ..... Result in the resulting evaluation context `EC~3~`, store `STO~2~`, and call result `RETURN None`.
   .... Else if let `exitResult` be `actionResult`:
    ..... Let `EC~2~` be `EC~1~[GLOBAL.FRAME = EC~callee_3~.GLOBAL.FRAME]`.
    ..... Let <<Copy_out, `STO~2~ p EC~2~ parameterIR~aligned~^{asterisk}^ @ LOCAL EC~callee_3~ (storageReference^?^)^{asterisk}^ ~> EC~3~`>>.
    ..... Result in the resulting evaluation context `EC~3~`, store `STO~2~`, and call result `EXIT`.
  ... Else if `cursor` matches pattern `BLOCK`:
   .... Let `EC~callee_0~` be `<<inherit_e, $inherit_e(BLOCK, EC~0'~)>>`.
