relation TableKey_eval: `EC~0~`, `STO~0~`, and `typedExpressionIR : nameIR ++_++ ;`


. Group exit:
 .. Let `EC~1~`, `STO~1~`, and `expressionResult` be the result of <<Expr_eval, evaluating `typedExpressionIR`, under cursor `LOCAL`, evaluation context `EC~0~`, and store `STO~0~`>>.
 .. Check that `expressionResult` has type `exitResult`.
 .. Let `exitResult` be `expressionResult`.
 .. Result in `EC~1~`, `STO~1~`, and `EXIT`.
. Group cont:
 .. Let `EC~1~`, `STO~1~`, and `expressionResult` be the result of <<Expr_eval, evaluating `typedExpressionIR`, under cursor `LOCAL`, evaluation context `EC~0~`, and store `STO~0~`>>.
 .. Check that `expressionResult` has type `continueResult<value>`.
 .. Let `value` be `expressionResult`.
 .. Let `tableKeyValue` be `value : nameIR`.
 .. Result in `EC~1~`, `STO~1~`, and `tableKeyValue`.


relation TableKeys_eval: `evalContext`, `store`, and `tableKeyIR''^{asterisk}^`


. Group :
 .. If `tableKeyIR''^{asterisk}^` is equal to `[ ]`:
  ... Result in `evalContext`, `store`, and `[ ]`.
 .. Let `tableKeyIR'''^{asterisk}^` be `tableKeyIR''^{asterisk}^`.
 .. Else if let `tableKeyIR~h~ {two-colons} tableKeyIR~t~^{asterisk}^` be `tableKeyIR'''^{asterisk}^`:
  ... Let <<TableKey_eval, `evalContext store |- tableKeyIR~h~ : EC~1~ STO~1~ tableKeyResult`>>.
  ... If let `exitResult` be `tableKeyResult`:
   .... Result in `EC~1~`, `STO~1~`, and `EXIT`.
  ... Else let `tableKeyValue~h~` be `tableKeyResult`:
   .... Let <<TableKeys_eval, `EC~1~ STO~1~ |- tableKeyIR~t~^{asterisk}^ : EC~2~ STO~2~ tableKeysResult`>>.
   .... If let `exitResult` be `tableKeysResult`:
    ..... Result in `EC~2~`, `STO~2~`, and `EXIT`.
   .... Else let `tableKeyValue~t~^{asterisk}^` be `tableKeysResult`:
    ..... Let `tableKeyValue^{asterisk}^` be `tableKeyValue~h~ {two-colons} tableKeyValue~t~^{asterisk}^`.
    ..... Result in `EC~2~`, `STO~2~`, and `tableKeyValue^{asterisk}^`.


relation TableEntryPriority_eval: `EC`, `STO`, and `tableEntryPriorityIR^?^`


. Check that `tableEntryPriorityIR^?^` is None.
. Group :
 .. Result in `None`.


relation TableMatch_eval: `EC~0~`, `STO~0~`, `tableKeyValue^{asterisk}^`, and `tableEntryIR`


. Group :
 .. Let `++_++ tableEntryPriorityIR^?^ keysetExpressionIR : tableActionReferenceIR ++_++ ;` be `tableEntryIR`.
 .. Let <<TableEntryPriority_eval, `EC~0~ STO~0~ |- tableEntryPriorityIR^?^ : n~priority~^?^`>>.
 .. Let <<Expr_eval_keyset, `EC~0~ STO~0~ |- keysetExpressionIR : EC~1~ STO~1~ keysetExpressionResult`>>.
 .. Check that `keysetExpressionResult` has type `continueResult<setValue*>`.
 .. Let `setValue^{asterisk}^` be `keysetExpressionResult`.
 .. Let `value~key~^{asterisk}^` be the list of `value~key~`, obtained by repeating:
+
--
    * Let `value~key~ : ++_++` be `tableKeyValue`.
--
+
for each `tableKeyValue` in `tableKeyValue^{asterisk}^`
 .. If `~<<match_keysets, $match_keysets(setValue^{asterisk}^, value~key~^{asterisk}^)>>`:
  ... Result in `EC~1~`, `STO~1~`, and `None`.
 .. Else `<<match_keysets, $match_keysets(setValue^{asterisk}^, value~key~^{asterisk}^)>>`:
  ... Let `tableMatch` be `n~priority~^?^ : tableActionReferenceIR`.
  ... Result in `EC~1~`, `STO~1~`, and `tableMatch`.


relation TableMatches_eval: `evalContext`, `store`, `tableKeyValue^{asterisk}^`, and `tableEntryIR^{asterisk}^`


. Group :
 .. If `tableEntryIR^{asterisk}^` is equal to `[ ]`:
  ... Result in `evalContext`, `store`, and `[ ]`.
 .. Let `tableEntryIR'^{asterisk}^` be `tableEntryIR^{asterisk}^`.
 .. Else if let `tableEntryIR~h~ {two-colons} tableEntryIR~t~^{asterisk}^` be `tableEntryIR'^{asterisk}^`:
  ... Let <<TableMatch_eval, `evalContext store |- tableKeyValue^{asterisk}^ @ tableEntryIR~h~ : EC~1~ STO~1~ tableMatchResult`>>.
  ... Check that `tableMatchResult` has type `continueResult<tableMatch?>`.
  ... Let `tableMatch~h~^?^` be `tableMatchResult`.
  ... Let <<TableMatches_eval, `EC~1~ STO~1~ |- tableKeyValue^{asterisk}^ @ tableEntryIR~t~^{asterisk}^ : EC~2~ STO~2~ tableMatchesResult`>>.
  ... Check that `tableMatchesResult` has type `continueResult<tableMatch*>`.
  ... Let `tableMatch~t~^{asterisk}^` be `tableMatchesResult`.
  ... Let `tableMatch'^{asterisk}^` be `<<opt_as_seq_, $opt_as_seq_<tableMatch>(tableMatch~h~^?^)>>`.
  ... Let `tableMatch^{asterisk}^` be `tableMatch'^{asterisk}^ {pp} tableMatch~t~^{asterisk}^`.
  ... Result in `EC~2~`, `STO~2~`, and `tableMatch^{asterisk}^`.


relation ActionBody_eval: `EC~0~`, `STO~0~`, and `blockStatementIR`


. Group :
 .. Let <<Block_eval, `EC~0~ STO~0~ |- blockStatementIR : EC~1~ STO~1~ statementResult`>>.
 .. If let `continueEmptyResult` be `statementResult`:
  ... Result in `EC~1~`, `STO~1~`, and `RETURN None`.
 .. Else if let `exitResult` be `statementResult`:
  ... Result in `EC~1~`, `STO~1~`, and `EXIT`.
 .. Check that `statementResult` is equal to `RETURN None`.
 .. Result in `EC~1~`, `STO~1~`, and `RETURN None`.


relation DefinedFunctionBody_eval: `EC~0~`, `STO~0~`, and `blockStatementIR`


. Group :
 .. Let <<Block_eval, `EC~0~ STO~0~ |- blockStatementIR : EC~1~ STO~1~ statementResult`>>.
 .. If let `continueEmptyResult` be `statementResult`:
  ... Result in `EC~1~`, `STO~1~`, and `RETURN None`.
 .. Else if let `exitResult` be `statementResult`:
  ... Result in `EC~1~`, `STO~1~`, and `EXIT`.
 .. Else if let `returnResult` be `statementResult`:
  ... Result in `EC~1~`, `STO~1~`, and `returnResult`.


relation Var_init: `EC~0~`, `typeIR`, and `nameIR`


. Group :
 .. Let `value` be <<default, the default value for type `typeIR`>>.
 .. Let `EC~1~` be `<<add_var_e, $add_var_e(GLOBAL, EC~0~, nameIR, value)>>`.
 .. Result in the resulting evaluation context `EC~1~`.


relation Extern_init: `EC`, `STO~0~`, and `nameIR`


. Group :
 .. Let `IC` be {PATH `[ ]`, GLOBAL `EC.GLOBAL`, BLOCK `EC.BLOCK`, LOCAL `EC.LOCAL`}.
 .. Let `(cid, constructorDef, id*)^?^` be `<<find_constructorDef_i, $find_constructorDef_i(IC, nameIR, [ ])>>`.
 .. Check that `(cid, constructorDef, id*)^?^` is Some value.
 .. Let `(++_++, constructorDef, ++_++^{asterisk}^)` be `(cid, constructorDef, id*)^?^`.
 .. Let <<Constructor_inst, `GLOBAL IC STO~0~ |- constructorDef < [ ] > ( [ ] # [ ] ) : STO~1~ object`>>.
 .. Let `oid~object~` be `[nameIR]`.
 .. Let `STO~2~` be `<<add_map, $add_map<oid, object>(STO~1~, oid~object~, object)>>`.
 .. Result in the resulting store `STO~2~`.


relation Program_init: `p4program`


. Group :
 .. Let `globalEvalLayer` and `STO` be the result of <<Program_inst, instantiating `p4program`>>.
 .. Let `blockEvalLayer` be {TYPE `<<empty_theta, $empty_theta>>`, CALLABLE `<<empty_callableDefEnv, $empty_callableDefEnv>>`, STATE `<<empty_stateEnv, $empty_stateEnv>>`, FRAME `<<empty_frame, $empty_frame>>`}.
 .. Let `localEvalLayer` be {TYPE `<<empty_theta, $empty_theta>>`, FRAMES `[<<empty_frame, $empty_frame>>]`}.
 .. Let `EC` be {GLOBAL `globalEvalLayer`, BLOCK `blockEvalLayer`, LOCAL `localEvalLayer`}.
 .. Result in the resulting evaluation context `EC` and store `STO`.


relation V1Model_init: `p4program`


. Group :
 .. Let `EC~0~` and `STO~0~` be the result of <<Program_init, initializing the evaluation context and store for `p4program`>>.
 .. Result in the resulting evaluation context `EC~0~` and store `STO~0~`.


relation V1Model_init_packet_in: `EC~0~`, `STO~0~`, and `externState~packet_in~`


. Group :
 .. Let `STO~1~` be the result of <<Extern_init, instantiating extern `EC~0~` in the evaluation context `STO~0~` and store `"packet_in"`>>.
 .. Let `EC~1~` be `<<add_var_e, $add_var_e(GLOBAL, EC~0~, "packet_in", ! ["packet_in"])>>`.
 .. Let `object'^?^` be `<<find_map, $find_map<oid, object>(STO~1~, ["packet_in"])>>`.
 .. Check that `object'^?^` is Some value.
 .. Let `object` be `object'^?^`.
 .. Check that `object` has type `externObject`.
 .. Let `externObject~packet_in~` be `object`.
 .. Let `EXTERN tid < theta > { ++_++ frame externMethodDefEnv }` be `externObject~packet_in~`.
 .. Let `externObject~packet_in_init~` be `EXTERN tid < theta > { externState~packet_in~ frame externMethodDefEnv }`.
 .. Let `STO~2~` be `<<add_map, $add_map<oid, object>(STO~1~, ["packet_in"], externObject~packet_in_init~)>>`.
 .. Result in `EC~1~` and `STO~2~`.


relation V1Model_init_packet_out: `EC~0~`, `STO~0~`, and `externState~packet_out~`


. Group :
 .. Let `STO~1~` be the result of <<Extern_init, instantiating extern `EC~0~` in the evaluation context `STO~0~` and store `"packet_out"`>>.
 .. Let `EC~1~` be `<<add_var_e, $add_var_e(GLOBAL, EC~0~, "packet_out", ! ["packet_out"])>>`.
 .. Let `object'^?^` be `<<find_map, $find_map<oid, object>(STO~1~, ["packet_out"])>>`.
