relation V1Model_init_globals: `EC~0~`, `STO`, and `i~port~`


. Group :
 .. Let `object'^?^` be `<<find_map, $find_map<oid, object>(STO, ["main"])>>`.
 .. Check that `object'^?^` is Some value.
 .. Let `object` be `object'^?^`.
 .. Check that `object` has type `packageObject`.
 .. Let `PACKAGE < theta > { ++_++ }` be `object`.
 .. Let `typeIR^?^` be `<<find_map, $find_map<tid, typeIR>(theta, "H")>>`.
 .. Check that `typeIR^?^` is Some value.
 .. Let `typeIR~hdr~` be `typeIR^?^`.
 .. Let `typeIR'^?^` be `<<find_map, $find_map<tid, typeIR>(theta, "M")>>`.
 .. Check that `typeIR'^?^` is Some value.
 .. Let `typeIR~meta~` be `typeIR'^?^`.
 .. Let `EC~1~` be the result of <<Var_init, instantiating global variable `"hdr"` of type `typeIR~hdr~` in the evaluation context `EC~0~`>>.
 .. Let `EC~2~` be the result of <<Var_init, instantiating global variable `"meta"` of type `typeIR~meta~` in the evaluation context `EC~1~`>>.
 .. Let `typeDefIR^?^` be `<<find_typeDef_e, $find_typeDef_e(GLOBAL, EC~2~, "standard_metadata_t")>>`.
 .. Check that `typeDefIR^?^` is Some value.
 .. Let `typeDefIR~standard_metadata~` be `typeDefIR^?^`.
 .. Let `typeIR~std_meta~` be `typeDefIR~standard_metadata~ < [ ] >`.
 .. Let `EC~3~` be the result of <<Var_init, instantiating global variable `"standard_metadata"` of type `typeIR~std_meta~` in the evaluation context `EC~2~`>>.
 .. Let `storageReference~port~` be `"standard_metadata" . "ingress_port"`.
 .. Let `value~port~` be `9 W i~port~`.
 .. Let <<Lvalue_write, `GLOBAL EC~3~ STO |- storageReference~port~ -> value~port~ : EC~4~`>>.
 .. Result in `EC~4~`.


